\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Hey, Mikie, WTF?\u8217\'20\'19: New Jersey governor facing outrage over attacks on Delaney Hall protesters\b0\par\par\uc2 Lex McMenamin in New Jersey \par \uc2 1,336 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2026\par 18:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Protesters say Mikie Sherrill has failed to address the dire hunger and labor strike at the immigration detention center\par \par \uc2 A few dozen protesters rallied outside the New Jersey statehouse in Trenton on Monday afternoon. They carried handmade signs with messages such as \u8220\'20\'1CU made it worse\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CGov Sherrill, stop lying about Delaney Hall\u8221\'20\'1D. One led a collective chant that summed up the rally\u8217\'20\'19s mood: \u8220\'20\'1CHey, Mikie, WTF?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The target of their ire: the governor, Mikie Sherrill. Protesters say the newly elected Democratic governor has failed to adequately address the dire situation at the Delaney Hall immigration detention center in Newark, where at least 300 detainees are on a hunger and labor strike.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Sherrill sent in state police to \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovSherrillNJ/status/2060438345348509848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lower the temperature}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D on the protests outside the facility, where hundreds of people had been gathering every day in support of the detainees striking over what they say are poor conditions, including maggot-ridden food and denial of access to medical care. However, when the state police arrived in riot gear and on horseback, tensions ticked up. According to multiple protest organizers who spoke to the Guardian, dozens of protesters were arrested, and some were hospitalized. State police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/new-jersey/delaney-hall-protest-news-crew-tear-gas/6507083/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled a local news crew}}}\uc2  from their vehicle, exposing them to teargas. Other journalists were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ChuckModi1/status/2061705401129664912"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  and held in custody for a full day.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Sherrill has yet to meet the strikers\u8217\'20\'19 demands - the first of which is to meet with the governor. Early last week, ICE denied her access to Delaney. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovSherrillNJ/status/2062261573373047179"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she is still being denied, but has met with family members of the detainees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will continue fighting for accountability, transparency, and better conditions at Delaney Hall,\u8221\'20\'1D Sherrill posted on X on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe detainees have requested to meet with me and I want to meet with them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protesters told the Guardian they were upset at Sherrill, as well as her appointed state attorney general, Jennifer Davenport, for sending in state police forces that brutalized protesters while failing to meet any of the demands issued by the hunger and labor strikers. On top of protesting outside Delaney, demonstrators are putting direct pressure on officials, rallying at their offices and reiterating the demands of the hunger strikers. They want the detainees released and for protesters\u8217\'20\'19 first amendment rights to be protected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about as gross a betrayal of these families [of detainees] and her voters as you can get,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sameer Khetan, a New Jersey resident who helped lead the Trenton rally.\par \par \uc2 The demands asked of Sherrill\par \par \uc2 Defending her deployment of state police, Sherrill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nj.com/news/2026/05/gov-sherrill-urges-aggressive-and-dangerous-protesters-to-calm-down-amid-delaney-hall-chaos.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed \u8220\'20\'1Cviolence\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  at the protests on \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople coming from out of state to create chaos and dangerous situations\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s true that some protesters have been coming to Delaney from nearby states such as New York and Pennsylvania, but many of the Delaney detainees are also from New York, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://austinkocher.substack.com/p/delaney-hall-detention-center-a-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis from Austin Kocher}}}\uc2 , a \uc2 Syracuse University\uc2  research assistant professor.\par \par \uc2 Advocates and organizers have condemned the \u8220\'20\'1Coutside agitator\u8221\'20\'1D rhetoric, saying that the state government\u8217\'20\'19s focus on policing protesters distracts from elected officials\u8217\'20\'19 responsibility to protect the detainees and close Delaney Hall.\par \par \uc2 On 3 June, hunger and labor strikers in Delaney issued a statement detailing violence within the facility in retaliation for the strike: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been subjected to reprisals, discrimination, mockery, mistreatment and threats, mainly from \u8216\'20\'18GEO\u8217\'20\'19 staff,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the \uc2 Geo Group\uc2 , which runs the facility. The strikers said that ICE agents came in and pepper-sprayed strikers, causing some to be sent to the hospital: \u8220\'20\'1CTo this day, we haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard anything about those people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Geo Group{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecityreporter.nyc/2026/05/29/delaney-hall-ice-detention-clashes-markwayne-mullin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed to the City Reporter}}}\uc2  that staff used \u8220\'20\'1Cchemical agents\u8221\'20\'1D in response to \u8220\'20\'1Ca physical altercation involving detainees\u8221\'20\'1D. In a statement, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/05/29/correct-record-dhs-debunks-sanctuary-politicians-smears-about-ices-delaney-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DHS claimed}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Call affected detainees were promptly evaluated by on-site medical personnel and were cleared with no serious injuries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Upon taking office in January, Sherrill, a former federal prosecutor and \uc2 US Congress\uc2  member, strengthened sanctuary protections within the state, signaling that she would be a staunch opponent of ICE operations. But Delaney has been a test of that promise. Sherrill joins a pattern of elected Democrats who have criticized ICE operations \u8211\'20\'13 including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kare11.com/article/news/local/city-leaders-address-overnight-protests-in-minneapolis/89-e2277a66-52cc-4134-bfb5-7076f5f10634"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minneapolis mayor, Jacob Frey}}}\uc2 , and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blockclubchicago.org/2025/11/12/protesters-keep-getting-arrested-at-broadview-by-state-police-despite-promise-to-protect-free-speech/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois governor, JB Pritzker}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 while presiding over law enforcement forces arresting citizens protesting those operations.\par \par \uc2 John Mark Rozendaal was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/reels/DY-WFu6vgpi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 playing his cello}}}\uc2  outside Delaney on Friday night when state police descended in riot gear. He said the police threw his cello to the side and removed his mask, exposing him to teargas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince [organizers] were asking for musicians, I took my cello and I played,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hoped that my playing out there outside the mutual aid tent was comforting and calming for someone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Instead, he was arrested. One protester outside Sherrill\u8217\'20\'19s office on Monday had already made a sign with livestream photos of Rozendaal playing the cello and his arrest. It was captioned \u8220\'20\'1CMikie Sherrill turning down the temperature\u8221\'20\'1D, a reference to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s language about her decision to send in state police.\par \par \uc2 Multiple protesters spoke to the Guardian about hopes that Sherrill could be removed from her office through a recall; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/progressivevic/status/2061569066373169361?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least one progressive group}}}\uc2  that had thrown its weight behind Sherrill called for her resignation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the person I thought I was voting for,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neal McGrath at the rally outside Sherrill\u8217\'20\'19s office on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I knew that this was going to happen, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I would\u8217\'20\'19ve voted for her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Steps toward accountability\par \par \uc2 The hunger-striking detainees and protesters have seen some wins in the two weeks since the Delaney hunger and labor strike began. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovSherrillNJ/status/2061058879878754633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Visitation}}}\uc2 , previously suspended, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/31/new-jersey-ice-facility-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowly being permitted again}}}\uc2 . According to advocacy group Cosecha New Jersey, as of 1 June, all the pregnant people inside Delaney Hall have been released.\par \par \uc2 That same day, the Newark mayor, Ras Baraka, announced the city would be taking over supervision of the protests from state police, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/newark-mayor-questions-state-police-tactics-delaney-hall-sherrills-order-calls-agency-sword"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distancing himself from their conduct}}}\uc2  over the weekend. Organizers say that part of the goal of the protests outside Delaney is to show support for those inside through noise; that is now possible again, with the removal of the \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech zone\u8221\'20\'1D barricades erected by state police and the city\u8217\'20\'19s curfew lifted.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey elected officials are also exploring accountability measures: On 2 June, both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7ny.com/post/delaney-hall-protests-newark-mayor-ras-baraka-file-lawsuit-operators-citing-safety-health-concerns/19217960/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Baraka}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jun/02/new-jersey-lawsuit-geo-group-delaney-hall-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sherrill and Davenport}}}\uc2  announced lawsuits against Geo Group, citing health concerns and the state department of health being denied full access to the facility. (The city of Newark has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/newyork/news/delaney-hall-newark-nj-ice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 engaged in legal action against Geo Group}}}\uc2  over the facility since April 2025.)\par \par \uc2 In a statement on X, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DHSgov/status/2061840060744376646"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DHS responded}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a frivolous lawsuit. ICE is committed to transparency, and Delaney Hall complies with all required state and local laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, pressure remains on Sherrill. On Wednesday, she told multiple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wnyc.org/browse/shows/episode/simplecast/b64927b4-5a20-4443-bae5-4b55cb8f9107"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WNYC callers }}}\uc2 who asked about the violence over the weekend that \u8220\'20\'1Cif state police crossed lines, the state attorney general would look into the matter\u8221\'20\'1D. On Thursday, she announced a $12m increase in funding for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/t.e2ma.net/click/rida6n/fd1rrbm/f5mzxeb__;!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!NrTK9HOqzyXvAjPBfHUzsEa5T-yi97aDvrPYtQr-PtegkKL7_7_0471DPol-jfwN_F4ea2wf785ZG04YJN4-YF0iZcI$"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detention Deportation Defense Initiative}}}\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s free legal services program for residents facing deportations, as well as a rapid legal response initiative for emergency immigration defense.\par \par \uc2 However, organizers say their work isn\u8217\'20\'19t over as long as detainees are in Delaney. After Baraka lifted the curfew around Delaney on Tuesday, protesters rushed back to the facility. It was the first time this week that people held inside were able to hear the protesters calling for their release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we\u8217\'20\'19re outside Delaney Hall, we\u8217\'20\'19re chanting: \u8216\'20\'18Free them all,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Rozendaal. \u8220\'20\'1CWe see them waving to us. We see them making little heart shapes with their hands. We hear from the families that the people inside are strengthened and rejoiced by our presence out there.\u8221\'20\'1DAdditional reporting by Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Olivares\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260605em65003bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
