\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump has made our K-shaped economy even more unequal\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,342 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 June 2026\par 15:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 While wealthy Americans hail a booming stock market, the rest of us worry about rising inflation and people struggling to make ends meetPeople in the US: tell us about your difficult consumer experiences\par \par \uc2 In case you\u8217\'20\'19re not familiar with the concept of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/12/31/nx-s1-5660842/what-is-a-k-shaped-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the K-shaped economy}}}\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s an important idea that captures a lot about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s America. Wealthy Americans are represented by the line of the K that angles sharply upward to the right, while the line of the K that dips downward represents non-rich Americans and the difficulties they face.\par \par \uc2 The economy\u8217\'20\'19s K-shape has been growing worse in recent months, in large part because of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies. The wealthy people\u8217\'20\'19s line is climbing further upward, while the line for the non-wealthy \u8211\'20\'13 the vast majority of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 has fallen further.\par \par \uc2 Viewed another way, the K-shaped economy is all about income and wealth inequality, and those are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/trump-economy-wealth-gap-americans-affordability-inflation-prices-rcna264112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing palpably worse under Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the country\u8217\'20\'19s wealthy, things are going gangbusters as the S&P 500 and other stock indices keep hitting record highs, notwithstanding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s costly, unsuccessful war against Iran. The richest 10% of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/wealthiest-10-americans-own-93-033623827.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 own 93% of all stock}}}\uc2  held by US households, and that means millions of average Americans aren\u8217\'20\'19t feeling Wall Street\u8217\'20\'19s rise \u8211\'20\'13 although they\u8217\'20\'19re very much feeling inflation\u8217\'20\'19s rise as it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2026/05/12/economy/us-cpi-inflation-april"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climbed to nearly 4%}}}\uc2 , as hourly earnings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/economicdata/realer_05122026.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fail to keep up with rising prices}}}\uc2  and as gas prices have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/data-graphics/gas-prices-iran-war-state-national-cost-trump-rcna265835"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jumped about 50%}}}\uc2  since Trump began bombing Iran. What\u8217\'20\'19s more, workers\u8217\'20\'19 hourly pay has risen by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/the-record-divide-between-corporate-profits-and-worker-pay-ea4c75bc?mod=hp_lead_pos11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mere 3% since 2019}}}\uc2  (after adjusting for inflation), while corporate profits have jumped by 50%.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a tale of two Americas. When some people look at the economy, they see a booming stock market, low unemployment, consumer spending chugging along and friends jetting off to overseas vacations. But those on the bottom end of the K see something very different: rising inflation, a sluggish job market, sky-high gas prices, problems with affordability and friends struggling to make ends meet. One big reason that consumer spending hasn\u8217\'20\'19t tanked is that the richest, we\u8217\'20\'19re-doing-just-fine 10% of Americans account for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/consumers/us-economy-strength-rich-spending-2c34a571"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly half of all consumer spending}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The economy\u8217\'20\'19s K shape is visible in many places. Airlines are adding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sherwood.news/business/us-airlines-are-still-doubling-down-on-premium-seats-as-the-k-shaped-economy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more business class seats}}}\uc2  as the wealthy clamor for those higher-priced spots. But \uc2 Spirit\uc2 , the low-price airline that many non-rich Americans relied on, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/spirit-airlines-trump-bailout-bankruptcy-37a4818e1b71c0905d022f669d85948c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has gone belly up}}}\uc2 . Sales of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/americans-sell-plasma-inflation-middle-class-expenses-economy-rcna258390"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 private jets and fancy yachts}}}\uc2  have soared even as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2026/05/27/nx-s1-5836441/food-insecurity-economy-new-york-fed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve says}}}\uc2  that more Americans are going hungry than during the pandemic. The McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s CEO complained recently of a \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/11/business/economy/k-shaped-economy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-tier economy}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, with sales to lower-income Americans declining even as McD\u8217\'20\'19s added premium, higher-end products, like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foodandwine.com/mcdonalds-big-arch-burger-prices-by-state-neomam-studios-report-11928377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Big Arch burger}}}\uc2 , which costs between $7.50 and $13, depending on the location. While wealthy Americans fly to Greece and safaris in Africa, many average Americans are so squeezed by $4.26-a-gallon gas that they\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msn.com/en-us/travel/tips/travel-budgets-are-shrinking-for-many-americans-survey-says/ar-AA220Xvu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cutting back on travel}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msn.com/en-us/travel/tips/travel-budgets-are-shrinking-for-many-americans-survey-says/ar-AA220Xvu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 piling on record amounts of debt}}}\uc2 . US consumers have shelled out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iranwarcost.watson.brown.edu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $52bn extra for gas}}}\uc2  due to the price increases, and as with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, soaring gas prices have squeezed non-rich Americans far more than wealthy ones. Americans in the bottom quarter by income (earning under $40,000 a year) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/05/24/rising-gas-prices-are-widening-gap-between-rich-poor/?utm_campaign=wp_main&utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=social&fbclid=IwY2xjawSGoaxleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETFoZnZERTRpWTRjdWFKZFdOc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHgKw-ulHvYY2A4LQzWPjFnR0RUkKHnrh-QjOsXeOT8I3FWHbETmZG8SiF96v_aem_Kr9-lmIq4aLbM6lQroto9Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spend approximately 4% of their income}}}\uc2  on average for gas, while households in the top fourth (earning $100,000 or more) spend less than 1%.\par \par \uc2 With the Iran war pushing up inflation and gas prices, most presidents would seek to show empathy by proclaiming: \u8220\'20\'1CI feel your pain.\u8221\'20\'1D But Trump did precisely the opposite, telling reporters that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about the economic pain Americans are feeling. \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000010901096/trump-iran-gas-prices-inflation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think about Americans\u8217\'20\'19 financial situation}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding that he only cares about Iran not having a nuclear weapon. Just as Trump has belittled concerns about affordability by saying those concerns are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/12/11/nx-s1-5639957/trump-affordability-hoax-economy-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hoax}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-trump-says-the-word-affordability-is-a-con-job-by-the-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 con job}}}\uc2 , he callously belittled Americans\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about soaring gas prices. \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kDZW5JzjXkY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is peanuts}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said about high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cflaunted his wealth, and people didn\u8217\'20\'19t mind\u8221\'20\'1D, Barrett Marson, a Republican strategist, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut now it\u8217\'20\'19s sort of like: \u8216\'20\'18{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/us/politics/trump-billionaire-iran-war-cost.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wow, you\u8217\'20\'19re really not feeling our pain}}}\uc2 , you are adding to our pain, and on top of that, you don\u8217\'20\'19t care about our pain.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With so many households just scraping by, it should be no surprise that Americans view this as a dark economic time. A May CBS/\uc2 YouGov\uc2  poll found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/politics/americans-largely-disapprove-of-trump-s-handling-of-the-economy-cbs-news-poll-finds/vi-AA23u0kB?uxmode=ruby"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 67% of Americans disapprove}}}\uc2  of how Trump is handling the economy. The \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  survey of consumer sentiment found in April that Americans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/consumer-sentiment-hits-record-low-per-michigan-survey-01ab85fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most pessimistic they\u8217\'20\'19ve been}}}\uc2  in the survey\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 Tragically, Trump is fiddling while many Americans are burning with anger about the state of the economy. Even as millions of hard-pressed Americans are traveling less and borrowing more, Trump is seeking to build a gilded ballroom and triumphal arch and make the Oval Office look like a room in Louis XIV\u8217\'20\'19s Versailles.\par \par \uc2 Trump seems to see himself as a gilded president of, by and for the gilded class. Not only did he invite many of the world\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/maryroeloffs/2025/01/20/billionaires-worth-a-combined-12-trillion-attended-trumps-inauguration-heres-who-was-there-from-musk-to-bezos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 richest billionaires to his inauguration}}}\uc2 , he took 15 CEOs, many of them billionaires, on his trip to China. Those CEOs\u8217\'20\'19 total wealth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/05/13/6-billionaires-worth-a-combined-1-trillion-join-trump-on-his-china-trip/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exceeded $1tn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many blue-collar Americans voted for Trump because they were convinced he would deliver to them, but those voters might not realize that Trump has taken many steps that have helped the rich and corporations while hurting average Americans. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/1-trillion-in-medicaid-cuts-1-trillion-in-tax-giveaways-for-the-richest-1-percent-the-one-big-beautiful-bills-budget-math/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1tn in tax cuts}}}\uc2  for the richest 1%, while it stuck it to people on the bottom with its $1.1tn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bipartisanpolicy.org/explainer/what-does-the-one-big-beautiful-bill-cost/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cuts to Medicaid and food assistance}}}\uc2 . In a big favor to the country\u8217\'20\'19s banks (and their shareholders), Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2026/03/16/the-zombie-regulator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gutted the Consumer Financial Protection Board}}}\uc2 , which was created to protect average Americans from being cheated by predatory financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 Trump has given a huge present to crypto companies and crypto billionaires by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/24/us/how-prediction-markets-and-crypto-firms-steamrolled-a-watchdog-agency.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ending nearly all enforcement}}}\uc2  against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/cryptocurrency-and-ai-scams-bilk-americans-of-billions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scandal-plagued industry}}}\uc2 , which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/crypto/articles/crypto-fraud-led-11-4b-173107843.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ripped off tens of thousands of Americans}}}\uc2 . Even as millions of Americans struggle, the Trump family\u8217\'20\'19s wealth, thanks to crypto and other investments, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/a-reporter-at-large/trumps-profiteering-hits-four-billion-dollars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared by an estimated $4bn}}}\uc2  since Trump won a second term. Trump promised to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/17/trump-energy-bill-prices-increase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chop energy prices in half}}}\uc2 , but he has instead pushed up electricity prices for many Americans by declaring war on cheap renewable energy sources such as solar and wind and by easing the way for AI companies to build electricity-devouring data centers.\par \par \uc2 As tens of millions of American struggle from paycheck to paycheck, Trump has done nothing to raise the $7.25-an-hour federal minimum wage. He has proposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2026/01/29/nx-s1-5626767/home-care-seniors-trump-labor-overtime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denying minimum wage and overtime protections}}}\uc2  to more than 3 million homecare workers. He has chopped the minimum wage for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-trump-administration-is-quietly-gutting-minimum-wage-protections-for-millions-of-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 workers employed by federal contractors}}}\uc2 , and with his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/27/magazine/trump-federal-workers-labor-unions.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many anti-union actions}}}\uc2 , he has weakened workers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to bargain for higher wages.\par \par \uc2 Candidate Trump talked repeatedly about fighting for average Americans, but, under Second-Term Trump, the US economy has essentially gone from being a lower-case k to an upper-case, more unequal K. Our Trumpified economy favors the wealthy more than ever.\par \par \uc2 In this new Gilded Age, Trump and many billionaires think a K-shape is exactly how the world and economy should be, with the rich getting ever richer, and who cares about the little people. But for the vast majority of Americans, those on the bottom part of the K, the K-shaped economy is definitely not OK, and they should say that loud and clear.\par \par \uc2 * Steven Greenhouse is a journalist and author, focusing on labor and the workplace, as well as economic and legal issues\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260604em64000mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
