\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Federal workers experiencing \u8216\'20\'18PTSD-like symptoms\u8217\'20\'19 after unlawful firings by Trump administration\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 979 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2026\par 16:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In survey of more than 300 fired probationary employees, 95% reported continuing mental health effects\par \par \uc2 US federal workers laid off by the Trump administration say they are experiencing mental health effects, including PTSD-like symptoms, from losing their jobs, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.27unihted.org/probationaryhome"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than 300 fired probationary employees were surveyed, with 95% reporting ongoing mental health effects, according to 27UNIHTED, a network of former National Institute of Health (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ) employees. Nearly half said they were experiencing PTSD-like symptoms, and a quarter are taking new medications to manage symptoms.\par \par \uc2 Survey respondents were located across 43 states and the US Virgin Islands and had worked in 12 different departments across 15 agencies, bureaus and subgroups.\par \par \uc2 The employees are a tiny fraction of the more than 300,000 federal workers who were laid off or pushed to resign or retire since the start of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second term. More than 25,000 workers were laid off in the middle of their probationary period, meaning they had started their positions within a year or two when they were abruptly fired.\par \par \uc2 Brier Ryver worked as a park ranger at the Crystal River national wildlife refuge, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s only wildlife refuge for manatees, when she was fired along with other federal probationary employees.\par \par \uc2 She was in the midst of a six weeks education program teaching children when another probationary colleague was terminated. She was temporarily reinstated in March 2025 but was ultimately fired again that May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love that job, so I went back to it, but the instability was very apparent,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryver said. \u8220\'20\'1CEven now, still talking to people who are still reinstated, it still feels like they\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for the other shoe to drop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atg.wa.gov/news/news-releases/judge-rules-trump-s-mass-terminations-broke-law-and-risked-public-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  in September that the firing of federal probationary employees was unlawful, though the federal government was not required to reinstate terminated employees. The judge overseeing the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cand.444883/gov.uscourts.cand.444883.261.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  concerns that the supreme court would overrule the relief if he ordered reinstatement of the fired workers.\par \par \uc2 Ryver noted the firings had set a precedent that could allow the federal government to fire employees on a whim despite civil service protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese unlawful terminations that should have never happened in the first place have had deep personal impacts,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryver said. \u8220\'20\'1CI still have PTSD-like symptoms in my own life that are impacting my ability to work, and although I\u8217\'20\'19m in a different role now, it\u8217\'20\'19s still at the back of my mind, what happened to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christa Reynolds worked as a contractor for the \uc2 NIH\uc2  for eight years before taking a role at the agency as a program analyst.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like I was doing really well. I got an award from my department, I got really good performance reviews,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said. \u8220\'20\'1CThen just like out of nowhere, this illegal firing took place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reynolds, who helped conduct the survey, said she was disappointed by the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in September, noting that federal workers are not supposed to do work at the whims of a president administration, but instead focus on benefiting the public.\par \par \uc2 She recalls a comment \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s lead architect, made in private in 2024, before he was appointed the head of the office of management and budget: \u8220\'20\'1CWe want the bureaucrats to be traumatically affected,\u8221\'20\'1D he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/10/who-is-russell-vought-trump-office-of-management-and-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just seems like a terrible thing to say. You\u8217\'20\'19re targeting people who have dedicated their careers to helping the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Reynolds.\par \par \uc2 The White House deferred comment to the office of personnel management. The office of personnel management did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Several court cases related to the firings of probationary employees are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/opm-directs-federal-agencies-to-fire-recently-hired-probationary-employees/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing}}}\uc2  and workers have filed appeals with the merit systems protection board.\par \par \uc2 As these cases proceed in the court, many probationary workers are still struggling to find a new job with comparable pay. One in five respondents reported being unemployed as of 31 January, and 49% who found new jobs reported earning significantly less in their new positions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.27unihted.org/probationarycareer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 11%}}}\uc2  of fired probationary workers found another role in the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Those findings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrgrapevine.com/us/content/article/2026-01-21-trump-brushes-off-317000-federal-job-cuts-with-one-word-critique"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contradict}}}\uc2  a claim Trump made in January that fired federal workers are \u8220\'20\'1Cgetting sometimes twice as much money, three times as much money\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re getting much better jobs and much higher pay\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dr Whitney Behr, who started working as a biologist with US Fish and Wildlife in June 2024, was fired in February 2025 while traveling for a work training event because she was in a probationary period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI moved out of my apartment immediately after being fired because I knew I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford it any more, and moved in with family a few hours away,\u8221\'20\'1D said Behr.\par \par \uc2 Though she was temporarily reinstated after a court order, \u8220\'20\'1Cit also seemed like they were going to fire us again\u8221\'20\'1D. By May 2025, when several agencies were firing probationary employees again, Behr had already accepted a job offer in the UK. More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.science.org/content/article/u-s-government-has-lost-more-10-000-stem-ph-d-s-trump-took-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10,000 doctoral-trained experts}}}\uc2  in science and related fields have left the US since Trump started his second term, according to an analysis by Science.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of PhD-level scientists that the government lost,\u8221\'20\'1D Behr said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are species going extinct right now and there\u8217\'20\'19s just nothing we can do about it. There are projects that were paid for that are not getting completed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Behr said that she continued to \u8220\'20\'1Crage at the open theft\u8221\'20\'1D from American taxpayers, who are paying into a dysfunctional federal government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would like people to be aware of what has been stolen from them, and not just our careers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI would like people to understand that they are being stolen from in ways that may not be able to be repaired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260603em63002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
