\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares drop after announcing $80bn share sale, as AI threatens to drive up youth unemployment \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Graeme Wearden \par \uc2 3,198 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2026\par 15:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rolling coverage of the latest economic and financial newsAnthropic confidentially files for initial public offering on US stock market\par \par \uc2 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing post\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/alphabet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alphabet}}}\uc2 , has said it plans to raise up to $80bn (\u163\'00\'A359bn) in equity to fund its vast artificial intelligence infrastructure investments, raising further questions over the economics of the AI boom.\par \par \uc2 The move, the largest equity fundraising ever according to analysts, includes a $10bn share sale to the US investment group \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2 , which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/03/warren-buffett-retirement-berkshire-hathaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led until last year}}}\uc2  by the investment guru \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 , which is behind the Gemini system that has been increasing its share of the AI chatbot market, said it would use the money to expand its \u8220\'20\'1Cworld-class AI compute infrastructure to meet its unprecedented customer demand\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The California-based company said: \u8220\'20\'1CAI is driving an expansionary moment for \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 . The company is experiencing strong demand for its AI solutions and services from enterprises and consumers, at levels that are exceeding the company\u8217\'20\'19s available supply. By scaling its investments, the company seeks to expand its foundational infrastructure to support the significant growth opportunity ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nicholas Hyett, the lead alternatives analyst at \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 , said the planned stock sale was much larger than previous secondary share sales, and would also raise more money than the largest stock market flotations, known as initial public offering (IPOs).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British Chambers of Commerce\uc2  has warned that youth unemployment in the UK will rise in 2026 and 2027, due to higher taxes, minimum wage rises and the rise of AI.\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are recovering some of their earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re now down 1.4%, at $370.99.\par \par \uc2 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  governor \uc2 Andrew Bailey\uc2  has told MPs it is important to get inflation back to target.\par \par \uc2 Testifying to the House of Lords\u8217\'20\'19 Economic Affairs Committee, Bailey said:\par \par \uc2 The answer to above-target inflation is not to lift the target\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surprisingly, the number of job vacancies across the US economy has jumped.\par \par \uc2 There were 7.6 million job openings available in April, the \uc2 U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  has reported, up from around 6.88m in March.\par \par \uc2 That might calm concerns that AI systems are hitting hiring and driving up unemployment.\par \par \uc2 In April, the number of job openings increased in professional and business services (+668,000), but decreased in finance and insurance (-135,000), the \uc2 US Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shares in US chip firm \uc2 Marvell\uc2  have jumped by 23% in early trading, after \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  chief executive JensenHuang said \uc2 Marvell\uc2  could be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next trillion-dollar company.\u8221\'20\'1D ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/jun/02/alphabet-80bn-share-sales-ai-spending-berkshire-hathaway-stock-markets-oil-interest-rates-inflation-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6a1eb4358f082ffc2d6f2812#block-6a1eb4358f082ffc2d6f2812"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see earlier post}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The tech-focused NasdaqComposite share index has dipped by 0.27% in early trading, with \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  among the big fallers.\par \par \uc2 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s planned $80bn equity raise, and AI rival \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s IPO filing last night, shows tech firms are making \u8220\'20\'1Ca decisive shift back toward public markets\u8221\'20\'1D as their funding demands accelerate.\par \par \uc2 So says Michael Field, chief equity analyst at investment research group \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 , adding:\par \par \uc2 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 's shares fall 4% after $80bn share sales announced\par \par \uc2 Over on Wall Street, shares in \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  have dropped at the start of trading after it announced $80bn of share sales last night.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share price is down by 4% in early trading to $361.10.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s down from its closing level of $376.37 on Monday night, which valued \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company at over $4.5trn.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/jun/02/alphabet-80bn-share-sales-ai-spending-berkshire-hathaway-stock-markets-oil-interest-rates-inflation-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6a1e75b48f08cd3a6a941d25#block-6a1e75b48f08cd3a6a941d25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As explained in the introduction of this blog}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  is raising $40bn to fund its \u8220\'20\'1CAI infrastructure and global compute\u8221\'20\'1D, plus another $40bn to cover costs such as \u8220\'20\'1Ctax obligations associated with vesting of employee equity awards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/jun/02/alphabet-80bn-share-sales-ai-spending-berkshire-hathaway-stock-markets-oil-interest-rates-inflation-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6a1eab188f088d87ce8faa45#block-6a1eab188f088d87ce8faa45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Analysts say }}}\uc2 this secondary share offering is the largest on record, dwarfing the amount raise in the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest IPOs.\par \par \uc2 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though economists still debate whether AI will destroy jobs or create them, the prevailing mood in Silicon Valley is far more pessimistic,\par \par \uc2 writes Harvard professor \uc2 Ken Rogoff\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 1.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 British Land\uc2  appoints \uc2 Joanne McNamara\uc2  as CEO\par \par \uc2 British Land\uc2 , one of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s biggest property developers, has appointed \uc2 Joanne McNamara\uc2  as its new chief executive, a senior executive from the real estate arm of a Canadian pension fund.\par \par \uc2 She will succeed SimonCarter, who{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.britishland.com/news/simon-carter-to-step-down-as-chief-executive-officer-of-british-land/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  quit in January}}}\uc2  after over five years as CEO of \uc2 British Land\uc2  and 18 years at the company. He is taking the reins at P3 Logistics Parks, an investor, manager and developer of warehouses in Europe owned by Singapore\u8217\'20\'19s sovereign wealth fund \uc2 GIC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McNamara currently runs the European business at \uc2 Oxford Properties\uc2 , a global real estate investor, developer and manager owned by the Ontario Municipal Employees Retirement System, one of Canada\u8217\'20\'19s largest pension funds.\par \par \uc2 She will be one of just a handful of female bosses at FTSE100 companies, and a rare female leader in the male-dominated real estate sector.\par \par \uc2 McNamara has more than 20 years\u8217\'20\'19 experience in real restate, and joined Oxford Properties in 2010 as one of its first team members in London, where she built a 70-plus European team and a portfolio of offices, retail, housing and warehouses worth \u163\'00\'A38bn. She previously worked at the developer Hammerson and the investment group DTZ.\par \par \uc2 She is expected to join British Land by the end of November at the latest after her notice period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoanne is one of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s most respected real estate professionals,\u8221\'20\'1D said WilliamRucker, chair of BritishLand. \u8220\'20\'1CWith her deep expertise of real estate, valuable experience in the world of private capital and a strong reputation for decisive leadership, she is exceptionally well placed to drive the business forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McNamara said:\par \par \uc2 British Land and Oxford Properties teamed to build the Leadenhall Building in the City, known as the Cheesegrater, which opened in July 2014\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s year-on-year inflation reached a record high in May, the worst since World War II, Associated Press report.\par \par \uc2 The Iranian consumer price index rose 77.2% in May compared to the previous year.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in daily and general needs \u8212\'20\'14 like medicine, taxi fares, tobacco and communication fees \u8212\'20\'14 rose 113.8% from the year before.\par \par \uc2 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oil price drops on Middle East peace hopes\par \par \uc2 The AI boom is one of two issues dominating the markets at the moment.\par \par \uc2 The other is the Middle East conflict, where investors are looking for signs of a breakthrough in the US-Iran peace talks.\par \par \uc2 Today, the oil price has dipped by around 1% after Donald Trump hailed an agreement to de-escalate the fighting in Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Trump said Hezbollah, through intermediaries, had pledged not to attack Israel, while Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu agreed to pull back any troops preparing to attack Beirut.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s helped to push Brent crude down to $93.90 a barrel, a day after oil prices jumped as relations between Tehran and Washington DC appeared to deteriorate.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets are a little higher today too, with the FTSE 100 share index up 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COil down, markets up \u8211\'20\'13 these are welcome movements for investors after three months of uncertainty around the Iran war,\u8221\'20\'1D says Russ Mould, investment director at AJ Bell, adding:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 11.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Nvidia\u8217\'20\'19s Jensen Huang says Marvell could be the next trillion-dollar company\par \par \uc2 Shares in semiconductor firm Marvell Technology have surged by 25% in premarket trading after Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang called the chipmaker the next \u8220\'20\'1Ctrillion-dollar company.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Huang made the comments at the Computex trade show in Taipei, where he was appearing alongside Marvell CEO MattMurphy.\par \par \uc2 Huang explained that Marvell\u8217\'20\'19s networking and connectivity chips are essential to data centres; they share computing tasks between thousands of connected chips, saying:\par \par \uc2 Before Huang\u8217\'20\'19s comment, Marvell\u8217\'20\'19s was valued at almost $192bn.\par \par \uc2 Last week, chipmakers SKHynix and Micron hit the $1tn mark for the first time.\par \par \uc2 11.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown: Alphabet AI share sale dwarfs previous fundraises\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/jun/02/alphabet-80bn-share-sales-ai-spending-berkshire-hathaway-stock-markets-oil-interest-rates-inflation-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6a1e75b48f08cd3a6a941d25#block-6a1e75b48f08cd3a6a941d25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s new $80bn share sale}}}\uc2  appears to be the largest equity raising ever, suggests Nicholas Hyett\u8203\'20\'0B, lead alternatives analyst at{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hl.co.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hyett explains that the stock sale is much larger than previous secondary share sales of this time, and is also raising more money than the largest stock market flotations (\u8216\'20\'18initial public offerings\u8217\'20\'19, os IPOs).\par \par \uc2 Hyett says:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.55am BST\par \par \uc2 11.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Wessex Water has announced the retirement of its chief financial officer, Andy Pymer, in the latest shake-up at the top of the utility owned by Malaysian group YTL.\par \par \uc2 Pymer will be replaced later this year by RichardEadie, executive finance director at Anglian Water Services. Eadie will serve under RuthJefferson, who replaced long-serving chief executive ColinSkellett in October 2024.\par \par \uc2 Pymer served as chief financial officer from 2020, during one of the most turbulent and scandal-hit periods ever for the water industry.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jan/10/wessex-water-bosses-extra-pay-uk-bonus-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay of Pymer and Jefferson came under scrutiny}}}\uc2  after the Guardian reported on previously undisclosed payments, worth a combined \u163\'00\'A350,000. The payments were made to the pair by other companies in the YTLGroup in the same year that the company was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/05/bosses-at-six-water-firms-had-bonuses-blocked-under-new-rules-ofwat-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned from paying bonuses}}}\uc2  - although Wessex denied they were bonus payments. Pymer\u8217\'20\'19s pay for the last financial year from the regulated water company was \u163\'00\'A3249,000.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s reporting on the pay arrangements prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hansard.parliament.uk/commons/2026-02-05/debates/AD3EEF99-081B-4F9C-B899-CF096C6D9854/WaterCompanyExecutivesUndisclosedPayments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questions in parliament}}}\uc2 . A junior environment minister, EmmaHardy, said the Wessex situation \u8220\'20\'1Cbaffles me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 Ruth Jefferson, Wessex\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, said that Pymer \u8220\'20\'1Chas made an outstanding contribution to Wessex Water over more than three decades, and it has been a great pleasure to work alongside him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Gold overtakes US Treasuries as world\u8217\'20\'19s top reserve asset, ECB says\par \par \uc2 In a landmark moment, gold has overtaken US government bonds as the world\u8217\'20\'19s top reserve asset, according to calculations from the European Central Bank.\par \par \uc2 The ECB says that gold made up 27% of total official foreign reserves at the end of 2025, ahead of US Treasuries (22% of reserves) and the euro (15%).\par \par \uc2 A year earlier, gold was 20% of reserves.\par \par \uc2 The jump last year was partly due to increased purchases by central banks, as geopolitical tensions have risen.\par \par \uc2 In a report on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/other-publications/ire/html/ecb.ire202606.en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The international role of the euro}}}\uc2 , ECB president ChristineLagarde says:\par \par \uc2 But the increase in gold holdings is also because the value of bullion jumped over the last two years, meaning the metal held by central banks is much more valuable.\par \par \uc2 The ECB says:\par \par \uc2 10.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Eurozone inflation rises to 3.2%\par \par \uc2 Inflation across the eurozone has risen to its highest level since September 2023, adding to the pressure on the European Central Bank to lift interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Eurozone consumer price inflation hit 3.2% in May, a new estimate from statistics body Eurostat shows, up from 3% in April.\par \par \uc2 That means prices are accelerating faster than the ECB\u8217\'20\'19s 2% target, which could spur policymakers to vote to raise eurozone interest rates at their meeting next week.\par \par \uc2 Energy prices drove inflation higher. Energy inflation rose to 10.9% in May, while services rose by 3.5% per year. Food, alcohol & tobacco inflation dropped to 2.0%, while industrial goods inflation rose slightly to 0.9%.\par \par \uc2 Emeritus professor JoeNellis, economic adviser at accountancy and advisory firm MHA, says:\par \par \uc2 9.55am BST\par \par \uc2 UK mortgage approvals highest since January 2025\par \par \uc2 UK mortgage approvals have hit a 15-month high, despite the Middle East crisis driving up interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of England has reported that 65,900 mortgages were approved in April, up from almost 64,000 in March, on a seasonally adjusted basis. That\u8217\'20\'19s the highest level since January 2025.\par \par \uc2 However, net borrowing of mortgage debt by individuals decreased to \u163\'00\'A34.4bn in April, from \u163\'00\'A36.8bn in March.\par \par \uc2 Martin Beck, chief economist at WPI Strategy, says:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.04am BST\par \par \uc2 9.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Alphabet shares down slightly\par \par \uc2 Shares in Alphabet have dipped in pre-market trading, as investors digest its planned $80bn stock sale.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re down 1.8% at $369.63.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a modest reaction, showing that traders hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been spooked.\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s because the $80bn stock sale won\u8217\'20\'19t land on the market in one go. The $40bn \u8220\'20\'1Cat-the-market (ATM) offering\u8221\'20\'1D will raise money for Alphabet over time, as shares are trickled onto the market gradually.\par \par \uc2 The $30bn of shares sold though the \u8220\'20\'1Caggregate underwritten offerings\u8221\'20\'1D will be held by the investment banks who underwrite the deal. They wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t dump the stock on the market in one go either.\par \par \uc2 Plus, Berkshire Hathaway could be expected to hold onto its new $10bn stake, as it has been investing in Alphabet for a while.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s shares are up 126% over the last year.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.21am BST\par \par \uc2 8.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly a fifth of young people set to be unemployed next year as AI hits jobs market\par \par \uc2 Youth unemployment in the UK is set to hit almost 18% next year, as the rollout of AI systems destroys some entry level jobs.\par \par \uc2 The British Chambers of Commerce has predicted that the UK\u8217\'20\'19s youth unemployment rate will rise to 16.9% this year, up from 16.1% in the last quarter of 2025, and then hit 17.88% in 2027.\par \par \uc2 That would mean that almost a fifth of young people would be out of work next year.\par \par \uc2 The BCC blamed higher taxes, minimum wage rises and the rise of AI, saying:\par \par \uc2 Last week, former health secretary Alan Milburn warned that the number of young people not in education, employment or training risked creating a \u8216\'20\'18lost generation\u8217\'20\'19:\par \par \uc2 The BCC has also trimmed its forecast for UK growth this year to 0.9%, down from 1.0% previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 It warned:\par \par \uc2 8.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Third economic pole needed to protect from 'Trump shock'\par \par \uc2 A new economic alliance between the EU and like-minded Asian allies should be set up to save the world\u8217\'20\'19s economies from \u8220\'20\'1CTrump shock\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chathamhouse.org/2026/06/saving-global-economic-governance-trump-shock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new report}}}\uc2  by Chatham House, the foreign affairs think tank, says.\par \par \uc2 It was authored by CreonButler, former director for international economic affairs in the National Security Secretariat in the UK cabinet office, and a \u8220\'20\'1Csous sherpa\u8221\'20\'1D at the G7 and G20 summits,\par \par \uc2 He calls for a \u8220\'20\'1Cthird economic pole\u8221\'20\'1D initially be made up of EU countries and members of the Comprehensive and Progressive Trans-Pacific Partnership who are committed to following rules-based trade.\par \par \uc2 The alliance should exclude the US and China as the former has made a dramatic break from rules while the latter has never fully committed to WTO rules, it argues.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chathamhouse.org/2026/06/saving-global-economic-governance-trump-shock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The report says}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Establishing a \u8220\'20\'1Cthird pole\u8221\'20\'1D would allow like minded countries to preserve and improve core rules in the largest economic space available with the EU and CPTPP countries between them accounting for 32% of global GDP. Others including the South Korea, Brazil, Turkey and South Africa.\par \par \uc2 The report adds:\par \par \uc2 The UK would be well position to take the group further. It is also the country likely to be \u8220\'20\'1Cmost damaged\u8221\'20\'1D if the current trade disorder prevails, it says, adding the \u8220\'20\'1Cthird pole\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D regardless of who is in the White House.\par \par \uc2 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Troy Hooper, co-head of equity capital markets for the Americas at the financial intelligence provider Mergermarket, said Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s funding plans underscored the intensity of the race to lead the AI buildout.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/6/2/google-parent-alphabet-to-sell-80bn-in-stock-to-fund-ai-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hooper }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/6/2/google-parent-alphabet-to-sell-80bn-in-stock-to-fund-ai-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/6/2/google-parent-alphabet-to-sell-80bn-in-stock-to-fund-ai-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Al Jazeera}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 8.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Tech giants are no longer 'capital-light free cash flow machines'\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the details of Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s $80bn equity raise:\par \par \uc2 Proposed Offerings\par \par \uc2 * Concurrent underwritten offerings: $30 billion underwritten public offerings, consisting of: $15 billion in depositary shares representing mandatory convertible preferred stock; and $15 billion in Class A Common Stock and Class C Capital Stock; and\par \par \uc2 * At-the-market offering: $40 billion at-the-market, or ATM, offering program for Class A Common Stock and Class C Capital Stock over time, expected to begin in Q3 2026.\par \par \uc2 Private Placement:\par \par \uc2 In addition, Alphabet has reached an agreement to sell $10 billion of stock to Berkshire Hathaway Inc. in a private placement, comprised of $5 billion in Class A Common Stock at a price of $351.81 per share and $5 billion in Class C Capital Stock at a price of $348.20 per share.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://74n5c4m7.r.eu-west-1.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.hl.co.uk%2Fwriters%2Fmatt-britzman/1/0102019e871db697-e516e67b-c99c-4761-ae90-721753776ed8-000000/OpFN9gC4qDnJG-2Z3XpswBB6AIs=473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Britzman}}}\uc2 , senior equity analyst at Hargreaves Lansdown, says this marks a shift in the financies of major tech firms:\par \par \uc2 7.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s massive share sale, and Anthropic\u8217\'20\'19s IPO, are also reminders that an AI crash would have serious consequences for investors, both large and small.\par \par \uc2 Ipek\par \par \uc2 Ozkardeskaya, senior analyst at Swissquote, explains:\par \par \uc2 7.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Alphabet to raise $80bn for AI spending\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 The economics of the AI boom are back in focus today, after Google\u8217\'20\'19s parent company Alphabet said it plans to raise up to $80bn in equity to \u8211\'20\'13 in part - fund its vast AI infrastructure investments.\par \par \uc2 The move is one of the largest equity raisings ever, and includes a $10bn share sale to investsment giant BerkshireHathaway\par \par \uc2 Alphabet, whose Gemini AI system has been growing its share of the AI chatbot market, says it will use the money to expand its \u8220\'20\'1Cworld-class AI compute infrastructure to meet its unprecedented customer demand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company says:\par \par \uc2 But, such a huge fundraising is also a warning to the markets that, for all the many billions of dollars thrown at AI infrastructure, meaningful returns are limited.\par \par \uc2 Jim\par \par \uc2 Reid, market strategist at DeutscheBank, told clients that Alhabet is reminding investors of the \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented scale of the AI spending boom\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 The decision to tap BerkshireHathaway is eye-catching too. Under the now-retired Warren Buffett, Berkshire made a habit of stepping in to provide important, and lucrative, funding for companies who really needed cash, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goldmansachs.com/our-firm/history/moments/2008-buffett-investment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the famous $5bn investment into Goldman Sachs at the height of the financial crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s206.q4cdn.com/479360582/files/doc_news/2026/Jun/01/attachments/2026-June-Alphabet-Equity-Capital-Raise-Press-Release-PDF.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In its filing}}}\uc2 , Alphabet explains that half the $80bn will be dedicated to \u8220\'20\'1Cscale AI infrastructure and global compute\u8221\'20\'1D, with $40bn set aside to cover \u8220\'20\'1Can administrative change to how it meets tax obligations associated with vesting of employee equity awards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet is also tapping investors before some of its largest AI rivals attempt to join the stock market.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Anthropic -which makes the Claude chatbot \u8211\'20\'13 said it had filed confidentially for an initial public offering on the US stock market.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic is now valued at $965bn after raising $65bn in funding, meaning it has leapfrogged OpenAI to become the world\u8217\'20\'19s most valuable startup.\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 * 9.30am BST: Bank of England mortgage approvals and consumer credit data\par \par \uc2 * 9.45am BST: Treasury Committee session on student loans\par \par \uc2 * 10am BST: Eurozone inflation report for May\par \par \uc2 * 3pm BST: US JOLTS vacancies report\par \par \uc2 * 3pm BST: Bank of England governor Andrew Bailey: Oral evidence to the Lords Economic Affairs Committee\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260602em620015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
