\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Protests continue at New Jersey ICE facility as hunger strike enters ninth day\b0\par\par\uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Olivares and Julius Constantine Motal in Newark \par \uc2 509 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2026\par 18:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Newark detention center has been at the forefront of anti-ICE protests \u8211\'20\'13 and now counterprotests\par \par \uc2 Protests continued on Saturday in front of the Delaney Hall immigration detention center in Newark, New Jersey, as a hunger and labor strike inside reached its ninth day, with detained immigrants demanding improved conditions and medical care.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday morning, a small group of rightwing counterprotesters in Trump hats began demonstrating outside the facility waving signs and chanting slogans in support of \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)\uc2 . The protesters supporting the detained immigrants and the counterprotesters supporting ICE yelled at each other across barricades set up by state police.\par \par \uc2 The dueling Saturday demonstrations followed a hectic Friday night, during which state police fired teargas canisters and pepper ball pellets at anti-ICE protesters. State police also arrived on horseback, driving protesters back from the detention center.\par \par \uc2 On Friday afternoon, New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Mikie Sherrill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/29/new-jersey-delaney-hall-police-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that state officials would be taking over policing outside the facility from ICE. As part of the state police\u8217\'20\'19s work, they attempted to set up fences to establish a \u8220\'20\'1Cprotected speech zone\u8221\'20\'1D to contain protesters.\par \par \uc2 Top Trump officials praised New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s governor following Friday night\u8217\'20\'19s clashes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you @GovSherrillNJ for cooperating with us to help restore law and order,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  secretary, \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SecMullinDHS/status/2060717271794774474"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  on social media. \u8220\'20\'1CWe support every Americans [sic] constitutional right to peacefully protest. No one has the right to RIOT and ASSAULT law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope to build on this partnership and work together to remove the worst of the worst from New Jersey communities,\u8221\'20\'1D Mullin added.\par \par \uc2 For nine days, detained immigrants inside the privately owned facility have been striking for improved conditions and medical care, and for their immigration cases to be resolved. Advocates said the striking immigrants have been met with retaliation by ICE and facility guards.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, guards inside the facility pepper-sprayed a group of immigrants who tried to stop guards from removing a detainee from the unit who was helping translate for the other strikers.\par \par \uc2 The facility is run by \uc2 Geo Group\uc2 , one of the biggest private prison companies in the US. A \uc2 Geo Group\uc2  spokesperson confirmed the pepper-spraying incident, telling the non-profit news site the City Reporter that guards were responding to \u8220\'20\'1Ca physical altercation involving detainees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Protesters in support of the strikers on Saturday outnumbered the rightwing counterprotesters, some of whom were members of the far-right Proud Boys.\par \par \uc2 In addition to state troopers, the Guardian observed a series of local law enforcement officers also present. This included local police from the Newark police department and county sheriff officers. A group of special agents with Homeland Security Investigations were posted behind the fences surrounding the detention center.\par \par \uc2 One of the main demands by the strikers has been to meet with the state governor. She was turned away from the facility this week.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260530em5u003uy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
