\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Burberry\uc2  boss could earn up to \u163\'00\'A312.2m under new bonus scheme as company rolls back climate goals\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Butler \par \uc2 707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 May 2026\par 15:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company, which paid boss \uc2 Joshua Schulman\uc2  \u163\'00\'A34m in year to March, becomes latest to extend deadline to become carbon neutralBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 The boss of \uc2 Burberry\uc2  could earn up to \u163\'00\'A312.2m after the luxury British brand introduced a new bonus scheme, while its annual report also revealed the company has scaled back its climate ambitions.\par \par \uc2 Joshua Schulman\uc2 , a former chief executive of the US fashion brand Coach who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/15/burberry-chief-executive-profit-warning-jonathan-akeroyd-joshua-schulman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hired in July 2024}}}\uc2  to help revive \uc2 Burberry\uc2 , was paid \u163\'00\'A34m in the year to March, up from \u163\'00\'A32.5m for his first nine months in the job.\par \par \uc2 The latest year\u8217\'20\'19s pay package included \u163\'00\'A31.2m in basic pay, a \u163\'00\'A32.3m annual cash bonus and \u163\'00\'A3299,000 in relocation assistance after a move from New York, according to \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual report published on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/may/14/burberrys-handbag-cotswolds-hits-sweet-spot-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made pre-tax profits of \u163\'00\'A349m}}}\uc2  in the year to 28 March, compared with a loss of \u163\'00\'A366m in the previous 12 months, as it cut \u163\'00\'A380m of annual costs, trimmed store numbers and won back Chinese and North American shoppers under Schulman\u8217\'20\'19s Burberry Forward campaign.\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 Burberry\uc2  has also become the latest business to push back its deadline to become carbon neutral by a decade to 2050. The annual report says: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have refined our climate targets to reflect a greater understanding of [greenhouse gas] emissions across our value chain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest change from a strategy set by Schulman\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, who five years ago pledged to have a net positive impact on the climate by 2040 and to reduce indirect greenhouse gas emissions by 46% by the end of the decade.\par \par \uc2 There have been similar moves to scale back efforts by other big companies, including \uc2 Unilever\uc2  and BP.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report states: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe our revised targets reflect a pragmatic response to external factors, while allowing us to maintain a level of ambition in line with our assessment of climate change as a principal risk facing our business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  sales remained flat year on year at \u163\'00\'A32.4bn once the effect of exchange rates was taken into account, as the brand moved away from discounting and prioritised sales of core products, including trench coats and scarves.\par \par \uc2 The pay package of \uc2 Kate Ferry\uc2 , the finance director of \uc2 Burberry\uc2 , has also more than doubled to \u163\'00\'A32.5m, up from \u163\'00\'A3904,000 the previous year, and included a \u163\'00\'A31.3m cash bonus and \u163\'00\'A3457,000 long-term bonus. Ferry could earn \u163\'00\'A35.6m this year if she hits all targets and \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share price increases by 50%.\par \par \uc2 From July, Schulman\u8217\'20\'19s basic pay will increase by 3% to \u163\'00\'A31.24m and he could also earn a new long-term share bonus worth up to 300% of salary if he meets performance targets that include increasing \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual revenues to \u163\'00\'A33.1bn by 2029.\par \par \uc2 That award will come on top of an existing share bonus that is being slightly reduced from a maximum of 162.5% of salary to 150%, if shareholders approve the new scheme at the company\u8217\'20\'19s annual meeting in July.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report said Schulman\u8217\'20\'19s target pay was \u163\'00\'A36.4m, which would put him at the upper end of FTSE 100 executive pay rates but the lower end of global peers. That figure could rise to \u163\'00\'A312.2m in three years based on the pay policy introduced this year if he hits the most \u8220\'20\'1Cstretching performance targets\u8221\'20\'1D and the share price increases by 50%. He could earn even more if his basic salary is increased further.\par \par \uc2 In the annual report, \uc2 Danuta Gray\uc2 , the chair of \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remuneration committee, said Schulman\u8217\'20\'19s reward scheme had \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen chosen so as to be appropriately incentivising\u8221\'20\'1D and aimed to retain him by improving his pay position relative to those heading the brand\u8217\'20\'19s luxury peers.\par \par \uc2 The report added that the scheme was also intended to be \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable\u8221\'20\'1D; \uc2 Burberry\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1Cnot sought to match USA pay levels\u8221\'20\'1D and the payout was also subject to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe delivery of stretching performance targets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Schulman became the chief executive of \uc2 Burberry\uc2  in July 2024, replacing \uc2 Jonathan Akeroyd\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260528em5s003jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
