\par\par \uc2 Money\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 Instagram\uc2  truly is the new \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19: why gen Z is using social media to get hired\b0\par\par\uc2 Jenna Zaza \par \uc2 1,257 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 May 2026\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In this competitive market, gen Z has started to turn to untraditional ways to land a job \u8211\'20\'13 including dating apps\par \par \uc2 Sibusisiwe Khupe, 26, entered the job market once again in September after a wave of unexpected layoffs at London marketing agency \uc2 Wieden+Kennedy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She knew landing her next full-time role was not going to be easy. Young workers have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/14/young-people-uk-jobs-market-unemployment-taxes-minimum-wages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit hard}}}\uc2  by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/mar/09/britain-job-market-floundering-companies-cautious-hiring"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weakening}}}\uc2  UK job market as vacancies fall and unemployment climbs to a five-year high.\par \par \uc2 Khupe, however, had a plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to not be confident or audacious because a lot of people are in the same boat,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She called herself a \u8220\'20\'1Creally hot, really talented, really funny\u8221\'20\'1D gen Zer in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/thelmasibusisiwe_chat-if-youre-looking-for-fresh-internet-breaking-share-7370551579059425281-af5R/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAD5tLwEBBiZyMBaxFU1HCmt_Yiq9G4xZD3M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI plastered my face across many, many slides along with my work experience. I was just very funny and authentic to who I was and just sent that to a bunch of senior executives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After about a four-month search, she landed a job that was also a step up \u8211\'20\'13 she is now a senior creative at Gravity Road, an advertising agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this climate, being bold and confident will go a long way because people will remember you,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Gen Z workers are entering the toughest job market since the pandemic. The number of job seekers vastly outweighs the number of positions, and competition is fierce. The global hiring rate has plunged to a five-year low and the number of applicants for every job opening has increased by nearly 30%, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://economicgraph.linkedin.com/content/dam/me/economicgraph/en-us/PDF/linkedIn-labor-market-report-building-a-future-of-work-that-works-jan-2026.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LinkedIn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As companies lean heavily on AI to vet r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9s and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/may/01/uk-job-hunters-frustration-ai-interviews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even do interviews}}}\uc2  en masse, new graduates are turning to social media platforms to stand out. Young workers are using quirky, personal videos, cold emails and offbeat social media posts to reach top executives directly.\par \par \uc2 TikToks are \u8220\'20\'1Cessentially becoming extensions of gen Z\u8217\'20\'19s r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9s\u8221\'20\'1D, said Vicki Salemi, career expert and talent strategist at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monster.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monster}}}\uc2  and a former recruiting manager at \uc2 Deloitte\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis generation is accustomed to creating content. They\u8217\'20\'19re treating the job search more like content creation than a traditional application process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gen Z is \u8220\'20\'1Caware that they have to employ every tactic out there available to them to get noticed\u8221\'20\'1D, said Priya Rathod, workplace trends editor at Indeed.\par \par \uc2 Going viral\par \par \uc2 Some gen Zers in the US say they are sending out as many as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2025/09/17/gen-z-graduate-unemployed-job-seeking-wall-street-poster-careers-linkedin-interviews/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,000}}}\uc2  applications without landing a job.\par \par \uc2 Anya Roodnitsky, 22, applied to hundreds of jobs in her senior year at \uc2 Dartmouth College\uc2 , where she\u8217\'20\'19s studying economics and environmental science. Each application took a few hours as she carefully tailored her r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 and cover letter to the role. By February, she hadn\u8217\'20\'19t heard back from a single company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot having a job offer lined up after college weighed down on me a lot,\u8221\'20\'1D Roodnitsky said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have an Ivy League degree. If I don\u8217\'20\'19t get a job, what was the point of me going to college and investing this much into my education?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After she hit the 300th application, she sat down at her kitchen table in New Hampshire, opened PowerPoint and filmed herself reformatting her r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 into a promotional slide deck, adding emojis, special skills and some desperate, self-deprecating humor. She described a $6,000 grant she got through school to model nuclear reactors as \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m, like, super cool. I\u8217\'20\'19m basically \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roodnitsky ended by adding that she loves wearing business casual, will bring baked goods to the office and a plea for advice or leads. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s getting bad out there,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Young workers in the US are facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2026/03/21/entry-level-jobs-gen-z-not-their-fault/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tough hiring conditions}}}\uc2  that are, by some measures, worse than they were during the Great Recession. Unemployment rates are higher, according to \uc2 LinkedIn{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://economicgraph.linkedin.com/content/dam/me/economicgraph/en-us/PDF/linkedIn-labor-market-report-building-a-future-of-work-that-works-jan-2026.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2 , and layoffs are rising fast.\par \par \uc2 Roodnitsky\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DU6VPHhEgGn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 94-second video}}}\uc2  got over half a million views and thousands of shares. She had 52 coffee chats, 20 referrals, 10 interviews and finally got one full-time job offer as a solar analyst. She starts soon after she graduates this May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Instagram\uc2  truly is the new \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she half joked.\par \par \uc2 Salemi said these strategies can help candidates network and land informational interviews. Video r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9s can also highlight soft skills like storytelling, enthusiasm and passion \u8211\'20\'13 helping applicants stand out.\par \par \uc2 However, Salemi said it \u8220\'20\'1Cis not a replacement to the r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 and structured hiring processes like applicant tracking systems\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Into the void\par \par \uc2 About 72% of candidates report that the job search negatively affects their mental health, and two-thirds feel burned out before they even land a job, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.theinterviewguys.com/state-of-job-search-mental-health-in-2026/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent analysis}}}\uc2  by The Interview Guys, a job-seeking website.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt often feels like they\u8217\'20\'19re applying into the void and hearing nothing back,\u8221\'20\'1D said Danielle Nicholson, a gen Z career coach. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not even certain if the jobs they\u8217\'20\'19re applying for are real \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s an extremely disheartening and maddening job market.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/may/24/gen-z-college-degree-employment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 College graduates}}}\uc2  face especially tough conditions. The unemployment rate for recent grads sits at almost 6% compared with the 4.2% for all workers of any age, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorkfed.org/research/college-labor-market#--:explore:unemployment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the Federal Reserve Bank of New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to become an influencer to get a job,\u8221\'20\'1D Nicholson said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut having some kind of professional presence online helps demonstrate that you\u8217\'20\'19re a real person with real skills.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 People who create custom videos and other materials with a strong application will stand out to employers, said Jade Walters, a gen Z career coach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you go above and beyond now, you probably will do the same when hired,\u8221\'20\'1D Walters added.\par \par \uc2 Some gen Zers are taking a step further by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://creators.yahoo.com/lifestyle/story/people-are-using-tinder-to-find-work-instead-of-love--some-say-its-working-213530555.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAIe6Rg1NrxLPRb5u_F72fMPJZebtKh-BHa2gS0YEci5yHnCi9o5tXJmL0JI1Rasco4B1z8aiwl6EMLuwSO2eCd7lgQ9vexpnshifR-hN2saiRUZkF22uQWLcsZfyBr6gB7RuLiWkbSXDtfRfD-cfAh5ZAXbts9nqMWKP8uWRNMep"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 using dating apps}}}\uc2  to build connections and land referrals. About one-third of dating app users say they use it for professional purposes, according to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.resumebuilder.com/1-in-3-dating-app-users-are-swiping-for-jobs-not-love/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  by Resume Builder.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The cherry on top\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Even if your \u8220\'20\'1CHire Me\u8221\'20\'1D video is a hit on social media, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean employment is guaranteed. \u8220\'20\'1CGoing viral isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough,\u8221\'20\'1D Roodnitsky said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am a very qualified person and still had to go through a lengthy application process to get my current job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And while gen Z tries out bold job-hunting stunts, there are some risks to making quirky \u8220\'20\'1Chire me\u8221\'20\'1D presentations too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVideo or decks may highlight a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s misalignment with the employer\u8217\'20\'19s culture, expectations or even industry norms,\u8221\'20\'1D Salemi said. And as more candidates use video, it risks losing its novelty. If a candidate decides to create a video r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 it needs to be specific for that industry, role and department, career coaches say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVideo r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9s could be like the cherry on top if the ice-cream is the exact flavor I want,\u8221\'20\'1D Rathod said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt may move the needle only if you have the other exact qualifications they are looking for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But many job seekers feel like moving the needle is exactly what they need. Luna Escobar, 20, a student at University of California, Berkeley, applied to nearly 30 internships, spending roughly eight hours per application or about 240 hours in total. Feeling like there was no way to stand out with traditional applications, she posted a video r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 on Instagram.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter posting the video, I finally heard back from one company after they ghosted me for months with a first-round interview request,\u8221\'20\'1D Escobar said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt definitely might\u8217\'20\'19ve pushed me to the next step. Hopefully I\u8217\'20\'19ll get a summer internship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260528em5s002js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
