\par\par \uc2 Food\par \b \uc2 Guzman y Gomez\uc2  faces class action from US workers over closed stores\b0\par\par\uc2 Jonathan Barrett Business editor \par \uc2 477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2026\par 05:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mexican-themed Australian fast food chain accused of terminating staff without adequate pay or notice as it pulls out of the US\par \par \uc2 American workers at \uc2 Guzman y Gomez\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shuttered US stores have launched a class action lawsuit against the Mexican-themed Australian fast food chain over allegations staff were terminated without adequate pay or notice.\par \par \uc2 The legal claim, filed in a US federal trial court in Illinois, was sparked by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/may/22/guzman-y-gomez-exits-us-after-succumbing-to-graveyard-for-australian-fast-food-chains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GyG\u8217\'20\'19s decision last week to immediately close its string of Chicago stores}}}\uc2  after giving up on its highly vaunted plans to expand in the US.\par \par \uc2 Workers say they first heard about the imminent closures on 21 May via an internal message posted on the company\u8217\'20\'19s message platform, according to the lawsuit filed by Chicago firm Haseeb Legal.\par \par \uc2 The message allegedly read: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter careful consideration, we have made the difficult decision to exit the US market. This means we will be closing all our restaurants from today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The class action claims that GyG was required under federal and state laws to provide 60 days\u8217\'20\'19 advance written notice before conducting a mass layoff.\par \par \uc2 It is seeking pay and benefits for up to 60 days for every affected employee \u8211\'20\'13 estimated by the law firm to number more than 500 \u8211\'20\'13 and is seeking a trial by jury.\par \par \uc2 A GyG spokesperson said the firm \u8220\'20\'1Cis aware of legal action filed in the United States and we are confident we have met all of our legal obligations to our US employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not in a position to provide further comment on this matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Australian-listed food chain has recorded significant growth in its home country and now boasts one of the fastest growing fast food networks in the country.\par \par \uc2 It ranks among the top 10 biggest fast food chains in Australia according to store numbers.\par \par \uc2 But its plans to break into a US market already rich with Mexican food and established competitors including Chipotle officially ended last week amid mounting losses.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have described the US market as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgraveyard\u8221\'20\'1D for Australian fast food chains after failed expansion attempts by Crust Pizza and Oporto.\par \par \uc2 Last week, GyG listed eight stores in its US network, all of which were located in the wider Chicago area. Its US website now reads: \u8220\'20\'1CAll GyG USA restaurants permanently closed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The class action has two named plaintiffs, both of whom had been baristas who were promoted to shift leaders. One earned $US21 an hour and the other $US23 an hour, according to the claim.\par \par \uc2 Neither received the required notice, nor required compensation, according to the class action allegations.\par \par \uc2 While the legal action names GyG\u8217\'20\'19s US entity as the defendant, it argues that the US operations and GyG Australia constituted a \u8220\'20\'1Csingle integrated enterprise\u8221\'20\'1D and employer, expanding the liability.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260525em5p0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
