\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Billionaires are trying to lull us into AI complacency. Don\u8217\'20\'19t let them\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,590 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2026\par 16:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As resistance to datacenters grows, Musk and others are painting a rosy picture. But the US must institute protections\par \par \uc2 As Americans grow increasingly worried that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI}}}\uc2  will wipe out millions of jobs and create a permanent new underclass, tech billionaires are rushing to reassure us not to worry \u8211\'20\'13 the subtext being: please don\u8217\'20\'19t bring out the anti-AI pitchforks.\par \par \uc2 Even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , who recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/02/technology/spacex-xai-deal.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merged SpaceX with his AI company}}}\uc2 , has joined the effort, essentially telling people \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t worry, be happy\u8221\'20\'1D about AI. Musk wrote last month that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2044990537145753894?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E2044990537145753894%7Ctwgr%5E2b808668231291a94df09f1cc5805ea8c0032b00%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Felon-musk-universal-high-income-government-checks-ai-job-losses-2026-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUniversal HIGH INCOME via checks}}}\uc2  issued by the Federal government\u8221\'20\'1D would save everyone thrown out of work by AI.\par \par \uc2 Musk says that AI will create such gigantic productivity gains and such vast economic abundance that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2044990537145753894?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E2044990537145753894%7Ctwgr%5E2b808668231291a94df09f1cc5805ea8c0032b00%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Felon-musk-universal-high-income-government-checks-ai-job-losses-2026-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there will be no inflation}}}\uc2  and no need to \u8220\'20\'1Cworry about squirreling money away for retirement in 10 or 20 years\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-steve-hanke-universal-high-income-inflation-ai-unemployment-2026-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saving for retirement will be irrelevant,\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  he added.\par \par \uc2 As part of this reassurance chorus, \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 OpenAI{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/561e7512-253e-424b-9734-ef4098440601/Industrial%20Policy%20for%20the%20Intelligence%20Age.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a report}}}\uc2  last month that said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe promise of superintelligence is extraordinary \u8230\'20\'26 [AI] will speed up scientific and medical breakthroughs, significantly increase productivity, lower costs for families by making essential goods cheaper, and open the way for entirely new forms of work, creativity, and entrepreneurship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2 , the billionaire co-founder of \uc2 Palantir\uc2 , has also sought to minimize worries about AI, saying, \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/26/opinion/peter-thiel-antichrist-ross-douthat.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s more than a nothing-burger}}}\uc2 , and it\u8217\'20\'19s less than the total transformation of our society.\u8221\'20\'1D Thiel added that if we don\u8217\'20\'19t develop AI, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/26/opinion/peter-thiel-antichrist-ross-douthat.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alternative is just total stagnation}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Americans battling to block new datacenters across the US, Musk and other tech billionaires are seeking to lull the masses into believing that they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t fear AI and certainly shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t fight against it. But as Musk and other billionaires maneuver to make tens of billions of dollars from AI, everyone should be doubly dubious about their assurances.\par \par \uc2 People should be worried considering that \uc2 Dario Amodei\uc2 , \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, said AI could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/05/28/ai-jobs-white-collar-unemployment-anthropic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminate half of all entry-level white-collar jobs}}}\uc2  in one to five years and lift the unemployment rate to 20%. The CEO of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  AI, \uc2 Mustafa Suleyman\uc2 , warned that most white-collar work \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/microsoft-ai-chief-sets-two-235739710.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAANyoDTwp4_yl2CznmfqeesAXM-DBq3qZkGETFYrsp_DIWkvTUXpOFAX7pPofHuKhS4hPH-l45QF0KoOu0I6pAr-cMPKLD5nb90P8_QTEdMltl_aZSP7xAr8pmGj6wwcok9YEQ4XK6kvs76VTkT7ZrlCPfHZ3Z9PU0Z1FYHBSPTq1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be fully automated by an AI}}}\uc2  within the next 12 to 18 months\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As AI is rolled out across various industries, it is likely to have another important impact on workers, beyond any layoffs \u8211\'20\'13 AI will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/may/11/ai-worker-control-surveillance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used to control and surveil}}}\uc2  workers and pressure them to increase their productivity.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fox-news-poll-broad-anxiety-about-ai-doesnt-extend-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News poll found}}}\uc2  that nearly one-third of Americans fear that AI will eliminate their job over the next five years. But the Trump administration seems singularly unconcerned. Donald Trump has enthusiastically embraced AI and sought to speed the way for AI companies to advance and build datacenters. Kevin Hassett, a top Trump economic adviser, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/05/11/trump-white-house-hassett-ai-jobs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplayed job concerns}}}\uc2 , saying AI {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.techechelon.com/post/white-house-says-ai-is-not-eliminating-jobs-even-as-tech-layoffs-mount"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 isn\u8217\'20\'19t costing anyone their jobs}}}\uc2  even as tech layoffs mount.\par \par \uc2 Young people entering the job market should be especially worried. They shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be comforted by Musk\u8217\'20\'19s claims that AI will bring some magical economic nirvana. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://substack.com/home/post/p-196647383"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many economists}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://budgetmodel.wharton.upenn.edu/p/2025-09-08-the-projected-impact-of-generative-ai-on-future-productivity-growth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disagree strongly}}}\uc2  with Musk\u8217\'20\'19s bullish prediction that AI will result in super gains in productivity and an overabundance of goods and services.\par \par \uc2 It would be far wiser to heed Bernie Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 warnings than Musk\u8217\'20\'19s super-optimism. As the top Democratic-aligned member on the Senate health, education, labor and pensions committee, Sanders issued a report saying that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/10.6.2025-The-Big-Tech-Oligarchs-War-Against-Workers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI could replace tens of millions of jobs}}}\uc2  and that we as a nation need to take major steps to protect against AI\u8217\'20\'19s harms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-ocasio-cortez-announce-ai-data-center-moratorium-act/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We cannot sit back and allow a handful of billionaire}}}\uc2  Big Tech oligarchs to make decisions that will reshape our economy, our democracy and the future of humanity,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe time for action is now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In sharp contrast, Musk suggests that if we just wait a few years, AI will bring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2045589182308040856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 untold prosperity}}}\uc2 . Sorry, Elon, but I side with Bernie on this. We need to take action now to protect against AI\u8217\'20\'19s potentially disastrous effects: millions of layoffs, a huge increase in economic inequality, and the creation of a large, new underclass. Even Amodei has cautioned that AI may create {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.darioamodei.com/essay/the-adolescence-of-technology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Can unemployed or very-low-wage \u8216\'20\'18underclass\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With some experts saying that AI is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/experts-ai-biggest-thing-happen-070256400.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most far-reaching technological}}}\uc2  development in history \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1COf all the things humans have ever created, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gatesnotes.com/meet-bill/tech-thinking/reader/the-year-ahead-2026"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI will change society the most}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 we need to be prepared. We need to have a stronger safety net in place asap because AI is advancing so rapidly. Mass layoffs may come far faster than expected. (Although they might come more slowly and be smaller than we fear, too.) We can hope for the best, but we should plan for the worst.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s talk of high-income checks for everyone sounds wonderful, but that would require having a big-hearted, compassionate president and Congress to enact legislation to create such generous checks. Let\u8217\'20\'19s not forget that Musk and other tech billionaires helped elect scores of rightwing politicians eager to shred or shrink the social safety net \u8211\'20\'13 last year those politicians passed legislation that makes it far harder to receive food stamps and Medicaid if you don\u8217\'20\'19t have a job. So we can\u8217\'20\'19t rely at all on Musk and other billionaires to win enactment of UHI, universal high-income checks. \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/04/24/2026/progressives-skeptical-of-tech-billionaires-ubi-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I am skeptical about [the billionaires\u8217\'20\'19 and big tech companies\u8217\'20\'19] willingness}}}\uc2  to pay or incur the taxes necessary to sustain such proposals,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, a US representative who has teamed with Bernie Sanders to push for safeguards against AI.\par \par \uc2 There are several important steps that we as a nation should take to protect against AI\u8217\'20\'19s harms.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 We should guarantee health insurance for everyone. The US overwhelmingly ties health insurance to one\u8217\'20\'19s job, and the fear that AI could displace millions of workers is a strong argument for the US to finally do what every other industrial nation has done: adopt a system of universal health insurance, perhaps through Medicare for All. That way, workers thrown to the curb by AI won\u8217\'20\'19t need to panic about losing health coverage.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Wage insurance would be a smart, targeted program to help workers displaced by AI. Many of those workers will move to new jobs that pay significantly less than their old jobs, and wage insurance would be an important wage supplement, perhaps $10,000 a year. It would help offset workers\u8217\'20\'19 lower wages and encourage the unemployed to search for new jobs. Beyond that, the US should make its deeply flawed unemployment insurance system more generous. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/best-worst-states-unemployment-checks-170046797.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s maximum jobless benefit}}}\uc2  is just $235 a week; in Florida, it\u8217\'20\'19s just $275.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 In the event that AI does eliminate millions of jobs, the US should put in place a New Deal-like Works Progress Administration that would create millions of jobs for the unemployed. Perhaps they would repair the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure or work in childcare centers. Amid predictions that AI could incinerate millions of jobs, it would be unwise to rely on the market to create enough jobs for all the workers displaced by AI.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Before AI wipes out a wide swath of jobs, we should vastly improve the nation\u8217\'20\'19s less-than-stellar job training programs to prepare workers for whatever the jobs of the future will be, whether in healthcare, construction, green energy or other fields.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 We should share the productivity gains from AI by legislating a 32-hour workweek at the old 40 hours\u8217\'20\'19 pay \u8211\'20\'13 a move that should help reduce layoffs. What\u8217\'20\'19s more, if AI means that our economy can thrive with the labor force working far fewer hours, then the US should finally enact a law mandating paid vacations for all workers: perhaps two weeks for new hires, three weeks after two years, and four weeks after four years. (Every worker in the 27 nations of the European Union is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/08/17/1194467863/europe-vacation-holiday-paid-time-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guaranteed four weeks\u8217\'20\'19 paid vacation}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/9b93e02a-c693-4070-9094-a2f532dfa929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Universal basic capital}}}\uc2  would give Americans some funds that would enable them to share in the wealth created by AI. This grant of capital \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps in the form of shares in a universal investment fund \u8211\'20\'13 could be given to every American or to all workers or just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://singjupost.com/transcript-ai-the-future-of-work-w-david-autor-daron-acemoglu-the-weekly-show/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to people at birth}}}\uc2 . This, unlike universal basic income, would not only allow people to share in the profits and rising stock values, but would give people corporate voting rights. It would give the public a voice in running the nation\u8217\'20\'19s corporations, and hopefully in running AI companies, too.\par \par \uc2 Seeing all the public anger at AI datacenters, Sanders and Ocasio-Cortez have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-ocasio-cortez-announce-ai-data-center-moratorium-act/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for halting construction}}}\uc2  of all new datacenters nationwide until Congress enacts some basic protections against AI. Sanders and AOC hope that such a moratorium would be a lever to win, for instance, a ban on AI companies releasing products that can threaten our privacy and the future of humanity.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, AI companies and many billionaires will vigorously oppose such a moratorium along with any meaningful limits on AI. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we need a powerful people\u8217\'20\'19s movement to fight for the strong safeguards that American workers, the American public and the world will need to protect against the vast potential dangers of AI.\par \par \uc2 * Steven Greenhouse is a journalist and author, focusing on labor and the workplace, as well as economic and legal issues\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260519em5j0030f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
