\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Labor leaders call collective bargaining veto a \u8216\'20\'18betrayal\u8217\'20\'19 by Virginia governor\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 698 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2026\par 06:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union leaders say veto from Democrat \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  is an about-face from promises she made on campaign trail\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , vetoed a bill on Thursday that would have restored collective bargaining rights for 500,000 public sector workers in the state. Union leaders say the veto is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetrayal\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cslap in the face\u8221\'20\'1D after the governor campaigned last year on promises to restore collective bargaining rights.\par \par \uc2 Though majorities in both chambers of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s general assembly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1214349.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  legislation that would restore bargaining rights to most public sector workers, Spanberger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1219772.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  an amended version of the bill last month that was eventually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lis.virginia.gov/bill-details/20261/HB1263/text/HB1263VG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  by the assembly.\par \par \uc2 According to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/virginia-governors-amended-collective-bargaining-bill-would-leave-workers-rights-optional-and-large-public-sector-pay-gap-unaddressed/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , Spanberger\u8217\'20\'19s amended bill so heavily weakened the collective bargaining rights initially passed by the general assembly that it would \u8220\'20\'1Clock Virginia into an unstable, ineffective system in which collective bargaining would remain merely \u8216\'20\'18optional\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The veto was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wric.com/news/politics/capitol-connection/spanberger-to-veto-public-sector-collective-bargaining/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised }}}\uc2 by conservatives who claimed the bill would have brought on large tax increases.\par \par \uc2 Union leaders say the veto is an about-face from promises she made on the campaign trail. In February, a month after entering office, the governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://virginiamercury.com/2026/05/15/spanberger-vetoes-bills-allowing-public-employees-to-collectively-bargain-working-condition-wages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attended}}}\uc2  a rally in support of the bill held by the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ), according to the Virginia Mercury.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 SEIU\uc2  leaders April Verrett, LaNoral Thomas and Jaime Contreras said in a joint statement said the veto was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetrayal of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s workers who were promised change\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCollective bargaining is not a privilege \u8211\'20\'13 it is a right. Governor Spanberger looked workers in the eye, met with our members, affirmed her support, and made a promise. Today, she broke it,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 Edward Kelly, president of the \uc2 International Association of Fire Fighters\uc2 , also said the veto \u8220\'20\'1Cis a slap in the face to every worker who put their faith in her\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://virginiamercury.com/2026/05/15/spanberger-vetoes-bills-allowing-public-employees-to-collectively-bargain-working-condition-wages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 11,000}}}\uc2  firefighters, about 8,000 to 9,000 still do not have collective bargaining rights as their municipalities have not opted into having them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirefighters keep their word every single day on the job. It\u8217\'20\'19s a shame the governor can\u8217\'20\'19t do the same,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said.\par \par \uc2 Lee Saunders\uc2 , president of the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2  (\uc2 AFSCME\uc2 ), the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/press/releases/2026/gov-spanberger-has-broken-the-promise-she-made-to-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest union }}}\uc2 of public sector workers in the US with 1.4 million members, noted the history of \u8220\'20\'1Canti-worker extremists\u8221\'20\'1D in Virginia who have given the state the \u8220\'20\'1Creputation as one of the most anti-worker in the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Spanberger campaigned on the promise to end this historic injustice. But she has broken that promise by vetoing legislation that would have finally granted most state and local workers the freedom to collectively bargain,\u8221\'20\'1D Saunders said.\par \par \uc2 The Virginia Public Sector Labor Coalition, a group of multiple major labor unions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://myemail.constantcontact.com/Gov--Spanberger-Betrays-More-Than-Half-a-Million-Public-Service-Workers-By-Vetoing-Historic-Collective-Bargaining-Legislation.html?soid=1131580853318&aid=Z1Kas_j-8tI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echoed}}}\uc2  sentiments of betrayal and noted \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , Spanberger\u8217\'20\'19s Republican predecessor, vetoed similar legislation last year.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Spanberger deferred comment to a press release and said the governor signed into law other legislation last month that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.virginia.gov/newsroom/news-releases/2026/april-releases/name-1116694-en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expands}}}\uc2  paid family and medical leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.virginia.gov/newsroom/news-releases/2026/april-releases/name-1116004-en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raises }}}\uc2 the minimum wage and helped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.virginia.gov/newsroom/news-releases/2026/april-releases/name-1116694-en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cracks down}}}\uc2  on wage theft.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI remain committed to continuing to work with the General Assembly, unions, localities and public servants across the Commonwealth to develop a public sector collective bargaining system that works for Virginia,\u8221\'20\'1D Spanberger said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, I believe additional amendments are needed to the enrolled bill currently before me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the Jim Crow era, Virginia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressbooks.library.virginia.edu/collectivebargaining/chapter/history-of-the-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\uc2  public sector collective bargaining in 1948 in response to a group of Black workers organizing a union at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2  hospital.\par \par \uc2 Before Virginia passed a law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/virginia-governors-amended-collective-bargaining-bill-would-leave-workers-rights-optional-and-large-public-sector-pay-gap-unaddressed/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permits}}}\uc2  local governments to enact their own collective bargaining system in 2021, the state was one of only three that have blanket bans on collective bargaining for public sector workers. Even after the law passed, collective bargaining for state government workers remains illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 17 May 2026. The number of workers affected by the collective bargaining bill veto is 500,000, not 50,000 as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260515em5f004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
