\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 North America\u8217\'20\'19s largest commuter rail system shuts down as workers strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts in New York and agencies \par \uc2 779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2026\par 03:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at the \uc2 Long Island Rail Road\uc2 , serving the eastern New York metropolitan area, walked off the job on Saturday\par \par \uc2 North America\u8217\'20\'19s largest commuter rail system was shut down on Saturday after unionized workers in the New York City area went on strike.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Long Island Rail Road\uc2  that serves the city\u8217\'20\'19s eastern suburbs ceased operations on early Saturday morning after five unions representing about half its workforce walked off the job.\par \par \uc2 The two sides have been negotiating for months on a new contract, and the Trump administration had even interceded to try and broker a deal. But the unions were legally allowed to strike starting at 12.01am on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Sexton, national vice-president of the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 , said no new negotiations have been scheduled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re far apart at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D Sexton said early on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are truly sorry that we are in this situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Janno Lieber\uc2 , the \uc2 MTA\uc2  chairman, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MTANewsroom/status/2055657938983800902/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Saturday that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis was not the result we were looking for\u8221\'20\'1D but added that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe cannot and will not do a deal that shifts huge costs to our riders by forcing fare hikes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He claimed that the agency\u8217\'20\'19s last offer \u8220\'20\'1Cgave the union everything they said they wanted in terms of pay\u8221\'20\'1D and that in his opinion,it was \u8220\'20\'1Capparent that these unions always intended to strike\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The walkout, the first for the \uc2 LIRR\uc2  since a two-day strike in 1994, promises to cause headaches for some sports fans planning to see the crosstown baseball rivals the \uc2 New York Yankees\uc2  and Mets battle this weekend or to watch the \uc2 NBA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 New York Knicks\uc2  playoff run at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  in Manhattan. Both sports venues have dedicated LIRR stops.\par \par \uc2 If the shutdown continues past the weekend, the roughly 250,000 people who ride the system to and from work each weekday will be forced to find alternative routes into New York City from its Long Island suburbs.\par \par \uc2 For many, that likely means navigating the region\u8217\'20\'19s notoriously congested roads.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovKathyHochul/status/2055507104845222155/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2 on Saturday morning that the unions\u8217\'20\'19 demands could \u8220\'20\'1Craise fares as much at 8%, pit workers against one another and risk tax hikes for Long Islanders\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stand with the \uc2 LIRR\uc2  riders and will fight to preserve the long-term stability of the \uc2 MTA\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul, who is up for re-election this year, said. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe a deal can be done and I urge both the \uc2 MTA\uc2  and these unions to return to the table and bargain non-stop until a deal is reached.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gil Lang, the general chair of the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s LIRR general committe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blet.org/news/blet-members-on-strike-at-long-island-rail-road/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2 on Saturday: \u8220\'20\'1CTo every LIRR passenger whose trip is disrupted, know that the \uc2 MTA\uc2  left us no choice but to strike.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MTA\uc2  has said it will provide free limited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mta.info/article/lirr-strike-may-2026"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shuttle buses}}}\uc2  on weekdays to New York City subway stations, but that contingency plan wasn\u8217\'20\'19t envisioned to handle all the riders the system normally carries on a workday. The \uc2 MTA\uc2  is also encouraging those who can to work from home and avoid nonessential travel.\par \par \uc2 The most recent contract talks have stalled on the question of worker\u8217\'20\'19s salaries and health care premiums.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MTA\uc2  has said the unions\u8217\'20\'19 initial demands would have led to fare increases and affected contract negotiations with other unionized workers.\par \par \uc2 The unions, which represent locomotive engineers, machinists, signalmen and other train workers, have said more substantial raises were warranted to help workers keep up with inflation and rising living costs.\par \par \uc2 But Gerard Bringmann, chair of the LIRR ommuter Council, a rider advocacy group, said in a statement that if the unions get the pay increases they are looking for, \u8220\'20\'1Cit will come at the expense of our riders who will see next year\u8217\'20\'19s 4% fare increase doubled to 8%\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike the union workers, we too are burdened by the increase in the cost of living here on Long Island\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 With Hochul, a Democrat, facing re-election later this year, the pressure might be on the \uc2 MTA\uc2  to strike a deal to end the shutdown, said William Dwyer, a labor relations expert at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2  in New Jersey, where commuter rail workers staged a three-day strike last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s up for re-election, and Long Island is a critical vote for her,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo if there\u8217\'20\'19s a significant fare hike, that does not bode well for her on election day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260517em5h000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
