\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  workers in UK vote to unionize amid deal with US military\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Speri \par \uc2 1,139 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2026\par 21:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 33\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: Worker pointed to Iran war and Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  feud as indications the department is \u8216\'20\'18not a responsible partner\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Workers developing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/google"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Google}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/technology+artificialintelligenceai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 artificial intelligence}}}\uc2  products in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK}}}\uc2  have voted to unionize, in part out of concerns about a deal between the company and the US military that was announced last week.\par \par \uc2 In a letter slated to go to management on Tuesday and shared exclusively with the Guardian, workers at Google {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/deepmind"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeepMind}}}\uc2 , the company\u8217\'20\'19s AI research laboratory, requested recognition of the \uc2 Communication Workers Union\uc2  and \uc2 Unite the Union\uc2  as joint representatives of the lab\u8217\'20\'19s UK-based staff.\par \par \uc2 DeepMind\u8217\'20\'19s UK workers voted to unionize in April. One of the workers said they were particularly driven by reports that \uc2 Google\uc2  was close to reaching a deal with the defense department and pointed to the US\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccapricious Iran war\u8221\'20\'1D and the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/mar/05/trump-anthropic-ai-pentagon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feud with Anthropic}}}\uc2  as indications that the department is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a responsible partner\u8221\'20\'1D. The deal was ultimately announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have joined the union due to concerns about AI being used to empower authoritarianism, whether through military or surveillance applications, both foreign and domestic,\u8221\'20\'1D added the worker, who requested anonymity because of fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CBy unionizing, we are taking the traditional route for workers to organize and have a say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another worker, who also requested anonymity, said that many at the company had struggled with what they had come to view as their complicity in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. The company provided the Israeli military with increased access to its AI tools from the early days of the war in Gaza, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/01/21/google-ai-israel-war-hamas-attack-gaza/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  last year, and in 2021, it signed, along with \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , a $1.2bn cloud-computing contract with the Israeli government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur technology helped the \uc2 IDF\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said the second UK worker, referring to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military. \u8220\'20\'1CI want AI to benefit humanity, not to facilitate a genocide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Google\uc2  wrote in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Google UK\uc2  recently received a letter from Unite and the Communications Workers Union requesting recognition for Google DeepMind UK employees. We have always valued constructive dialogue with employees and we\u8217\'20\'19ll remain focused on creating a positive and successful workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D A second spokesperson added that the company was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot aware of any vote to officially unionise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Concerns by \uc2 Google\uc2  workers and investors have been mounting for years but have particularly escalated after the company last year dropped a pledge not to develop militarized AI. That development was a driving motivation for \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  workers\u8217\'20\'19 union in the UK, two of them said. While small groups of \uc2 Google\uc2  employees have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/jan/04/more-than-200-us-google-employees-form-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unionized}}}\uc2  in the US before, the UK workers are the first in a \u8220\'20\'1Cfrontier\u8221\'20\'1D AI lab to seek union recognition, they said. \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  is headquartered in London but has about a dozen offices across North America and Europe. At least 1,000 workers will be represented if the company recognizes the union, according to union officials.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Pentagon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/01/pentagon-us-military-pairs-with-spacex-google-openai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  it had reached agreements with seven leading AI companies, \uc2 Google\uc2  among them. Others included \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , Reflection, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon Web Services\uc2 . \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 , whose technology is in wide use by the US military but which has sparred with the Pentagon over future contracts, was notably absent from the group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese agreements accelerate the transformation toward establishing the United States military as an AI-first fighting force and will strengthen our warfighters\u8217\'20\'19 ability to maintain decision superiority across all domains of warfare,\u8221\'20\'1D the defense department officials said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has pushed AI companies to make their tools available on classified networks without the standard restrictions they apply to users. \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s contract with the Pentagon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/28/google-classified-ai-deal-pentagon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  includes language stating: \u8220\'20\'1CThe parties agree that the AI System is not intended for, and should not be used for, domestic mass surveillance or autonomous weapons (including target selection) without appropriate human oversight and control.\u8221\'20\'1D But that language is non-binding, and the agreement also says \uc2 Google\uc2  has no right to control or veto \u8220\'20\'1Clawful\u8221\'20\'1D government operational decision-making.\par \par \uc2 Workers who voted to join the union said they did so to raise pressure on \uc2 Google\uc2  to meet demands {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://utaw.tech/campaigns/google"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already made}}}\uc2  by other employees at the company, including that it commit not to develop technology \u8220\'20\'1Cwhose primary purpose is to cause harm or injury to people\u8221\'20\'1D, establish an independent ethics oversight body, and grant workers the individual right to refuse to contribute to projects on moral grounds. Should the company refuse, they said, they are considering protests and \u8220\'20\'1Cresearch strikes\u8221\'20\'1D, during which staff abstain from work expected to significantly improve core products such as Gemini, \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s AI bot, while avoiding detection by continuing to perform less significant updates.\par \par \uc2 Workers across Google have been increasingly vocal about their opposition to militarized applications of their technology. Last week, amid reports of the pending deal, more than 600 Google employees signed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.bwbx.io/documents/users/iqjWHBFdfxIU/riE1wPuvIT5M/v0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open letter}}}\uc2  to CEO, Sundar Pichai, demanding the company not make its AI systems available for classified use.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to see AI benefit humanity; not to see it being used in inhumane or extremely harmful ways,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CMaking the wrong call right now would cause irreparable damage to Google\u8217\'20\'19s reputation, business, and role in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tech workers have increasingly challenged management over the use of the technology they have helped develop. In 2024, Google {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/27/google-project-nimbus-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  50 workers who had protested against Project Nimbus, the 2021 contract with the Israeli government. At Microsoft, which the Guardian revealed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/06/microsoft-israeli-military-palestinian-phone-calls-cloud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supplied}}}\uc2  Israel with cloud storage used in the mass surveillance of Palestinians, workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/aug/19/microsoft-workers-protest-washington-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occupied}}}\uc2  a company campus with signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CNo Labor for Genocide\u8221\'20\'1D. (The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/25/microsoft-blocks-israels-use-of-its-technology-in-mass-surveillance-of-palestinians"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminated}}}\uc2  the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s access to that technology after the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s reporting.)\par \par \uc2 Investors have also raised concerns. A coalition of shareholders who own about $2.2bn of Alphabet\u8217\'20\'19s \u8203\'20\'0Bshares wrote a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5d0cee8d37a63200017a0906/t/69efc23f8e44177005f01985/1777320511980/Alphabet+2026+Investor+Letter+Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to Google\u8217\'20\'19s parent company last week demanding a meeting and greater transparency about Google Cloud and AI deployments in \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-risk\u8221\'20\'1D contexts. They cited concerns about the company providing services to US immigration \u8288\'20\'60authorities, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/29/google-amazon-israel-contract-secret-code"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project Nimbus}}}\uc2 , and raised questions about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe effectiveness of policy guardrails, internal escalation processes, and Board oversight of AI deployments in conflict-affected or security-sensitive environments\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Google also dealt with widespread employee protests over a military contract known as Project Maven, in which the company agreed to build AI products for the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of drone footage. In response to the backlash, the company did not renew the contract in 2019 and published a set of principles for its work on AI that included the pledge, now dropped, not to design AI for weapons. Palantir took over Project Maven, which continues today.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260505em5500105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
