\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump administration investigates \uc2 Smith College\uc2  for admitting transgender women\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 579 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2026\par 13:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Civil rights inquiry claims policy may breach Title IX as administration escalates attacks on trans rightsSign up for the Breaking News US newsletter email\par \par \uc2 The US education department is investigating one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest women\u8217\'20\'19s colleges over its admittance of transgender women in another escalation of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attacks on trans people.\par \par \uc2 The department\u8217\'20\'19s office of civil rights announced the investigation on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-release/us-department-of-education-opens-title-ix-investigation-all-womens-smith-college-admitting-men"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a press release}}}\uc2 , saying the Massachusetts college could be violating federal law by \u8220\'20\'1Callowing biological males into women\u8217\'20\'19s intimate spaces\u8221\'20\'1D, including dorms, bathrooms, locker rooms and sports teams.\par \par \uc2 Title IX, the federal law that seeks to prevent sex-based discrimination in education and extracurriculars, includes an exemption for all-male or all-female colleges. But, the department said, that applies only to \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological sex difference, not subjective gender identity\u8221\'20\'1D. Admitting transgender students would mean the college no longer qualifies as single sex.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn all-women\u8217\'20\'19s college loses all meaning if it is admitting biological males,\u8221\'20\'1D assistant secretary for civil rights, Kimberly Richey, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAllowing biological males into spaces designed for women raises serious concerns about privacy, fairness, and compliance under federal law. The Trump Administration will continue to uphold the law and fight to restore common sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s admission policy allows for \u8220\'20\'1Cany applicants who self-identify as women\u8221\'20\'1D, including \u8220\'20\'1Ccis, trans and nonbinary women\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the college\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smith.edu/admission-aid/apply-smith/first-year-applicants#who-is-eligible-to-apply-to-smith?-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2 . The college opened in 1875 and counts among its alumni multiple first ladies, elected officials and civic leaders.\par \par \uc2 The investigation comes as the Trump administration seeks to drive transgender people out of public spaces. The administration has sought to end transgender participation in sports, including filing lawsuits against states that allow such participation, and is seeking to ban access to gender-affirming medical care. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  banned trans people from joining the military and required passports to match biological sex at birth.\par \par \uc2 The college said in a statement that it has received notice of the Title IX investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe College is fully committed to its institutional values, including compliance with civil rights laws,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe College does not comment on pending government investigations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A rightwing education group, Defending Education, filed a complaint in June 2025 to the education department\u8217\'20\'19s office of civil rights against Smith, urging the department to investigate the college. The group goes after schools and teachers unions nationwide over diversity policies and perceived biases, saying it wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight indoctrination in classrooms and on campus\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIronically, in what appears to be yet another exercise in sex discrimination, Smith admits natal men who identify as women but does not admit natal women who identify as men,\u8221\'20\'1D Defending Education wrote in its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://defendinged.org/complaints/ocr-complaint-smith-college/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The college affirmed in 2015 that its policy would include admitting transgender women, which came after a year of studying the issue and conferring with students and alumni.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe mission of \uc2 Smith College\uc2  is to educate women of promise for lives of distinction. In the years since Smith\u8217\'20\'19s founding, concepts of female identity have evolved. Smith alumnae have been leaders in the movement to afford women greater freedoms of aspiration and self-expression,\u8221\'20\'1D the college\u8217\'20\'19s leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smith.edu/president-kathleen-mccartney/letters/2014-15/admission-policy-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote at the time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Smith College{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thesophian.com/staying-in-the-game-losing-teammates-smith-athletes-respond-to-ncaa-rule-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it would follow a new policy from the \uc2 National Collegiate Athletic Association\uc2  on transgender participation in athletics, which prohibits transgender women from playing in women\u8217\'20\'19s sports.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260505em55003ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
