\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 CEO pay soared in 2025, 20 times faster than workers\u8217\'20\'19 pay\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 493 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2026\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Analysis finds real wages fell 12% since 2019, with inequality widening in the US beyond global levels\par \par \uc2 CEO pay increased 20 times faster than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/pay+work-and-careers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worker pay}}}\uc2  around the world in 2025, according to a new{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oxfamamerica.org/press/top-global-ceo-pay-increased-20-times-faster-than-workers-pay-in-2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  analysis}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  and the \uc2 International Trade Union Confederation\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest trade union federation.\par \par \uc2 When adjusted for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation}}}\uc2 , global worker pay declined 12% between 2019 and 2025, the equivalent of 108 days of free work during that time period. In comparison, CEO compensation increased by 54% between 2019 and 2025.\par \par \uc2 The average CEO received $8.4m in total compensation in 2025 compared to $7.6m in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The analysis also found billionaires were paid $2,500 a second in dividends in 2025, according to the investment portfolios of more than 1,000 billionaires. For every two hours in the 2025, the average billionaire received more in dividends than the average worker earned in annual pay.\par \par \uc2 The wealth of billionaires has reached record highs in 2026, with the wealthiest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/national-news/articles/2026-03-10/breaking-down-the-forbes-worlds-billionaire-list#:~:text=The%20list%20is%20a%20compilation,the%20brain%20implant%20startup%20Neuralink."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaining $4tn}}}\uc2  over the past 12 months, a 13.2% increase from 2025.\par \par \uc2 Inequality in the US was worse than the global average, with CEO pay increasing 20.4 times faster than worker pay in 2025.\par \par \uc2 For 384 CEOs in the S&P 500 where CEO compensation data was available, pay increased by 25% from 2024 to 2025, while average hourly earnings for workers at private companies increased 1.3% in the same period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis analysis exposes the billionaire coup against democracy and its costs for working people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Luc Triangle, general secretary of the \uc2 International Trade Union Confederation\uc2 , in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CCompanies promise us a virtuous cycle, but what we see is a vicious cycle led by mega corporations \u8211\'20\'13 they undermine collective bargaining and social dialogue while billionaire CEOs capture the wealth created by productivity gains.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The top-paying 1,500 corporations across 33 countries that report CEO compensation for 2025 were covered under the analysis. Among these corporations, researchers found a 16% gender pay gap, noting women at these companies essentially work for free after 4 November every year.\par \par \uc2 The top 10 highest paid CEOs received more than $1bn collectively last year, with four corporations \u8211\'20\'13 Blackstone, \uc2 Broadcom\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/microsoft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Microsoft}}}\uc2  paying their CEOs more than $100m in 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t continue to let a handful of super-rich people siphon off the rewards of work that belong to millions. Governments must cap CEO pay, fairly tax the super-rich and ensure minimum wages at the very least keep pace with inflation and ensure a dignified living,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Amitabh Behar\uc2 , executive director of \uc2 Oxfam International\uc2 , in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese measures can do far more than redistribute income; they can create economies that reward work, invest in communities and hold powerful interests accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D added Behar. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how we turn a system rigged for the few into one that works for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260501em510020d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
