\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s probably good\u8217\'20\'19: Donald Trump Jr gets muted endorsement from his father for The Apprentice reboot\b0\par\par\uc2 Sian Cain \par \uc2 683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2026\par 05:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Speculative reports say \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is considering relaunching the reality show once hosted by the US president, with his eldest son floated as a possible hostGet our weekend culture and lifestyle email\par \par \uc2 Amid speculative reports that Donald Trump Jr is being considered by \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to lead a reboot of The Apprentice, he\u8217\'20\'19s already received a slightly muted endorsement from the reality show\u8217\'20\'19s former host: his father.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/media/amazon-discusses-apprentice-rebootwith-don-jr-as-a-potential-host-fe09e885?st=wSRHZ7&reflink=article_imessage_share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal reported on Wednesday}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was considering rebooting The Apprentice, which was hosted by the now US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  between 2004 and 2015, for its streaming service Prime Video.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal cited anonymous sources who said Amazon MGM Studios head \uc2 Mike Hopkins\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbegan talking about the reboot idea internally early last year, around the time Trump was being sworn in for his second term, according to some of the people familiar with the talks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said in a statement that a reboot was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot in active development\u8221\'20\'1D, but confirmed to Variety that \u8220\'20\'1Cpreliminary internal discussions about what\u8217\'20\'19s next for The Apprentice\u8221\'20\'1D had begun since the media company acquired \uc2 MGM\uc2 , and with it The Apprentice franchise, in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny reporting on details of the show or names of potential hosts would be purely speculative,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Hollywood Reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/politics-news/donald-trump-jr-the-apprentice-reboot-host-amazon-1236581037/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited a source}}}\uc2  close to Trump Jr, who said he had learned about his potential new role from the media.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/newsletters/2019/oct/18/saved-for-later-sign-up-for-guardian-australias-culture-and-lifestyle-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for the fun stuff with our rundown of must-reads, pop culture and tips for the weekend, every Saturday morning}}}\par \par \uc2 But at an Oval Office executive order signing event on Thursday, Trump was asked about the reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been hearing it,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/cnMsM1HeSXA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo we\u8217\'20\'19ll see what happens. He\u8217\'20\'19s good. He\u8217\'20\'19s a good guy. He\u8217\'20\'19s probably good. He\u8217\'20\'19s got a little charisma going.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Amazon\uc2  reboots The Apprentice with a Trump at the helm, it would be a sign that the company is determined to cement a relationship with the family after it released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/feb/09/melania-drops-67-at-us-box-office-as-rotten-tomatoes-defends-record-breaking-audience-scores"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania}}}\uc2 , Brett Ratner\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/jan/30/melania-review-trump-film-is-a-gilded-trash-remake-of-the-zone-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critically panned documentary}}}\uc2  about the first lady. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  paid $40m for the rights to the film \u8211\'20\'13 plus an as-yet unaired docu series \u8211\'20\'13 $26m higher than the offer from the second highest bidder, \uc2 Disney\uc2 . \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spent a further $35m on marketing Melania, which made just $16m at the box office \u8211\'20\'13 leading some questioning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/jan/28/melania-trump-documentary-amazon-release"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s eye-watering $75m spend was really the price of ingratiating itself with Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Starting in 2004, The Apprentice saw business contestants compete in tasks such as selling products and negotiating deals, with the ultimate prize being a job within Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business empire. Each episode saw Trump grill the players before delivering his catchphrase: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Apprentice was hugely successful and spawned several spin-offs in the US and internationally. Trump hosted the show until 2015 when he left to run for office, but remained involved as an executive producer. Arnold Schwarzenegger then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2017/jan/03/new-celebrity-apprentice-schwarzenegger-premiere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became host of The New Celebrity Apprentice}}}\uc2  in 2017, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/mar/03/arnold-schwarzenegger-quits-celebrity-apprentice-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left after one season as Trump repeatedly criticised him on social media}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Trump being involved in the show people have a bad taste and don\u8217\'20\'19t want to participate as a spectator or as a sponsor or in any other way support the show,\u8221\'20\'1D Schwarzenegger told Empire in 2017. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a very divisive period now and I think this show got caught up in all that division.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump responded by claiming Schwarzenegger \u8220\'20\'1Cwas fired by his bad (pathetic) ratings, not by me. Sad end to great show.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Two years ago, Trump revealed he had already endorsed one of his children to be his successor on The Apprentice \u8211\'20\'13 but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t Trump Jr.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI said, \u8216\'20\'18The best person to hire would be \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 ,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Ramin Setoodeh, in an interview for his book Apprentice in Wonderland. \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t press it. But I felt Ivanka would have been by far the best person you could hire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260501em51000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
