\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It feels like a betrayal\u8217\'20\'19: anger as \uc2 Apple\uc2  to close its first unionized store in the US\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2026\par 17:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tech giant accused of \u8216\'20\'18cynical attempt to bust the union\u8217\'20\'19 in decision to shutter location in Towson, Maryland\par \par \uc2 Workers at the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/apple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Apple}}}\uc2  store to unionize in the US are pushing back against the company\u8217\'20\'19s decision to shut it down by June, alleging that \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision is rooted in \u8220\'20\'1Ca cynical attempt to bust the union\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the union filed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goiam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Charge-Apr-27-26.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair labor practice charge}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Apple\uc2 , alleging unionized employees at the store in Towson, Maryland, are being denied transfer rights and other rights compared with workers at non-unionized stores. The union is also alleging retaliation for being unionized.\par \par \uc2 According to the union, \uc2 Apple\uc2  claims the collective bargaining agreement prevents relocation, a claim the union says is \u8220\'20\'1Csimply false, and raises serious concerns that this closure is a cynical attempt to bust the union\u8221\'20\'1D, the union said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goiam.org/news/imail/iam-union-statement-on-apples-decision-to-close-first-unionized-apple-retail-store/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  denied the claims in the charge. \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly disagree with the claims made, and we will continue to abide by the agreement that was negotiated and agreed with the union. We look forward to presenting all of the facts to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  [\uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 ],\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said in an email.\par \par \uc2 The union is calling on \uc2 Apple\uc2  to reverse the closure decision and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/letters/tell-apple-to-keep-the-towson-md-apple-store-open"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on customers}}}\uc2  to support its effort. It has also urged people to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/petitions/tell-apple-to-respect-its-unionized-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contact }}}\uc2 the company\u8217\'20\'19s board of directors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about whether workers are treated fairly under the law or punished for exercising their rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Brian Bryant, the international president of the \uc2 IAM union\uc2 , said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Apple\uc2  is denying union-represented workers the same opportunities it is giving to others \u8211\'20\'13 and doing so because these workers chose to organize. That is discrimination, and it is exactly what federal labor law is designed to prevent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nearly 90 workers at the store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/19/apple-workers-vote-to-join-union-a-first-for-the-tech-giant-in-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  their union election in June 2022 to join the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers Coalition of Organized Retail Employees (IAM Core).\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the union election, \uc2 Eric Brown\uc2 , an \uc2 Apple\uc2  store employee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/apple-store-union-election-towson-maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re trying to make changes to actually have a right to a say in our workplace conditions, in how we\u8217\'20\'19re treated, with pay and policy changes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers faced delays in bargaining for a first union contract with \uc2 Apple\uc2 , which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/news/releases/unionized-workers-call-apple-uphold-commitments-shareholders-and-include-organized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  unionization and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/may/15/apple-union-workers-strike-vote-bargaining-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled}}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  alleging labor law violations. A first union contract was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmar2news.com/local/apple-update-towson-store-union-wins-historic-deal#:~:text=The%20members%20of%20the%20IAMCORE%20tech%20union,starting%20pay%20for%2080%25%20of%20job%20classifications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached}}}\uc2  in August 2024.\par \par \uc2 Now Brown and his co-workers are facing layoffs due to the store closure and being forced to reapply for a position with the company elsewhere rather than be transferred.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis job is more than a job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brown in a press conference about the store closure. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a family to us. There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason why, on your last day, we clap you out and wish you a fond farewell, and we say that we\u8217\'20\'19re losing a family. There are people that we built real relationships with, not just showing up to work every day and working side by side. I met my partner there, and we\u8217\'20\'19re having another child next month. So this is a huge impact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brown said the tactic of shutting down a store to avoid dealing with a union was a concern at the bargaining table and said the union had ensured transfer protections were in place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like a betrayal,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CFinancially, we were doing fine. Foot traffic, we\u8217\'20\'19re doing fine. So there\u8217\'20\'19s no other reason to shut us down then to basically bust up the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we went in there and negotiated that if you open up a store within 50 miles, that that would essentially be us moving, because we didn\u8217\'20\'19t want them to say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, you know, there\u8217\'20\'19s a downtown Baltimore store. No need for the Towson store. Get out of here.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Courtney Jenkins, president of the Metropolitan Baltimore AFL-CIO, criticized the treatment of the unionized workers and the store closure, noting the \uc2 Apple\uc2  store in Towson is the only local store accessible by public transit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about jobs. It\u8217\'20\'19s about equity, it\u8217\'20\'19s about access, and it\u8217\'20\'19s about whether one of the wealthiest corporations in human history is willing to turn this back on both,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jenkins. \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is clear. Relocation, not resignation. Our sisters and brothers in the machinists\u8217\'20\'19 union deserve to keep their jobs, and our community deserves to keep this valuable resource.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Apple\uc2  spokesperson claimed the collective bargaining agreement prohibits transfer rights offered to other stores, claiming the transfer rights are limited if \uc2 Apple\uc2  opens a new store within 50 miles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the departure of several retailers and declining conditions at Trumbull Mall, the Shops at North County, and Towson Town Center, we\u8217\'20\'19ve made the difficult decision to close our stores at these locations. Our team members at Trumbull and North County will continue their roles at nearby \uc2 Apple\uc2  retail stores,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CTowson employees will be eligible to apply for open roles at Apple in accordance with the collective bargaining agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260428em4s0048t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
