\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The \u8216\'20\'18wizards\u8217\'20\'19 behind the online version of Magic: the Gathering are unionizing\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 651 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2026\par 15:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Developers at the studio \uc2 Wizards of the Coast\uc2  cited AI and layoff protections as some issues driving unionization effort\par \par \uc2 Magic: the Gathering is casting lots for a union. Game developers at the popular digital and tabletop studio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://company.wizards.com/en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wizards of the Coast}}}\uc2 , a subsidiary of \uc2 Hasbro\uc2  that develops online versions of the popular card game are seeking to join the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The workers announced their intent to unionize on Monday to join the \uc2 CWA\uc2 , which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/news/releases/video-game-workers-launch-industry-wide-union-communications-workers-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organized thousands}}}\uc2  of workers in the tech and video game industry in recent years, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/news/releases/quality-assurance-workers-activision-establish-largest-certified-union-us-video-game#:~:text=Quality%20Assurance%20Workers%20at%20Activision,America%20%7C%20Communications%20Workers%20of%20America"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest certified union}}}\uc2  in the US video game industry in 2024 representing 600 quality assurance workers at \uc2 Activision\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than 100 game designers, programmers, producers, artists and other workers at the studio will be represented by the bargaining unit, with workers stating they have a supermajority of support. They are requesting voluntary recognition, but have filed for a union election at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  as well, offering to withdraw the petition if they are voluntarily recognized by 1 May.\par \par \uc2 Workers cited layoff protections, remote work protections, generative AI protections for workers, sustainable workloads and defined career progressions as some of the issues driving the unionization effort.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Wizards of the Coast\uc2  studio, based in Renton, Washington, has engaged in several layoffs in recent years, including{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.geekwire.com/2025/wizards-of-the-coast-reportedly-lays-off-staff-working-on-virtual-tabletop-sigil/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  about 30 employees laid off}}}\uc2  in March 2025 and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.geekwire.com/2023/new-round-of-layoffs-at-hasbro-impacts-wizards-of-the-coast-read-ceos-memo-to-staff/?fbclid=IwY2xjawRYqodleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETFQakV2ZlBXbWFGZFhvUEI2c3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHlCiDFkv43coVeRtsS0Q3fazjFYuLL3Otl5QqscCcsnYpdA-XipjDIRsc-dD_aem_8Xm2Vx9x5xuvl7rMrNI3dg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant round of layoffs}}}\uc2  affecting 1,100 workers across \uc2 Hasbro\uc2  in December 2023.\par \par \uc2 Rogue Kessler, a designer at the studio, explained the unionization effort at the studio ramped up in response to a recent return to office mandate, where workers who work remotely are being told they must relocate to Washington or lose their jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have people living all over the country, and many of those folks were hired remotely in the first place. They\u8217\'20\'19ve never been to Washington. They\u8217\'20\'19ve never lived here, and now they\u8217\'20\'19re being told all of a sudden that they need to move to Seattle, uproot their families, sell their homes and relocate here in two years or lose their job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kessler. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had a few round rounds of layoffs here at \uc2 Hasbro\uc2  and Wizards, and so that\u8217\'20\'19s something that has a lot of us very spooked as well. We want to see some robust protections there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Valentine Powell, a software engineer at the studio, said management hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been responsive in trying to address these issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey just aren\u8217\'20\'19t working with the people who are on the ground level and so unionization is our best effort to try and rectify that,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said.\par \par \uc2 They added the union was also pushing for protections and guardrails for how artificial intelligence is used, arguing: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to the product that we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to make, I believe that AI has consistently shown worse results. It takes longer and it just sort of harms the end product.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Powell warned if initiatives like the return to office mandate are forced upon workers at the studio, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to result in losing several skilled artists, developers and workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I would like to say to our players is the people who make your game love making it. The co-workers that I\u8217\'20\'19ve had here are some of the most dedicated to trying to make a really, really outstanding game and trying to make their players happy and keep those lines of communication open. And it\u8217\'20\'19s those people that we\u8217\'20\'19re very likely to lose if some of the initiatives go forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said. \u8220\'20\'1CI really believe unionization is the only thing that\u8217\'20\'19s going to save the games industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the public announcement of the unionization effort, \uc2 Wizards of the Coast\uc2  and \uc2 Hasbro\uc2  were contacted for comment, but they did not immediately respond.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260427em4r003uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
