\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Staff decry \u8216\'20\'18constant turbulence\u8217\'20\'19 under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s labor secretary, as she blames \u8216\'20\'18deep state\u8217\'20\'19 in resignation\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 815 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2026\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lori Chavez-DeRemer resigned amid allegations of an affair and steering grants to politically connected figures\par \par \uc2 The secretary of the Department of Labor, Lori Chavez-DeRemer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/20/trump-labor-secretary-lori-chavez-deremer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  this week after several controversies surrounding her brief tenure at the helm of the agency. But labor officials say even though her troubled reign is over, the US labor authority remains in a state of \u8220\'20\'1Cconstant turbulence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/20/trump-labor-secretary-lori-chavez-deremer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under investigation}}}\uc2  over claims she had an affair with a subordinate and allegedly misused travel funds, and that her aides allegedly steered grants to politically connected figures. Her husband was banned from the agency\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters over allegations of sexual assault by at least two staffers.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DXYFKg4DEki/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on Instagram}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/lchavezderemer/status/2046391020791722218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2  announcing her resignation, Chavez-DeRemer denied the allegations and claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe allegations against me, my family, and my team have been peddled by high-ranked deep state actors who have been coordinating with the one-sided news media and continue to undermine President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mission\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer is the latest official in the Trump administration to leave their leadership role in recent weeks, following the US attorney general, Pam Bondi, and the homeland security secretary, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Omar Algeciras, vice-president of \uc2 AFGE\uc2  Local 2391, which represents workers at the Department of Labor, where Algeciras also works, criticized Chavez-DeRemer\u8217\'20\'19s statement on her resignation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLabeling these workers as \u8216\'20\'18deep state\u8217\'20\'19 dismisses the mission and the people who carry it out every day,\u8221\'20\'1D said Algeciras.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCareer staff have kept this agency moving despite constant turbulence. As a union leader, I see first-hand how employees continue to deliver for workers across the country under difficult conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis resignation creates an opening, but without stable leadership, respect for the workforce and a clear commitment to the mission, the challenges facing the department will continue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He claimed Chavez-DeRemer never signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/OASAM/legacy/files/2017-Policy-Statement-on-Harassing-Conduct-in-the-Workplace.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassment policy statement}}}\uc2  for the agency, despite it being a requirement. The Department of Labor did not respond for comment on this allegation.\par \par \uc2 Under Chavez-DeRemer, the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  shed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/03/mass-resignations-at-labor-department-threaten-workers-in-us-and-overseas-warn-staff-as-more-cuts-loom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 20%}}}\uc2  of its workforce due to buyouts, resignations and firings. The agency also eliminated millions of dollars in international grants.\par \par \uc2 Last year, several workers at the agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/16/trump-administration-labor-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  that morale had \u8220\'20\'1Cplummeted\u8221\'20\'1D amid the cuts, deregulatory efforts, and threats to and intimidation of staff, including a memo threatening workers for speaking to the media.\par \par \uc2 In January 2026, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/14/union-leaders-trump-administration-white-supremacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian spoke with union leaders}}}\uc2  who criticized the Department of Labor\u8217\'20\'19s shift on social media to posts that they said echoed Nazi rhetoric. After the criticisms, the social media staffer at the agency was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/11/us/politics/trump-administration-social-media-homeland-security.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Labor experts and leaders also criticized Chavez-DeRemer\u8217\'20\'19s leadership at the labor department, where she oversaw significant cuts to the agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce and rollbacks of worker protections and regulations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSecretary Lori Chavez-DeRemer sat by as her department\u8217\'20\'19s budget was slashed, as worker protections for other agencies were dismantled, supported the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to annihilate the federal workforces\u8217\'20\'19 unions and placed a three-story portrait of the president on the [labor department] building,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cathy Creighton, director of the Cornell University School of Industrial and Labor Relations\u8217\'20\'19 Buffalo Co-Lab, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Creighton cited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/department-of-labor-announces-deregulatory-agenda-to-weaken-wage-standards-workplace-safety-and-other-protections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deregulation agenda}}}\uc2  announced by the agency in July 2025 that included rescission of overtime and minimum wage protections for homecare and domestic workers, rolling back farm worker labor protections, and withdrawing a rule that would prevent employers from paying workers with disabilities a sub-minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Labor caucus co-chairs \uc2 Donald Norcross\uc2 , Mark Pocan, Steven Horsford and \uc2 Debbie Dingell\uc2  issued a joint statement strongly criticizing Chavez-Deremer\u8217\'20\'19s leadership at the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSecretary Chavez-DeRemer advanced the administration\u8217\'20\'19s anti-worker agenda, facing removal only for the scandals she was involved in, and not the decisions she made that reduced oversight of workplace safety and enforcement of labor laws, leaving workers more vulnerable to injury, wage theft and exploitation,\u8221\'20\'1D said the congressional members in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CHer tenure leaves workers with less protections and greater economic insecurity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer was nominated with strong support from the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , with the union\u8217\'20\'19s president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/11/19/congress/obriens-pick-for-labor-secretary-00190495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing }}}\uc2 her to be nominated to the position shortly after Trump won the 2024 election in November. Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.livenowfox.com/video/1552349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 photographed}}}\uc2  with Chavez-DeRemer and O\u8217\'20\'19Brien during the announcement of the nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are grateful to President Trump for putting American workers first by nominating Representative Chavez-DeRemer to this important role,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2025/02/teamsters-strongly-support-lori-chavez-deremer-for-labor-secretary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  in February 2025.\par \par \uc2 The Teamsters did not respond to multiple requests for comment on Chavez-DeRemer\u8217\'20\'19s resignation.\par \par \uc2 The US Department of Labor did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260425em4p001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
