\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Meta\uc2  cut thousands of staff as they bet big on AI\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,143 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2026\par 12:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2  to lay off 10% of its staff and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  to offer retirement to 7% of US workforce. Plus, Iron Maiden at 50Don\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/23/meta-microsoft-tech-ai-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cutting thousands of employees}}}\uc2  as they bet big on AI and executives claim that the technology is meeting productivity needs.\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2  told staff on Thursday that on 20 May it would cut 10% of its personnel \u8211\'20\'13 just under 8,000 employees \u8211\'20\'13 to boost efficiency, part of a layoff plan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/mar/13/meta-layoffs-ai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made months ago}}}\uc2 . The company is also closing about 6,000 open roles. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  announced to employees, for the first time, that it would offer voluntary retirement to about 7% of its US workforce of roughly 125,000.\par \par \uc2 * What have they said about AI? \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  said in January that AI was making some hiring unnecessary. \uc2 Mustafa Suleyman\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s AI chief, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/microsoft-ai-boss-says-ai-134000462.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in February that he believed AI would be able to replace most white-collar work within the next 12 to 18 months.\par \par \uc2 * How many tech layoffs have there been in 2026? In four months, more than 92,000 employees in the industry have lost their jobs, according to the tracker Layoffs.fyi. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/06/tech-layoffs-ai-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 But some experts believe companies}}}\uc2  may be \u8220\'20\'1CAI washing\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 using it as cover for a slowing labor market and demand or rising costs.\par \par \uc2 Trump claims US has total control over strait of Hormuz after Iran seizes two container ships\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/trump-claims-us-has-total-control-over-strait-of-hormuz-as-iran-seizes-two-container-ships"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed the US has \u8220\'20\'1Ctotal control over the strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , a statement that appeared dubious in light of Iran seizing two container ships and a US report warning it could take six months to clear the strait of mines.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments on Thursday came after US special forces boarded a stateless oil tanker in the Indian Ocean, which the Pentagon claimed was carrying Iranian crude oil. The military operation took place hours after Iran\u8217\'20\'19s seizure of the two container ships, as both sides continued to impose competing blockades on the strait.\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed Iran\u8217\'20\'19s leadership was so weakened by internal conflict that it was unclear who was in charge. He also told reporters on Thursday that a ceasefire between Israel and Lebanon would be extended by three weeks. \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  has not been a participant in the talks and bouts of fighting have continued throughout the most recent truce.\par \par \uc2 * What about a peace deal with Iran? When asked how long he would wait for a long-term deal with Iran, he replied: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t rush me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Follow developments in this fast-moving story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/24/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-strait-israel-lebanon-truce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on our live blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Israeli killing of Lebanese journalist draws international condemnation\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/23/lebanon-journalist-amal-khalil-israel-death-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominent Lebanese journalist Amal Khalil}}}\uc2  in a double-tap strike has been condemned internationally.\par \par \uc2 Khalil was killed in what colleagues described as a sustained attack by Israeli forces, with rescuers who attempted to dig her out of the rubble also targeted and prevented from providing life-saving aid. Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister described the attack as a war crime.\par \par \uc2 The journalist, who was buried on Thursday, had previously spoken of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1427131/amal-khalil-lebanese-journalist-receives-israeli-death-threat-urging-her-to-leave-southern-lebanon.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 receiving a threat}}}\uc2  via an unidentified Israeli phone number that she would be killed if she did not leave southern Lebanon, where she was based.\par \par \uc2 * What is a double-tap attack? Forces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/16/israel-escalates-attacks-on-medics-in-lebanon-with-deadly-quadruple-tap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 target a location}}}\uc2 , wait until people gather to help survivors, and then strike again.\par \par \uc2 * How many journalists have been killed in Lebanon in 2026? Khalil was the ninth journalist killed in Lebanon this year. Last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/28/lebanon-condemns-blatant-war-crime-israel-kills-three-journalists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three journalists}}}\uc2  were killed in a double-tap attack.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has shared comments online calling India a \u8220\'20\'1Chellhole\u8221\'20\'1D, leading India to criticize the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/24/india-trump-hellhole-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  inflammatory post as inappropriate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general has said it will audit the department\u8217\'20\'19s compliance with the Epstein Files Transparency Act. The mandated release of documents has been marred by missed deadlines, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/epstein-files-transparency-act-audit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked victims\u8217\'20\'19 information and excessive redactions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A US soldier involved in the capture of the Venezuelan president Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro has been charged over allegedly betting on the capture, federal authorities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/maduro-raid-soldier-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * At least one person was killed and five people injured on Thursday during a shootout in a mall in Baton Rouge, according {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/louisiana-mall-shooting-baton-rouge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to police}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: More than $1bn was traded on \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  during Super Bowl Sunday\par \par \uc2 Gambling addiction is spinning \u8220\'20\'1Cout of control\u8221\'20\'1D in the US, a leading campaigner for stricter regulation of the industry has warned, a position that chimes with that held by large sections of the US public, 40% of whom back the federal government \u8220\'20\'1Cdoing more to regulate sports betting\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co.uk/us-news/2026/apr/24/gambling-addiction-out-of-control-betting-markets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than $1bn was traded}}}\uc2  on the betting platform \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  during Super Bowl Sunday alone.\par \par \uc2 Culture pick: The seven best shows to stream this week\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re searching for a new show to get stuck into, look no further. From Widow\u8217\'20\'19s Bay \u8211\'20\'13 described as a \u8220\'20\'1Ca genuinely creepy comedy horror\u8221\'20\'1D from the maker of Parks and Recreation \u8211\'20\'13 to a documentary series about a woman who turned informant when her fiance confessed that he had killed a man, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/apr/24/widows-bay-to-should-i-marry-a-murderer-the-seven-best-shows-to-stream-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here are seven great options}}}\uc2  to choose from.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18I nearly quit to become a fencing teacher\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Iron Maiden at 50\par \par \uc2 Iron Maiden reflect on half a century of life as heavy metal legends, which has included lineup changes and constant gigging, but also some truly dire communication skills. In the mid-80s, the band was so burned out that its singer, Bruce Dickinson, considered quitting to become, of all things, a fencing teacher. With a new documentary reflecting on their journey out next month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/apr/24/i-nearly-quit-to-become-a-fencing-teacher-iron-maiden-on-50-years-of-heavy-metal-hard-living-and-hopeless-communication-skills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the band looks back over the decades}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Republican lawmakers attempt to shield big oil from climate lawsuits in \u8216\'20\'18alarming\u8217\'20\'19 bills\par \par \uc2 Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/republicans-big-oil-climate-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers are trying to create legal protections}}}\uc2  for the oil and gas industry, alarming environmental advocates. New House and Senate bills, led by Harriet Hageman, a Wyoming representative, and Ted Cruz, a Texas senator, respectively, would shield fossil fuel companies from lawsuits aimed at holding them accountable for damages caused by their emissions.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Crunch time! \u8216\'20\'18Kraken-like\u8217\'20\'19 giant octopuses 100m years ago crushed bones of prey\par \par \uc2 Scientists have found evidence that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/apr/23/kraken-like-giant-octopuses-crunched-cretaceous-bones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ckraken-like\u8221\'20\'1D giant octopuses}}}\uc2  were among the most formidable predators of the Cretaceous oceans, according to research finding they used to crunch through the bones of their prey. Measuring up to 62ft (19 metres) in length, the palaeontologist behind the research said fossils showed that \u8220\'20\'1Cthese were not simply large versions of modern octopuses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260424em4o0038q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
