\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 What is May Day Strong, the \u8216\'20\'18no work, no school, no shopping\u8217\'20\'19 protests against Trump?\b0\par\par\uc2 Kim Kelly \par \uc2 1,221 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2026\par 13:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Day of action to support workers set for 1 May \u8211\'20\'13 who is organizing May Day Strong, and how can people join?\par \par \uc2 Anyone who attended one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/28/no-kings-protests-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,000 No Kings protests in March}}}\uc2  might have learned of the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/mar/29/no-kings-protest-next-steps-activism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effort to protest}}}\uc2  against Trump administration policies: May Day Strong.\par \par \uc2 The single-day protest on 1 May is taking its cue from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/23/minnesota-economic-blackout-ice-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the massive day of action that shut down Minneapolis}}}\uc2  in January by asking Americans not to shop, work or go to school. Rallies, marches and teach-ins will also take place across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe labor movement in our country cannot advance while ignoring the assault on democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neidi Dominguez, founding executive director of Organized Power in Numbers and executive team member of May Day Strong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the pro-democracy movement can\u8217\'20\'19t ask working people to defend abstract principles while they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford housing, paying bills or accessing healthcare. We need a national movement that does both. That\u8217\'20\'19s why labor and community organizations are throwing down hard this May 1.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What is May Day Strong?\par \par \uc2 Organizers are expecting more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/mayday/c/mayday-2026/event/create/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,500 actions}}}\uc2  across the country \u8211\'20\'13 from street protests to walkouts \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cunder the banner of workers over billionaires, taxing the rich, demanding ICE out, money for people not wars, and expanding democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, said Dominguez.\par \par \uc2 Since 2024, the May Day Strong coalition has been hosting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SRVN2dvjZbwc6moK10Gz50-TkX8WgYaa2t_ooJvMjUc/edit?usp=drivesdk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solidarity School organizing trainings}}}\uc2 , sharing toolkits and encouraging people to set up their own May Day events. The labor unions involved are already using their institutional muscle to help, too: the \uc2 Chicago Teachers Union\uc2  (\uc2 CTU\uc2 ) successfully fought to have 1 May declared a \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ctulocal1.org/posts/may-day-heres-the-plan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 day of civic action}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in the city, and the \uc2 National Education Association (NEA)\uc2  has posted a handy May Day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nea.org/mayday-toolkit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning guide }}}\uc2 on its website.\par \par \uc2 The goal is \u8220\'20\'1Ca nationwide day of economic disruption\u8221\'20\'1D, organizers said \u8211\'20\'13 by bringing business as usual to a halt, protesters will show how powerful the working class can be when it flexes its collective muscle.\par \par \uc2 Who is organizing May Day Strong?\par \par \uc2 The May Day Strong coalition is made up of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maydaystrong.org/coalition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formidable list}}}\uc2  of unions, Democratic Socialists of America chapters, pro-democracy groups such as Indivisible (who have jumped on board to amplify the May Day message), and labor, racial justice, anti-war, pro-democracy, climate justice, immigrant rights and reproductive justice organizations.\par \par \uc2 That intersectional approach is a core aspect of their work, Dominguez said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more of us than there are of them. We just have to organize ourselves together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Where can I find May Day Strong events in my area?\par \par \uc2 May Day Strong\u8217\'20\'19s website has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maydaystrong.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a searchable map}}}\uc2  to help people find May Day actions and sign up to host their own. Signing the May Day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/8705046/WOB-NO-WORK-NO-SCHOOL-NO-SHOPPING"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledge}}}\uc2  is another way to get connected and receive more information about events.\par \par \uc2 Is it a general strike (and does that matter)?\par \par \uc2 No \u8211\'20\'13 at least not in 2026. \u8220\'20\'1CA general strike is basically a work stoppage that paralyzes multiple major industries,\u8221\'20\'1D said Eric Blanc, an assistant professor of labor studies at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not what May Day Strong is planning for this year. As many organizers have noted, it will take years to organize a full-on, sustained general strike in the US \u8211\'20\'13 which is why 2028 has emerged as a target date.\par \par \uc2 Rather, May Day Strong organizers are amplifying the call for \u8220\'20\'1Cno work, no school, no shopping\u8221\'20\'1D that anchored Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mn.gov/governor/assets/01.23.2026%20Day%20of%20Truth%20and%20Freedom_tcm1055-720666.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Day of Truth and Freedom}}}\uc2  on 23 January, bringing millions of protesters out to demand an end to ICE\u8217\'20\'19s occupation in their cities.\par \par \uc2 General strikes are rare in the US, though historically they have been one of organized labor\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful tools. In 1877, railroad workers launched a strike that paralyzed the nation; in 1919, workers in Seattle shut down the city for five days. Minneapolis saw its own general strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/about/teamster-history/the-minneapolis-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 1934}}}\uc2 , when unionized truck drivers brought the city to a standstill and lit a signal fire for other workers across the midwest to organize.\par \par \uc2 However, the passage of the 1946 Taft-Hartley Act essentially outlawed the general strike and severely limited workers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to strike in solidarity with one another. The US hasn\u8217\'20\'19t seen a true general strike since.\par \par \uc2 The tactic remains a potent lever for political change in other countries, such as India and Italy. \u8220\'20\'1CExperience across the world suggests that it may take such an action \u8211\'20\'13 or at least the credible threat of one \u8211\'20\'13 to reverse authoritarianism in the US,\u8221\'20\'1D said Blanc.\par \par \uc2 What is the May Day 2028 general strike?\par \par \uc2 That inconvenient piece of anti-labor legislation is exactly why the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/may-day-2028-general-strike-working-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Auto Workers\u8217\'20\'19 call for}}}\uc2  a May Day general strike in 2028 has generated so much excitement. The union and its lawyers are well aware of those legal constraints, which is why they had to find a loophole.\par \par \uc2 In April 2024, Shawn Fain, president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/may-day-2028-general-strike-working-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on all unions}}}\uc2 , across industries and sectors, to align their contract expiration dates for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/autoworkers-uaw-shawn-fain-may-2028-national-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1 May 2028}}}\uc2 . If those unions\u8217\'20\'19 contracts expire, so do the no-strike clauses that many contain; with no contract, there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing stopping members from going on strike. If it just so happens that thousands \u8211\'20\'13 or millions \u8211\'20\'13 of workers find themselves in that situation on the same day, well, there\u8217\'20\'19s not much the law can do to stop it.\par \par \uc2 Several major unions, including the CTU, the NEA, the American Federation of Teachers and the American Postal Workers Union, have already pledged to join them. The May Day Strong coalition is also working to support the 2028 general strike by giving non-union organizations a way to get their members ready to participate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is: without workers, the world stops running,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain wrote in an op-ed for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/may-day-2028-general-strike-working-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In These Times}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CA successful general strike is going to take time, mass coordination, and a whole lot of work by the labor movement. As working people, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://may1.uaw.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 we must come together}}}\uc2 . We can no longer allow corporations, politicians and borders to divide us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What is the history behind May Day?\par \par \uc2 May Day, or International Workers\u8217\'20\'19 Day, was first celebrated in the US in 1886, when anarchist labor organizers Lucy and Albert Parsons {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.iww.org/history/library/misc/origins_of_mayday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led 300,000 striking workers }}}\uc2 in Chicago on the first American May Day parade. While the first of May has a much older history rooted in ancient pagan rites and the changing seasons, in a political context it has since become known as a global day of celebration, struggle and remembrance for the working class.\par \par \uc2 May Day is an official holiday in 66 countries and is celebrated informally in many others, marked by marches, parades, strikes and demonstrations. However, in the US, 1 May is designated \u8220\'20\'1CLoyalty Day\u8221\'20\'1D; the workers\u8217\'20\'19 holiday, Labor Day, has been relegated to the first Monday in September. And, yes, the lack of recognition for May Day is very much {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.teenvogue.com/story/history-labor-day-us-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intentional}}}\uc2 . This has been a source of frustration for labor\u8217\'20\'19s left flank for decades, and the recently renewed focus on 1 May as a day of collective action nods to labor\u8217\'20\'19s history as well as its future.\par \par \uc2 As Fain said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time we reclaimed May Day for the working class.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260422em4m003h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
