\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 Uber\uc2  for nurses\u8217\'20\'19: gig-work apps lobby to deregulate healthcare, report finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 762 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2026\par 18:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Growing use of AI tech comes at expense of workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, protections and pay, report warns\par \par \uc2 Billion-dollar tech platforms are aggressively pushing for deregulation of the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Uber\uc2  for nursing\u8221\'20\'1D industry in an effort to expand gig work in the healthcare sector, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ainowinstitute.org/publications/uber-for-nursing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The report from the AI Now Institute, \uc2 Uber\uc2  for Nursing Part II: How Gig Nursing Companies Are Lobbying States to Deregulate Healthcare, examines the use of artificial intelligence to staff hospitals and other healthcare facilities.\par \par \uc2 The report warns that growing use of the technology comes at the expense of workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, protections and pay.\par \par \uc2 As has increasingly become the case with ride-share companies, the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Uber\uc2  for nurses\u8221\'20\'1D model relies on artificial intelligence to set pay rates for work shifts, to surveil performance metrics, and to use that data to determine a worker\u8217\'20\'19s future access to gigs and pay rates. The industry also allows nurses to bid on work shifts, with the lowest pay rate winning the shift.\par \par \uc2 The model has been lucrative for its promoters. Three nurse gig platforms have reached a $1bn valuation, according to the report, as they have received an influx of investment from private equity firms and are securing government contracts to staff public facilities, including \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)\uc2  detention centers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAI is incorporated into all these human management software systems, and for nurses that means dropping them into all kinds of places, without orientation, without workers\u8217\'20\'19 comp, without any way to protect themselves if they\u8217\'20\'19re sick and they need to cancel,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Katie J Wells, co-author of the report and a senior fellow at AI Now. \u8220\'20\'1CThat also means, for a lot of these apps, using AI technologies to facilitate a bidding war against nurses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A screenshot of a quick-bid auction from a nurse gig platform, \uc2 Clipboard Health\uc2 , states: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can choose the rate you\u8217\'20\'19d like as a bid, and the lowest bid wins!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The auction allows gig nurses to make an hourly-wage bid for work shifts at a medical facility, and the lowest-wage bid secures the position.\par \par \uc2 Clipboard Health\uc2  also uses disciplinary point systems for gig nurses, including deducting points from nurses for canceling a shift, with more points deducted for less notice being given for the cancellation, and other point deductions for showing up late to shifts.\par \par \uc2 Wells noted these trends are increasingly concerning, given healthcare has been one of the few sectors experiencing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/18/health-care-jobs.html#:~:text=The%20health%2Dcare%20sector%20has,wrote%20in%20an%20analysis%20Tuesday."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reliable and consistent job growth}}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The latest report found that since 2022 lawmakers in at least 17 states have introduced bills designed to make gig nursing platforms exempt from the regulations applied to other healthcare staffing agencies.\par \par \uc2 The lobbying by gig companies has led to exemption bills being advanced in Colorado, Illinois, Iowa, Louisiana, Minnesota, Missouri, Nevada and Rhode Island.\par \par \uc2 The gig platforms have also lobbied in favor of policies that exempt these platforms from worker protection laws, with these carve-out policies advancing in Georgia, Ohio, California, Pennsylvania, Missouri and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Gig nursing platforms are currently exempt from worker protection laws in West Virginia and unemployment insurance laws in Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 The report likens these lobbying efforts to those of ride share companies, which sought to avoid being regulated as a transportation or taxi industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really hoping that we can protect healthcare from what I fear is a sort of more aggressive attack, at least if we look since 2022 at just how much ground these companies have traveled,\u8221\'20\'1D added Wells. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve made such headway in so many places about pushing back worker protections, but also public safety concerns and in patient wellbeing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The industry has also been lobbying at the federal level, pushing for legislation to grow and expand \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent work\u8221\'20\'1D, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/1701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduction of a bill}}}\uc2  that would allow gig nursing platforms to be contracted by the government for emergencies and indemnifying these platforms from liability for patient injury.\par \par \uc2 The report contrasts these legislative pushes with New York state, which passed a law in 2025 that mandates these gig platforms must comply with state regulations for healthcare staffing agencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge concern that if this model continues to gain acceptance or carve-outs, a lot of jobs, I think, could go this way,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Wells. \u8220\'20\'1CWe focus so often on how AI is going to replace your jobs, and, OK, maybe. But also, first AI is going to totally degrade it and leave you without protections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260421em4l002xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
