\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump labor secretary Lori Chavez-DeRemer resigns amid misconduct investigation\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 753 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2026\par 15:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer, entangled in string of controversies, leaving for private sector, president\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson says\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s labor secretary, Lori Chavez-DeRemer, is stepping down, the administration announced on Monday, after a series of misconduct allegations including having an affair with a subordinate and drinking on the job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLabor Secretary Lori Chavez-DeRemer will be leaving the Administration to take a position in the private sector,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2 , a Trump spokesperson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/StevenCheung47/status/2046336343387558053"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media. \u8220\'20\'1CShe has done a phenomenal job in her role by protecting American workers, enacting fair labor practices, and helping Americans gain additional skills to improve their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer is the third cabinet member \u8211\'20\'13 all women \u8211\'20\'13 to depart during the president\u8217\'20\'19s second term, following homeland security secretary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/05/kristi-noem-fired"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem}}}\uc2  and attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/03/trump-pam-bondi-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pam Bondi}}}\uc2 . She wrote on the X social media platform: \u8220\'20\'1CIt has been an honor and a privilege to serve in this historic Administration and work for the greatest President of my lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Chavez-DeRemer\u8217\'20\'19s exit comes after she became entangled in a string of political and personal controversies. The labor secretary and her close aides are currently under investigation by the department\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general over allegations of professional misconduct.\par \par \uc2 These include claims that Chavez-DeRemer had an affair with a member of her security detail, kept a \u8220\'20\'1Cstash\u8221\'20\'1D of alcohol in her office and used government resources for personal travel, while her aides allegedly sought to channel grants towards politically connected figures, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/02/us/politics/labor-secretary-chavez-deremer-investigation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported in March.}}}\par \par \uc2 The inspector general is also reviewing material showing Chavez-DeRemer and her top aides and family members routinely sent personal messages and requests to young staff members, another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/us/politics/labor-secretary-text-messages.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Times report said last week}}}\uc2 . Chavez-DeRemer\u8217\'20\'19s husband and father exchanged text messages with young female staff members, according to the newspaper.\par \par \uc2 The scandals did not end there. The secretary\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Shawn DeRemer, an anesthesiologist, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/business/labor-secretary-husband-sexual-assault-allegations.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barred from the department\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters}}}\uc2  after allegations by at least two female staff members that he had sexually assaulted them. The women told department officials that Shawn DeRemer had touched them inappropriately at the department\u8217\'20\'19s building on Constitution Avenue in Washington.\par \par \uc2 His lawyer rejected the claims, suggesting they form part of an effort to force his wife from office. Police and prosecutors declined to pursue charges. But the inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation was believed to be nearing its conclusion and at least four department officials had been forced from their jobs as it progressed.\par \par \uc2 John Kennedy, a Republican senator from Louisiana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/19/republican-senator-criticizes-trump-pope-feud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Monday}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI think the secretary demonstrated a lot of wisdom in resigning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chavez-DeRemer, the daughter of a member of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters}}}\uc2  union, was previously a Republican congresswoman from Oregon. She had support from trade unions in her district but lost her 2024 re-election bid after one term in office.\par \par \uc2 Her nomination by Trump was welcomed by unions skeptical of the president\u8217\'20\'19s second-term agenda for workers. In March last year the Senate confirmed Chavez-DeRemer 67-32 with more than a dozen Democrats joining Republicans in backing her.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Chavez-DeRemer wrote on X: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the Department of Labor, I am proud that we made significant progress in advancing President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mission to bridge the gap between business and labor and always put the American worker first. We created new pathways to mortgage-paying jobs, prepared workers to excel in the age of AI, took steps to lower prescription drug costs, promoted retirement security, and so much more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But during her tenure, the administration cancelled millions of dollars in international grants that a labor department division administered to combat child and slave labor around the world, ending their work that had helped reduce the number of child laborers worldwide by 78 million over the last two decades.\par \par \uc2 The department also moved to rewrite or repeal more than 60 workplace regulations it saw as obsolete. The rollbacks included minimum wage requirements for homecare workers and people with disabilities, and rules governing exposure to harmful substances and safety procedures at mines. The effort drew condemnation from union leaders and workplace safety experts.\par \par \uc2 The proposed changes also included eliminating a requirement that employers provide adequate lighting for construction sites and seat belts for agriculture workers in most employer-provided transportation.\par \par \uc2 Cheung said Keith Sonderling would take on the role of acting secretary of labor.The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260420em4k006pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
