\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Employees at first ever \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store seek to unionize amid fight for contract\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 938 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2026\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Store opened in 1971 in Seattle\u8217\'20\'19s Pike Place Market joins growing unionization campaign across the coffee chain\par \par \uc2 Workers at the historic first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store are seeking to unionize as the coffee retail giant and its union appear stalemated over their first contract.\par \par \uc2 The first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pikeplacemarket.org/vendor/the-first-starbucks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened}}}\uc2  in 1971 in Seattle\u8217\'20\'19s Pike Place Market, and the store serves as a tourist site in Seattle.\par \par \uc2 Nailah Diaz, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista for about five years, three of those at Pike Place, said the Pike Place store can often have lines out the door, with waits up to two hours for tourists to come inside and look around.\par \par \uc2 She said workers at Pike Place are tasked with greater customer service responsibilities and the significant tourist traffic can bring about issues with disruptive customers and safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI myself have experienced unfair treatment, favoritism, discrimination and harassment with little to no support from management, and for me, joining this fight is me making sure that no one else has to go through what I have,\u8221\'20\'1D said Diaz. \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel personally empowered by each other\u8217\'20\'19s courage, the encouragement of our fellow union baristas and honestly, the unwavering support from our Pike Place Market community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers at Pike Place{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DWrXvDMmKdr/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  announced }}}\uc2 their union election filing earlier this month, seeking to join the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionelections.org/data/starbucks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 600 Starbucks stores }}}\uc2 that have won union elections in the US since 2021.\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  unionization campaign has continued growing, the fight for a first union contract remains ongoing. Starbucks Workers United recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/business/starbucks/starbucks-union-complaint-signals-rough-start-to-latest-round-of-talks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice (ULP) charge against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , alleging regressive bargaining when negotiations resumed this month after nearly a year without any movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has returned to the bargaining table, but its behavior hasn\u8217\'20\'19t improved. We filed a ULP over the company\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to illegally withdraw from seven signed tentative agreements previously achieved through months of bargaining,\u8221\'20\'1D Starbucks Workers United said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The average time it takes for a union to reach a first contract is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/union-first-contract-fact-sheet/#:~:text=Analysis%20published%20in%202021%20by,ratification%20was%20over%20500%20days."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 465 days}}}\uc2 , but \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are still fighting for a union contract more than four years after the first store unionized.\par \par \uc2 While the fight for a first contract continues, the union is asking the public to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nocontractnocoffee.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refrain from buying}}}\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in solidarity and to{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/04/starbucks-strike-workers-urge-customers-delete-app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  delete the Starbucks app}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Skyler Blair, a barista at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for about five years, said the Pike Place store has a lot more workers than most store locations.\par \par \uc2 Blair described the first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store as a museum or time capsule that receives visitors from all over the world with a focus on telling the company\u8217\'20\'19s story and listening to the stories of the people who come to visit the store.\par \par \uc2 Unlike most \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  locations, the store does not have food, mobile orders, or a designated lobby area where people can sit and hang out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCustomers come in, are excited to be there, and want to see and talk with us to learn the history of the store, and over time, things have gotten a little bit more difficult in order to focus on that, whether that be unsafe working conditions or the prolonged stress and fatigue that comes with such an active role in the store. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we started reaching out to the union,\u8221\'20\'1D said Blair. \u8220\'20\'1CWe felt that experience we care so much about, we\u8217\'20\'19re feeling it\u8217\'20\'19s becoming harder and harder to maintain that with the current way \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is operating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that workers at the store began discussing unionizing after realizing they had similar experiences of feeling they had been treated unfairly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTalking with each other, we started realizing that some people had gone to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for resolution and had not reached that and we all kind of shared similar sentiment, so eventually that led to us reaching out to the union and deciding to really join the fight for a better workplace,\u8221\'20\'1D Blair said.\par \par \uc2 Both Blair and Diaz cited \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s record of union busting, including allegations of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fastcompany.com/91413779/starbucks-stores-closing-full-list-59-union-locations-doomed-in-restructuring"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shutting down}}}\uc2  unionized stores and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DXKVQiKiTQp/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing or disciplining workers}}}\uc2  for union activities, which \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has denied.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , as a company, has a pretty historic record of union busting,\u8221\'20\'1D said Diaz.\par \par \uc2 Blair said that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s record on unionization instills fear in workers of being retaliated against, but the unity in workers coming together to improve their workplace has offset those fears.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe the unity that I have with fellow baristas with me in this cause to really fight for a better workplace is stronger than any fear that could be out there,\u8221\'20\'1D Blair said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo while it may be challenging at times, I do feel like there is hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  spokesperson, Jaci Anderson, said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has been engaging in good faith and put forward comprehensive proposals that build on \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 already competitive pay and industry-leading benefits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSignificant changes have occurred over the past two years, including during the period when Workers United chose not to bargain, and it is appropriate that proposals reflect current business realities, customer expectations, and partner interests. We are at the table and engaging in good faith,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anderson.\par \par \uc2 In response to the Pike\u8217\'20\'19s Place location\u8217\'20\'19s union drive, Anderson said the workers at the store earn more than typical Starbucks workers and that not all workers at the store are supportive of the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFiling a petition is simply the start of a process. Our partners are at the heart of who we are, and today, we offer industry-leading pay and benefits,\u8221\'20\'1D added Anderson.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260417em4h0030d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
