\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Power in the hands of people\u8217\'20\'19: union leaders push to revive ailing US labor movement\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato in New York \par \uc2 1,264 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2026\par 13:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Organizers unveil new drive to reverse decline in union membership as workers seek to combat growing wealth inequalityWhat does Trump\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive voter ID bill mean for US democracy? Our reporters answered your questions\par \par \uc2 Leaders of some of the largest unions in the US have unveiled a drive to jumpstart the country\u8217\'20\'19s ailing labor movement and combat growing wealth inequality under Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 To make it easier for workers to join a union, and strengthen the hand of new unions negotiating with powerful businesses, a string of prominent organizers joined together to launch Union Now, a non-profit designed to increase labor union density.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is really about trying to put power in the hands of people,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2 , the largest flight attendants union in the US, and one of the leaders of the push.\par \par \uc2 She suggested the time had come for workers to start thinking \u8211\'20\'13 in some ways \u8211\'20\'13 more like the companies that employ them. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s 70% of workers who want a union, and 10% have them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nelson. \u8220\'20\'1CIf it were a company, they would figure out how to get the product into the hands of the 70% who wanted it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The architects of Union Now hope it will provide mobilizing workers with financial firepower. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is that even if unions spent all of their money on organizing and all of their efforts on organizing, it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be enough,\u8221\'20\'1D Nelson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have to also do all the representation of their current members, have contract fights and all the rest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is really about making it possible for working people to get a union, to outweigh the boss, to be able to stand up to bosses who fire workers illegally during organizing drives, to support recognition strikes and to support contract strikes too,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll in together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Union density in the US was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R47596#:~:text=While%20peak%20union%20density%20occurred,also%20generally%20increased%20until%201979."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 30% }}}\uc2 in the 1950s, but declined precipitously over the ensuing decades. It stood at just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=10+percent+union+density+2025+theguardian&sca_esv=2872a9e5c3ead16d&sxsrf=ANbL-n4t7HRZefL28k8dVO7QnHykaBLliw%3A1776030725783&ei=BRTcafvEL-nU5NoPp6DZwAo&biw=970&bih=500&ved=0ahUKEwi725SEpumTAxVpKlkFHSdQFqgQ4dUDCBE&uact=5&oq=10+percent+union+density+2025+theguardian&gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiKTEwIHBlcmNlbnQgdW5pb24gZGVuc2l0eSAyMDI1IHRoZWd1YXJkaWFuMgUQIRigATIFECEYoAFIpBZQtQFYgBVwAHgCkAEAmAGFBKABhxCqAQswLjEuMS4yLjEuMbgBA8gBAPgBAZgCB6ACkxDCAgQQABhHwgIHECEYChigAZgDAIgGAZAGCJIHCTEuMS4xLjIuMqAH3RSyBwkwLjEuMS4yLjK4B5EQwgcDNS4yyAcFgAgB&sclient=gws-wiz-serp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10% in 2025}}}\uc2 , despite opinion polls indicating vast public approval and support for labor unions.\par \par \uc2 The number of union members in the US peaked in 1979 at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R47596#:~:text=Figure%202%20shows%20the%20total,also%20generally%20increased%20until%201979."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 21 million members}}}\uc2 , compared with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf#:~:text=Union%20Representation%20Workers%20represented%20by%20a%20union,covered%20by%20a%20union%20contract%20(1.8%20million)."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14.7 million }}}\uc2 today. Over the same period, the US population has grown by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/dec/popchange-data-text.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 100 million}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn NYC, as across the country, one of the biggest challenges workers who have already chosen a union has faced is the time it takes to get a first contract,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Su, deputy mayor for economic justice in New York City, and former secretary of labor under the Biden administration, said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese delays are, in effect, a form of union busting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , the federal watchdog for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, has meanwhile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/14/labor-movement-union-trump-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken a starkly different path}}}\uc2  since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEmployers fail to honor their employees\u8217\'20\'19 decision and their rights, hoping that as long as there is no first contract, workers will start to tire and question the value of being in a union,\u8221\'20\'1D said Su. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you add explicit unfair labor practices to this, and an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  hostile to workers, the results are predictable and devastating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It can take on average {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ibewgov.org/new-bill-calls-for-faster-first-contract-talks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 450 days }}}\uc2 for a first union contract to be reached. While efforts to reform labor law to facilitate union organizing and bargaining have stalled in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , many employers drag out and delay bargaining for several years after workers vote to form a union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be a real union town, we have to use every lever the city has to combat this, including showing up for workers who are organizing and coming from a position of strength when we contract with, purchase from, and work with companies so our expectations are clear,\u8221\'20\'1D said Su. \u8220\'20\'1COver 60 million people across the US say they would join a union if they could, yet we have seen ever-decreasing union density.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a rally marking the launch of Union Now on Sunday, Senator Bernie Sanders and the New York City mayor, Zohran Mamdani, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/13/bernie-sanders-warns-worst-is-yet-to-come-in-rallying-cry-against-billionaires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a rallying cry to workers looking to take on the power of billionaires}}}\uc2 . Workers involved in some of the most high-profile union organizing efforts in the US over the past several years that have faced staunch employer opposition, including from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/apr/08/long-fight-organize-us-workers-amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/us-union-boom-starbucks-amazon#:~:text=According%20to%20a%202022%20article%20by%20Michael,to%20handle%20the%20surge%20in%20labor%20activity**"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 REI}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/03/delta-flights-attendants-union-push"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delta Air Lines}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/02/wells-fargo-workers-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wells Fargo}}}\uc2 , also appeared.\par \par \uc2 Even in cases where workers have successfully unionized, such as at hundreds of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores since 2021, employers have dragged out and delayed reaching a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are more of us than there are them,\u8221\'20\'1D Brittany Norris, a \uc2 Delta Air Lines\uc2  flight attendant based in New York City who is involved in organizing flight attendants at the airline, told the rally. \u8220\'20\'1CLife experience has taught me that we, the employees, are the living, breathing workforce that builds and maintains true community, a community that looks out for one another, protects each other, and provides and protects us when we need it most.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The organizing effort at \uc2 Delta Air Lines\uc2  is the largest currently in the US, aimed at mobilizing 30,000 flight attendants at the last major US airline where flight attendants have yet to unionize. Delta has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/05/delta-airlines-union-wages-record-profits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  the effort, while federal labor law mandates the workers must have a majority of union authorization cards signed within 12 months to be able to file for a union election.\par \par \uc2 Delta affirmed its position against unionization. \u8220\'20\'1CDelta\u8217\'20\'19s culture is firmly rooted in taking care of its employees who, over the past two decades, have repeatedly chosen to reject AFA [Association of Flight Attendants] representation,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBefore I worked at Starbucks, I was at Chipotle under then CEO Brian Niccol,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mina Leon, a Starbucks worker in New York City, among those still fighting for a first union contract at the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were understaffed, underpaid and overworked. But I remember hearing about this new Starbucks workers union. It felt like every week, more baristas were joining, and it gave me hope that things could be better.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, in 2025 I started working at Starbucks under our CEO, Brian Nichol. Would you believe it? We are understaffed, underpaid and overworked. But now I\u8217\'20\'19m a member of the union I looked up to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Starbucks did not respond a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Connor Spence, president of the Amazon Labor Union, which represents Amazon workers at JFK8 in Staten Island, New York, said the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest retailer had spent the past four years trying to overturn the results of its victorious union election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery day in this movement, there are workers who are putting it all on the line at great cost to themselves, in defiance of an employer whose main weapon is futility and isolation and despair,\u8221\'20\'1D said Spence. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile this fight is far from over, know that we are making progress. None of it would be possible without each other. So when we win, and I believe that we will win, it will be because we fought together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon denied allegations of interfering with workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to choose whether or not to join a union. \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon employees have the choice of whether or not to join a union,\u8221\'20\'1D said spokesperson Eileen Hards. \u8220\'20\'1CThey always have. The fact is we already provide much of what the Teamsters are requesting including safe and inclusive workplaces, competitive pay, health benefits on day one, and opportunities for career growth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260415em4f002pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
