\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Israeli strike kills paramedic, says \uc2 Lebanese Red Cross\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Fulton, Marina Dunbar, Yohannes Lowe, Hayden Vernon and Imogen Dewey \par \uc2 8,864 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2026\par 07:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. Our live coverage continues here\par \par \uc2 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this page now but our live coverage continues on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/13/iran-war-live-news-ceasefire-peace-talks-us-trump-strait-hormuz-blockade-middle-east-crisis-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new blog here}}}\uc2 , including a snapshot of the latest key developments. Thanks for following along.\par \par \uc2 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump blasts Pope Leo after pontiff denounces 'delusion of omnipotence'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has launched a scathing attack on Pope Leo XIV, saying he is \u8220\'20\'1Cweak on crime and terrible for foreign policy\u8221\'20\'1D and is hurting the Catholic church.\par \par \uc2 The US president also posted on his Truth Social platform that it was only because he was president that the US-born Leo became pope.\par \par \uc2 Trump said in the post:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attack came after Leo denounced the \u8220\'20\'1Cdelusion of omnipotence\u8221\'20\'1D as fuelling the US-Israel war in Iran and demanded political leaders stop and negotiate peace.\par \par \uc2 Leo also presided over an evening prayer service in St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica on Saturday as the US-Iran talks began in Pakistan amid the fragile ceasefire, the Associated Press reports\par \par \uc2 The pope didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention the US or Trump by name in his prayer but the pontiff\u8217\'20\'19s tone and message appeared directed at Trump and US officials, who have boasted of US military superiority and justified the war in religious terms.\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke to reporters in Maryland soon after his social media post and said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s doing a very good job,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not a fan of Pope Leo\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vow to block the strait of Hormuz came after the weekend US-Iran talks failed to reach a deal. But the two sides turned up in Pakistan to test each other\u8217\'20\'19s resolve, writes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/patrickwintour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Wintour}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and it was probably unrealistic to expect a long-running dispute to be settled in one marathon session.\par \par \uc2 The report from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic editor says:\par \par \uc2 See the full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/us-iran-21-hours-talks-war-vance-pakistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planeloads of negotiators and too little time: US and Iran\u8217\'20\'19s 21 hours of talks}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Australian shares fall after Trump announces Hormuz strait blockade\par \par \uc2 The Australian share market dropped sharply on Monday morning after US-Iran peace talks broke down and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said the navy would blockade the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 The S&P/ASX 200 fell 0.8% to trade at the 8,890 point mark in the opening minutes of trading. The benchmark had been poised to open higher, according to futures pricing over the weekend, before the breakdown in peace talks spooked traders.\par \par \uc2 Market strategy consultant Greg Boland, from trading platform Moomoo, says the increase in geopolitical tension will weigh on market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices have also risen back above the $US100 a barrel this morning, according to futures pricing.\par \par \uc2 Global equity markets have been pulled up and down by the Middle East conflict given energy disruptions and increased oil costs contribute to global inflation by elevating costs across nearly all goods and services.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentary speaker, who led Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s negotiators at the weekend talks with Washington, has taunted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over petrol prices amid the US president\u8217\'20\'19s vow to blockade the strait of Hormuz.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mb_ghalibaf/status/2043425869570416802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf}}}\uc2  posted on X above an image appearing to show prices per gallon at gas stations in the White House area:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister has said his government wants to see negotiations between the US and Iran continue and that Australia has not been asked to participate in any US blockade of the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Albanese told Channel 9 television on Monday morning:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 The war with Iran has cost Israel about\par \par \uc2 35bn shekels (US$11.5bn) in direct budgetary expenses, according to preliminary estimates from the \uc2 Israeli finance ministry\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ministry said the war \u8211\'20\'13 involving Israel and the US against Iran \u8211\'20\'13 had inflicted severe economic damage, including a significant contraction of GDP and a surge in government spending.\par \par \uc2 Officials warned that the full financial impact \u8211\'20\'13 including long-term reconstruction and economic recovery costs \u8211\'20\'13 might not be fully realised for some time.\par \par \uc2 The largest portion of the budget was consumed by the \uc2 Israel Defence Forces\uc2 , the defence ministry, the national security ministry and various intelligence organisations.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump considering limited military strikes against Iran \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his advisers are looking at resuming limited military strikes in Iran in addition to the US blockade of the Hormuz strait as a way to break a stalemate in peace talks, the Wall Street Journal is reporting, citing officials and people familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 That was among the options the president was considering on Sunday, hours after negotiations collapsed in Pakistan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/trump-weighs-limited-strikes-on-iran-after-talks-collapse-71908883?mod=WSJ_home_mediumtopper_pos_3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the report}}}\uc2  quoted the officials as saying.\par \par \uc2 It continued:\par \par \uc2 After the collapse of the US-Iran talks in Pakistan, Trump spent much of Sunday at his resort in Miami, calling in to a Fox News show, golfing and talking with advisers, the report said. He remained open to a diplomatic solution, aides said, even as he promised the blockade and threatened again to target Iran\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 A White House spokesperson declined to discuss Trump\u8217\'20\'19s specific options, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 * Trump said the US Navy would\par \par \uc2 start blockading the strait of Hormuz and would also interdict every vessel in international waters that had paid a toll to Iran. In a lengthy Truth Social post, he said the US was going to start \u8220\'20\'1CBLOCKADING any and all Ships trying to enter, or leave, the Strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * In another post Trump also claimed that Iran had \u8220\'20\'1Cknowingly failed\u8221\'20\'1D to make good on its promise to open the strait, causing \u8220\'20\'1Canxiety\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpain\u8221\'20\'1D for many countries around the world.\par \par \uc2 * US Central Command (Centcom) announced it would begin its blockade of the strait beginning Monday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CCentcom forces will begin implementing a blockade of all maritime traffic entering and exiting Iranian ports on April 13 at 10am ET [1400 GMT], in accordance with the president\u8217\'20\'19s proclamation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Iran\u8217\'20\'19s Revolutionary Guards warned in their latest statement that \u8220\'20\'1Capproaching military vessels to the strait of Hormuz is considered a violation of the ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Trump reiterated his threat to destroy Iran\u8217\'20\'19s power plants and other civilian energy infrastructure if no deal is reached to end the war, which he started with Israel in what is widely seen as an illegal and unprovoked attack. \u8220\'20\'1CI could take out Iran in one day,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Fox News on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 * Trump also said the US didn\u8217\'20\'19t need the strait. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t get our oil from there. We have so much oil,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president told Fox. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have boats pouring up to the United States \u8230\'20\'26 We don\u8217\'20\'19t need the strait.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Iran\u8217\'20\'19s top negotiator, Mohammad Baqer Qalibaf, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new threats would have no effect on the Iranian nation. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you fight, we will fight, and if you come forward with logic, we will deal with logic. We will not bow to any threats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Oil prices rose in early trading on Sunday after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vow over the Hormuz strait, with US crude increasing 8% to $104.24 a barrel and Brent crude rising 7% to $102.29.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oil prices rise after Trump blockade vow\par \par \uc2 More on the oil price lift: the price of US crude increased 8% to $104.24 a barrel and Brent crude oil rose 7% to $102.29 in early market trading on Sunday after Donald Trump said the US would blockade Iranian ports starting on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports that Brent crude \u8211\'20\'13 the international standard \u8211\'20\'13 has swung dramatically during the Iran war, rising from roughly $70 a barrel before the war in late February to more than $119 at times.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, ahead of the peace talks in Pakistan, Brent for June delivery fell 0.8% to $95.20 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Iran has been effectively controlling the strait of Hormuz, a key waterway for global oil and LPG shipping. US Central Command said the blockade would be \u8220\'20\'1Cenforced impartially against vessels of all nations\u8221\'20\'1D entering or departing Iranian ports and coastal areas.\par \par \uc2 It said it would still allow ships traveling between non-Iranian ports to transit the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 About a fifth of the world\u8217\'20\'19s traded oil typically flows through the strait of Hormuz every day. Saudi Arabia, Iraq, the United Arab Emirates, Kuwait and Iran are all major exporters.\par \par \uc2 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oil prices have reportedly risen in early market trading after Donald Trump said the US would blockade the strait of Hormuz following the failure of weekend peace talks.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s minister of foreign affairs, Abbas Araghchi, said that yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations between the US and Iran actually came close to agreement at some point, but ultimately fell apart due to the US \u8220\'20\'1Cshifting goalposts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn intensive talks at the highest level in 47 years, Iran engaged with US in good faith to end the war,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/araghchi/status/2043441805270696045"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut when just inches away from \u8216\'20\'18Islamabad MoU\u8217\'20\'19, we encountered maximalism, shifting goalposts, and blockade. Zero lessons earned. Good will begets good will. Enmity begets enmity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mohammad-Bagher Ghalibaf, Parliament speaker of Iran, also chimed in to remind the White House of rising gas prices in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnjoy the current pump figures,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mb_ghalibaf/status/2043425869570416802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWith the so-called \u8216\'20\'18blockade\u8217\'20\'19, soon you\u8217\'20\'19ll be nostalgic for $4\u8211\'20\'13$5 gas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Lebanese Red Cross said an Israeli drone strike hit their unit and killed a paramedic on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis evening, while carrying out a humanitarian mission at a site on the road to the town of Beit Yahoun, Lebanese Red Cross teams came under direct targeting from an Israeli drone, resulting in the martyrdom of paramedic Hassan Badawi, the injury of another paramedic with minor wounds, and their transfer to Tebnine Governmental Hospital,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RedCrossLebanon/status/2043401652233789769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 2,055 people in Lebanon have been killed in Israeli strikes since the start of the latest war between Israel and Hezbollah, according to the Health Ministry. Among the dead are 252 women, 165 children, and 87 medical workers. 6,588 others have been wounded.\par \par \uc2 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Central Command says it will begin blockade of Iranian ports Monday\par \par \uc2 US Central Command (Centcom) has announced that they will begin their blockade of the strait of Hormuz beginning Monday morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCentcom forces will begin implementing a blockade of all maritime traffic entering and exiting Iranian ports on April 13 at 10am ET, in accordance with the President\u8217\'20\'19s proclamation.\u8220\'20\'1CThe blockade will be enforced impartially against vessels of all nations entering or departing Iranian ports and coastal areas, including all Iranian ports on the Arabian Gulf and Gulf of Oman. Centcom forces will not impede freedom of navigation for vessels transiting the strait of Hormuz to and from non-Iranian ports.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said earlier that he plans to begin blockading the strait in an attempt to take control of the strategic waterway from Iran in the aftermath of failed peace negotiations between the countries in Pakistan.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 UK prime minister Keir Starmer held a call with French president Emmanuel Macron this afternoon to discuss the ongoing regional crisis in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders reportedly focused on the necessity of immediate de-escalation, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/news/pm-call-with-president-macron-of-france-12-april-2026"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  from Downing Street. Starmer emphasized the need for a \u8220\'20\'1Clasting ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D with both heads of state agreeing that such an agreement must encompass Lebanon to ensure genuine regional stability.\par \par \uc2 The leaders also underscored the critical role of the strait of Hormuz in maintaining global trade and energy security. They committed to mobilizing a broad international coalition to safeguard freedom of navigation.\par \par \uc2 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iranian president Masoud Pezeshkian says that an agreement with the US is achievable if \u8220\'20\'1Cthe American government abandons its totalitarianism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the American government abandons its totalitarianism and respects the rights of the Iranian nation, ways to reach an agreement will certainly be found,\u8221\'20\'1D Pezeshkian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drpezeshkian/status/2043402196180722101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His statement follows an earlier call Pezeshkian held with Russian president Vladimir Putin on Sunday, in which he reportedly said that Tehran is prepared to reach a deal to secure \u8220\'20\'1Clasting regional peace\u8221\'20\'1D, provided that Iran\u8217\'20\'19s national interests are respected.\par \par \uc2 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The failure of negotiations to end the US war with Iran has unleashed a barrage of starkly partisan political responses, with leading Republicans making hawkish calls for Donald Trump to \u8220\'20\'1Cfinish the job\u8221\'20\'1D while top Democrats warned that it would be disastrous for the president to resume hostilities.\par \par \uc2 The former UN ambassador during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidency, Nikki Haley, led the Republican charge. She told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union on Sunday that the current two-week ceasefire was a test of nerves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is like a game of chicken,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s who caves first. The Iranian regime is hoping that Trump will cave. Today, he showed he\u8217\'20\'19s not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley was alluding to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threat, made hours after marathon peace talks in Pakistan ended without result, that the US military would blockade the strait of Hormuz to prevent Iran profiting from its control of the narrow shipping passage. She encouraged Trump to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo after Iran where it hurts\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that what would \u8220\'20\'1Creally bring Iran to its knees is to go after it economically\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week, US senator Ron Johnson \u8211\'20\'13 a Wisconsin Republican \u8211\'20\'13 also urged Trump to take a hard line. He advocated the total removal of the Iranian regime, admitting that the task \u8220\'20\'1Ccould be longer term\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/us-lawmakers-us-israel-iran-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US lawmakers split on party lines over negotiations\u8217\'20\'19 failure to end Iran war}}}\par \par \uc2 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s navy chief Shahram Irani on Sunday called US president Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threat to blockade the strait of Hormuz \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D, after marathon talks between Tehran and Washington in Pakistan failed to deliver a deal to end the conflict, reports AFP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe brave men of the naval force of the army of the Islamic Republic of Iran are monitoring and supervising all the movements of the aggressive American army in the region. The threats of the US president to blockade Iran at sea... are very ridiculous and funny,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, according to state TV.\par \par \uc2 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has said the US will begin blockading the strait of Hormuz in an attempt to take control of the strategic waterway from Iran in the aftermath of failed peace negotiations between the countries in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/pakistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pakistan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US president also threatened to bomb Iran\u8217\'20\'19s water treatment facilities as well as its power plants and bridges, repeating an earlier threat, if Tehran did not agree to abandon its nuclear weapons programme \u8211\'20\'13 the key sticking point between the two sides.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s surprise announcement of a blockade came after 21 hours of face-to-face peace negotiations between the US and Iran in Islamabad collapsed on Sunday morning.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the vice-president and head of the US team, said Iran had refused to give up the possibility of developing nuclear weapons, while the Iranian delegates said Washington needed to do more to win their trust.\par \par \uc2 My colleagues Dan Sabbagh and Sam Jones have more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/trump-says-us-will-blockade-strait-of-hormuz-as-iran-peace-talks-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says US will blockade strait of Hormuz after Iran peace talks fail}}}\par \par \uc2 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 'We will not bow to any threats,' Iran's chief negotiator says in state media reports\par \par \uc2 Iran had very good initiatives to show goodwill in talks with the US which led to progress in the negotiations, the country\u8217\'20\'19s top negotiator Mohammad Baqer Qalibaf said in comments carried by state media on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Qalibaf said Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new threats will have no effect on the Iranian nation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you fight, we will fight, and if you come forward with logic, we will deal with logic. We will not bow to any threats, let them test our will once again so that we can teach them a bigger lesson,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The UK will not be involved in any blockade of the strait of Hormuz, the Guardian understands, despite claims by Donald Trump on Sunday the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to be blockading the strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D with the assistance of Nato allies.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox News, the US president said \u8220\'20\'1Cit won\u8217\'20\'19t take long to clean out the strait\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cnumerous countries are going to be helping us\u8221\'20\'1D, adding the UK and other nations were sending minesweepers.\par \par \uc2 The UK has previously suggested it could play a role in making the strait of Hormuz safe to pass, and has mine-hunting systems and anti-drone capabilities already in the region. But there have been concerns in Whitehall that complying with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demand to send ships could escalate the crisis. The UK\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to consider a role in mine removal operations is seen as distinct from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blockade proposal.\par \par \uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/wes-streeting-attacks-trump-outrageous-iran-war-rhetoric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK will not join any Trump blockade of strait of Hormuz}}}\par \par \uc2 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reports from multiple outlets state that JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s goal in the talks with Iran was to outline America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cred lines\u8221\'20\'1D and look for room to negotiate. But Iran\u8217\'20\'19s delegates could not agree to all of the stated red lines.\par \par \uc2 Robert Malley, a lead negotiator on the 2015 Iran nuclear deal, has commented in response to the \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BarakRavid/status/2043365165026996277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red lines}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D that the US reportedly detailed during yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations.\par \par \uc2 These lines include: Ending all uranium enrichment, dismantling all major nuclear enrichment facilities, and fully opening the strait of Hormuz, charging no tolls for passage.\par \par \uc2 Malley responded to these demands on social media, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Rob_Malley/status/2043368155418873906"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIf these were actual red lines, they could have spared themselves the trip.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Malley previously led the Middle East desk of the National Security Council under the Obama administration, becoming a key negotiator on the Iran nuclear deal.\par \par \uc2 Hooman Majd, an Iranian-American journalist and political commentator, also responded to the red lines list, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/hmajd/status/2043371195651805408"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no way that Iran will ever concede every one of these points (if it even considers any of them at all).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo realistically, either Trump chooses to go back to talks and is willing to offer compromises, or goes back to war with all the consequences that will ensue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) said on Sunday that the Israeli military has been ramming and shooting at them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn two occasions today, Israel Defense Forces (IDF) soldiers rammed UNIFIL vehicles with a Merkava tank, in one case causing significant damage,\u8221\'20\'1D UNIFIL wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/UNIFIL_/status/2043372712924475793"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe soldiers had blocked a road in Bayada that is used to access UNIFIL positions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past week, Israeli soldiers have fired \u8216\'20\'18warning shots\u8217\'20\'19 in the area, striking and damaging clearly identifiable UNIFIL vehicles,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement continued. \u8220\'20\'1CIn one case, a \u8216\'20\'18warning shot\u8217\'20\'19 landed a meter away from a peacekeeper who had dismounted his vehicle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iranian president Masoud Pezeshkian reportedly told Russian president Vladimir Putin on Sunday that Tehran is prepared to reach a deal to secure \u8220\'20\'1Clasting regional peace\u8221\'20\'1D, provided that Iran\u8217\'20\'19s national interests are respected.\par \par \uc2 According to a readout from Iranian state media, Pezeshkian used the call to condemn the US\u8217\'20\'19s use of military bases in Gulf nations to launch strikes against Iran. Despite these tensions, he characterized neighboring Gulf countries as \u8220\'20\'1Cbrothers\u8221\'20\'1D and reaffirmed Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s desire to establish a regional security framework that excludes \u8220\'20\'1Coutside powers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s Revolutionary Guard (IRGC) has warned in its latest statement that \u8220\'20\'1Capproaching military vessels to the strait of Hormuz is considered a violation of the ceasefire\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Navy of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps declares that contrary to the false claims of some enemy officials, the strait of Hormuz is under intelligent control and management, open for the harmless passage of non-military vessels in accordance with specific regulations, and any military vessels attempting to approach the strait of Hormuz under any pretext or excuse will be considered a violation of the ceasefire and will be dealt with harshly and decisively.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Warner, a Virginia Democrat and the vice-chairman of the US Senate intelligence committee, told CNN on Sunday that he questions the logic of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blockade strategy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how blockading the strait is going to somehow push the Iranians into opening it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t get the connection there,\u8221\'20\'1D Warners told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 Warner added that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t see \u8220\'20\'1Chow blockading the strait gets it open suddenly, I don\u8217\'20\'19t get that logic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US 'doesn't need the strait' for its oil, Donald Trump tells Fox News\par \par \uc2 During his Fox News interview, Trump also said that the US \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t need the strait\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t get our oil from there. We have so much oil,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have boats pouring up to the United States. They\u8217\'20\'19ll be filling them up, and they\u8217\'20\'19ll be leaving and they\u8217\'20\'19ll be packed with the best oil you can get. Light, sweet, crude. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need the strait,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 When asked if blockading the strait would result in lower oil and gas prices, Trump responded: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, eventually it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be lower. No, it might not happen initially but it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna go down. When this is all over, look, the stock market, the Dow hit 50,000.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones industrial average crossed 50,000 for the first time back in February, as ballooning tech valuations and hopes of lower interest rates drove it to new highs. However, the Dow has since been falling and is currently sitting under 48,000, due largely to surging energy costs caused by the war on Iran.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump also defended his earlier threats during his Fox News interview, saying on Sunday that his previous post where he wrote that a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole civilization will die tonight, never to be brought back again\u8221\'20\'1D was what brought Iran to be willing to negotiate. He also accused the Islamic Republic of making worse statements, such as \u8220\'20\'1CDeath to America. Death to Israel. America is a Satan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then reiterated his threats: \u8220\'20\'1CIn one half of a day they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have one bridge standing, they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have one electric generating plant standing and they\u8217\'20\'19re back in the stone ages.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump threatens to destroy Iran's energy infrastructure if no deal is reached\par \par \uc2 Trump has reiterated his threat to destroy Iran\u8217\'20\'19s power plants and other civilian energy infrastructure if no deal is reached to end the war, which he started with Israel in what is widely seen as an illegal and unprovoked attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI could take out Iran in one day,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 Maria Bartiromo by phone. \u8220\'20\'1CI could have their entire energy everything, every one of their plants, their electric generating plants, which is a big deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats to launch mass bombing of civilian infrastructure in Iran would likely amount to war crimes if carried out, according to legal scholars.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIntentionally attacking civilian infrastructure constitute war crimes under international law,\u8221\'20\'1D Agn\u232\'00\'E8s Callamard, secretary general of Amnesty International {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/04/iran-president-trumps-apocalyptic-threats-of-large-scale-civilian-devastation-demand-urgent-global-action-to-prevent-atrocity-crimes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said last week}}}\uc2 , after Trump warned that \u8220\'20\'1Ca whole civilization will die tonight\u8221\'20\'1D unless Iran agreed a deal to end the war and unblock the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven in the limited cases that civilian infrastructure qualify as military targets, a party still cannot attack them if this may cause disproportionate harm to civilians,\u8221\'20\'1D Callamard said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPower plants, water systems and energy infrastructure are indispensable to civilian life, underpinning access to clean water, medical care, hospital electricity, food supply chains, and basic livelihoods. Attacking them would be disproportionate and thus unlawful under international humanitarian law and could amount to a war crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says UK among countries sending minesweepers to help with strait of Hormuz\par \par \uc2 Trump also told Fox News that \u8220\'20\'1Cnumerous countries are going to be helping us\u8221\'20\'1D with the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 He said the UK is among those that were sending minesweepers to remove mines that may have been placed in the water.\par \par \uc2 Downing Street has not publicly confirmed this yet, although the UK has been working to figure out a \u8220\'20\'1Cpractical\u8221\'20\'1D plan to reopen the strait.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have minesweepers there. Now we have highly sophisticated underwater minesweepers, which are the latest and the greatest, but we\u8217\'20\'19re also bringing in more traditional minesweepers,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in an interview with Maria Bartiromo on Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 Sunday Morning Futures with Maria Bartiromo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so I understand is the UK and a couple of other countries are sending mine sweepers,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says 'it will take a little while' for US to blockade strait of Hormuz\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has followed up on his statements made on Truth Social a short while ago (see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/12/middle-east-crisis-live-us-iran-pakistan-peace-talks-jd-vance-delegation-leaves-without-a-deal?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-69db9a008f08dd4830774b67#block-69db9a008f08dd4830774b67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this post}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/12/middle-east-crisis-live-us-iran-pakistan-peace-talks-jd-vance-delegation-leaves-without-a-deal?page=with%3Ablock-69db9aa98f08dd4830774b6c#block-69db9aa98f08dd4830774b6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that post}}}\uc2 ) in a phone interview with Fox News. He said again that the US will be blockading the strait of Hormuz, in what would be a major escalation in the war, but acknowledged that it may \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a little while\u8221\'20\'1D to do so. Trump then claimed that it won\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Ctake long\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cclean out\u8221\'20\'1D the strait.\par \par \uc2 He claimed that Nato, which he has repeatedly criticised for the alliance\u8217\'20\'19s unwillingness to assist in his war on Iran, wants to help with unblocking the strait.\par \par \uc2 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group armed with automatic weapons tried to board a vessel in the Red Sea about an hour ago, the UK maritime security monitors have said.The Royal Navy coordinated UK Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) said the vessel was \u8220\'20\'1Capproached by a skiff with approximately 10-12 people on board, 4-5 of whom were armed with automatic weapons\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe crew requested that the sailing vessel stopped and when the Master refused they attempted to pull the skiff alongside to board.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8220\'20\'1CThe Master deployed a flare and the skiff turned away and departed to the southeast. Authorities are investigating,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.The incident happened at about 11.25am universal time or 12.25 British Summer Time. It took place off the cost of Yemen. UKMTO acts as a bridge between military forces and merchant vessels reporting incidents including drones and missile or projectile attacks in Indian Ocean, the Red Sea and the Gulf region.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.13am BST\par \par \uc2 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Iran has cost Israel 35 billion shekels ($11.52bn; \u163\'00\'A38.57bn) in budgetary expenses, with 22 billion shekels ($7.3bn; \u163\'00\'A35.4bn) of that going to defence, the finance ministry said, citing a preliminary estimate.\par \par \uc2 The amount has already been added to the 2026 budget, it added.\par \par \uc2 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump signed off one of his Truth social posts by saying the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cfully locked and loaded\u8221\'20\'1D, warning Iran that the American military \u8220\'20\'1Cwill finish up the little that is left\u8221\'20\'1D of the country if he decides on that action at some point in the future.\par \par \uc2 These continued threats by Trump are unlikely to foster positive relations between Washington and Tehran before any future diplomatic talks.\par \par \uc2 From his statement it sounds as if he may be warning Iran of future US military attacks if it strongly resists or reacts militarily to the promised American blockade of the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims Iran has 'knowingly failed' to make good on promise to open strait of Hormuz\par \par \uc2 In another Truth Social post, Trump also claimed that Iran has \u8220\'20\'1Cknowingly failed\u8221\'20\'1D to make good on its promise to open the strait, causing \u8220\'20\'1Canxiety\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpain\u8221\'20\'1D for many countries around the world. He went on to warn that Tehran \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter begin the process\u8221\'20\'1D of opening the vital waterway and to do it quickly, saying the regime has \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated\u8221\'20\'1D every \u8220\'20\'1Claw in the book\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he has been debriefed by his vice president, JD Vance, his special envoy Steve Witkoff and son-in-law/advisor Jared Kushner on the Pakistan talks that failed to produce a breakthrough to bring an end to the war.\par \par \uc2 He said Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting in Islamabad lasted close to 20 hours. \u8220\'20\'1CI could go into great detail, and talk about much that has been gotten but, there is only one thing that matters \u8212\'20\'14 IRAN IS UNWILLING TO GIVE UP ITS NUCLEAR AMBITIONS! In many ways, the points that were agreed to are better than us continuing our Military Operations to conclusion, but all of those points don\u8217\'20\'19t matter compared to allowing Nuclear Power to be in the hands of such volatile, difficult, unpredictable people,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says US to start blockading the strait of Hormuz\par \par \uc2 The US president, Donald Trump, said the US Navy would immediately start blockading the strait of Hormuz and would also interdict every vessel in international waters that had paid a toll to Iran.\par \par \uc2 In a lengthy Truth Social post, he said the US is going to start \u8220\'20\'1CBLOCKADING any and all Ships trying to enter, or leave, the Strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump said that the US Navy is going to start \u8220\'20\'1C destroying the mines the Iranians laid in the straits\u8221\'20\'1D, warning that any Iranian who fires at the US or at \u8220\'20\'1Cpeaceful vessels will be blown to hell\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one who pays an illegal toll will have safe passage on the high seas,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that the blockade \u8211\'20\'13 which will involve so far unspecified other countries \u8211\'20\'13 will \u8220\'20\'1Cbegin shortly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIran will not be allowed to profit off this Illegal Act of EXTORTION. They want money and, more importantly, they want Nuclear,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sultan Al Jaber, the chief executive officer of the Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (Adnoc), has said the strait of Hormuz has never been Iran\u8217\'20\'19s to close \u8288\'20\'60or restrict navigation \u8288\'20\'60through.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny attempt to do so is not merely a regional issue, but represents a disruption to a global economic lifeline and a direct threat to the energy, food, and health security of all countries in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SultanAlJaber/status/2043305695505007103"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said in a post on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis behavior is illegal, dangerous, and unacceptable, and the world cannot bear its consequences or allow it to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said at least 22 ships have been targeted and nearly 400 oil tankers stranded since 28 February, when the US and Israel launched their war on Iran by killing the country\u8217\'20\'19s former supreme leader in airstrikes on Tehran.\par \par \uc2 In response to the attacks, Tehran effectively closed the strait of Hormuz to vessels, only allowing a relatively small number of ships from \u8220\'20\'1Cfriendly\u8221\'20\'1D countries like China, Malaysia and Pakistan through.\par \par \uc2 Iranian authorities have since demanded the right to impose tolls on vessels transiting the vital waterway, where roughly 20% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s oil and liquefied natural gas usually passes through, including after the war ends.\par \par \uc2 Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s 10-point ceasefire plan would reportedly permit Iran and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/oman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oman}}}\uc2  to charge a fee of up to $2m (\u163\'00\'A31.5m) a ship on vessels moving through the strait.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports on some of the victims of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strikes on Lebanon:\par \par \uc2 1.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iranians reacted with a mixture of disappointment and defiance on Sunday after peace talks with the US failed to reach an agreement, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Standing outside a newsstand in the capital, Tehran, Farhad Simia said he had hoped for successful negotiations and an end to the fighting, but stood with Iran despite the failure of the talks. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m against war. I think negotiation is the better path,\u8221\'20\'1D Simia, 43, said. He blamed \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate demands\u8221\'20\'1D by the US for the failure to reach a deal.\par \par \uc2 Mehdi Hosseini, also 43, agreed: \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that the Iranian negotiating team managed to preserve what it achieved in the war, while refusing to back down and surrender, gives reason for hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The streets of Tehran were lined up with large Iranian flags and giant billboards glorifying the country\u8217\'20\'19s leaders and military achievements. One large mural depicted Iranian men in uniform lifting a fishing net out of the sea with a catch of miniature-sized US military aircraft and warships. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Strait Remains Closed,\u8221\'20\'1D the billboard read.\par \par \uc2 Hamid Haghi, 55, said \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s overreach\u8221\'20\'1D was the reason for the talks\u8217\'20\'19 failure. The US wants \u8220\'20\'1Cto come to the Strait of Hormuz, which is a legacy from our fathers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can oversee (it) ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like many Iranians, 60-year-old Mohammad Bagher believes Iran should continue to stand strong against the US in what he sees as a war of their own making. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are a nation of dialogue and negotiation as long as our interests are respected. We have never sought war,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will stand firm to the end, we are ready to sacrifice our lives, and will not give them one inch of our land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 12.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a round-up of the key events from the Middle East so far today:\par \par \uc2 * The US failed to gain trust of the Iranian delegation in Pakistan peace talks, Iran\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentary speaker said. Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, said he stressed before the talks yesterday that Iran had no \u8220\'20\'1Ctrust in the opposing side\u8221\'20\'1D after \u8220\'20\'1Cthe experiences of the two previous wars\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Iran\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry downplayed the stalling of negotiations on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CNaturally, from the beginning we should not have expected to reach an agreement in a single session. No one had such an expectation,\u8221\'20\'1D ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei said, according to state broadcaster IRIB.\par \par \uc2 * Strait of Hormuz \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely\u8221\'20\'1D under Iranian control, deputy parliament speaker said. The Iranian deputy parliament speaker, Haji Babaei, has been quoted by the Mehr news agency as having said that the strait of Hormuz is \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely\u8221\'20\'1D under Iranian control, adding that tolls must be paid in the country\u8217\'20\'19s currency, rials.\par \par \uc2 * Saudi Arabia says east-west pipeline, energy facilities restored to \u8220\'20\'1Coperational capacity\u8221\'20\'1D after attacks. \u8220\'20\'1CEnergy facilities and the east-west pipeline damaged by attacks have recovered and regained their operational capacity, enhancing the reliability of supplies,\u8221\'20\'1D the official Saudi Press Agency reported, citing an energy ministry statement.\par \par \uc2 * In a call this morning, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Keir Starmer, and the Sultan of Oman agreed that all sides should avoid \u8220\'20\'1Cany further escalation\u8221\'20\'1D in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/us-israel-war-on-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Israel war on Iran}}}\uc2 . A Downing Street spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey discussed the peace talks held in Pakistan over the weekend and urged both sides to find a way through. It was vital there was a continuation of the ceasefire, and that all parties avoided any further escalation, the leaders agreed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Javad Zarif, a former Iranian foreign minister, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JZarif/status/2043226590751166744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a post on X}}}\uc2  this morning that the Pakistan talks failed because Iran is not going to accept terms dictated to it by the US. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo negotiations \u8211\'20\'13 at least with Iran \u8211\'20\'13 will succeed based on \u8220\'20\'1Cour/your terms.\u8221\'20\'1D The US must learn: you can\u8217\'20\'19t dictate terms to Iran. It\u8217\'20\'19s not too late to learn. Yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 12.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Javad Zarif, a former Iranian foreign minister, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JZarif/status/2043226590751166744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a post on X}}}\uc2  this morning that the Pakistan talks failed because Iran is not going to accept terms dictated to it by the US.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo negotiations \u8211\'20\'13 at least with Iran \u8211\'20\'13 will succeed based on \u8220\'20\'1Cour/your terms.\u8221\'20\'1D The US must learn: you can\u8217\'20\'19t dictate terms to Iran. It\u8217\'20\'19s not too late to learn. Yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zarif, who was Iran\u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat between 2013 and 2021 in the government of the \u8216\'20\'18moderate\u8217\'20\'19 president Hassan Rouhani, was in office when the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/jul/14/iran-nuclear-programme-world-powers-historic-deal-lift-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached its nuclear deal}}}\uc2  with Iran in 2015 under Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump exited the agreement three years later by claiming that Iran was building a nuclear program, without providing evidence to support this claim at the time.\par \par \uc2 11.38am BST\par \par \uc2 In a call this morning, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Keir Starmer, and the Sultan of Oman agreed that all sides should avoid \u8220\'20\'1Cany further escalation\u8221\'20\'1D in the US-Israel war on Iran.\par \par \uc2 A Downing Street spokesperson said:\par \par \uc2 You can read what the health secretary, Wes Streeting, said this morning about the peace talks held in Pakistan over the weekend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/12/middle-east-crisis-live-us-iran-pakistan-peace-talks-jd-vance-delegation-leaves-without-a-deal?page=with%3Ablock-69db49448f08dd48307749bf#block-69db49448f08dd48307749bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.40am BST\par \par \uc2 11.13am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran}}}\uc2  is unable to find the mines it laid in the strait of Hormuz and does not have the capacity to remove the explosives, preventing Iran from allowing more traffic through the waterway, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/10/us/politics/iran-mines-strait.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  reported, citing US officials.\par \par \uc2 Iran laid mines in the strait of Hormuz last month after the US and Israel declared war against the country, dropping explosives throughout the waterway with small boats.\par \par \uc2 The US was mostly unable to monitor the small boats that were mining the strait, leaving the country uncertain about the location and number of mines in the waterway.\par \par \uc2 Maritime traffic through the strait ground almost to a standstill due to the mines, as well as Iranian drones and missiles that threatened to hit ships. A senior Revolutionary Guards official said on 2 March the country would set ships \u8220\'20\'1Cablaze\u8221\'20\'1D if they tried to traverse the strait.\par \par \uc2 A small number of ships have continued to pass through after being given the go-ahead by Iran, which allowed through vessels from friendly nations that paid tolls.\par \par \uc2 US officials have said that Iran placed mines in the strait erratically, and may not have marked where it put all of them. Some mines also drifted or moved from their original location, US officials suggested.\par \par \uc2 Neither Iran nor the US have the capacity to quickly demine the strait, particularly after the US destroyed much of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s navy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/iran-us-strait-of-hormuz-mines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US officials claim Iran unable to find mines it laid in strait of Hormuz, report says}}}\par \par \uc2 10.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Strait of Hormuz 'completely' under Iranian control, deputy parliament speaker says\par \par \uc2 The Iranian deputy parliament speaker, Haji Babaei, has been quoted by the Mehr news agency as having said that the strait of Hormuz is \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely\u8221\'20\'1D under Iranian control, adding that tolls must be paid in the country\u8217\'20\'19s currency, rials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C250 members of parliament unanimously supported the strait of Hormuz plan, and according to the leadership formula, this strategic waterway is non-negotiable under any circumstances,\u8221\'20\'1D he was quoted as having said. \u8220\'20\'1CDespite sanctions, Iran\u8217\'20\'19s oil exports have exceeded 1.6 million barrels, and today our country\u8217\'20\'19s oil has become practically non-sanctionable. The Iranian nation will not back down from its demands even an inch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The opening of the strait \u8211\'20\'13 a chokepoint for a fifth of the world\u8217\'20\'19s oil supply \u8211\'20\'13 for all vessels (not just those deemed friendly by Iran) is a primary demand of the US to end the war and forms a key part of the conditional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/08/iran-10-point-plan-ceasefire-donald-trump-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-week ceasefire plan agreed with Iran last week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The virtual closure of the strait has sent fuel prices soaring and threatens to hurt Republican electoral fortunes in the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 US military officials on Saturday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CENTCOM/status/2043005033600479516"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that their forces \u8220\'20\'1Cbegan setting conditions for clearing mines in the strait\u8221\'20\'1D, with two navy guided-missile destroyers said to be conducting operations. Iran, which closed the strait in response to the US and Israel attacking the country on 28 February, has denied that the two vessels sailed through the area.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.53am BST\par \par \uc2 10.30am BST\par \par \uc2 US failed to gain trust of Iranian delegation in Pakistan peace talks, parliamentary speaker says\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentary speaker, Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, said the US delegation \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed to gain the trust of the Iranian delegation in this round of negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mb_ghalibaf/status/2043251931124990055"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a lengthy post on X}}}\uc2 , the speaker said he stressed before the talks yesterday that Iran had no \u8220\'20\'1Ctrust in the opposing side\u8221\'20\'1D after \u8220\'20\'1Cthe experiences of the two previous wars\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ghalibaf, who led the Iranian delegation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/us-iran-talks-peace-deal-islamabad-pakistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the Pakistani mediated talks with the US in Islamabad}}}\uc2 , added that his country\u8217\'20\'19s delegation negotiated in good faith and raised \u8220\'20\'1Cforward-looking initiatives\u8221\'20\'1D, without specifying what these were.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica has understood our logic and principles, and now it\u8217\'20\'19s time for it to decide whether it can earn our trust or not?\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on social media, as he thanked Pakistan for its mediation efforts.\par \par \uc2 Iranian state media reported earlier that major points of disagreement included Iran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear program and transit through the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 10.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The internet blackout in Iran has entered its 44th day, according to internet monitoring group NetBlocks. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/netblocks/status/2043231585269408086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a social media post}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Those without access to Starlink or alternative ways to communicate \u8211\'20\'13 which are often expensive \u8211\'20\'13 are cut off, not only from the outside world but the blackout also severely curtails Iranian\u8217\'20\'19s ability to communicate with each other, making mobilisation, for example, much more difficult.\par \par \uc2 A select number of officials are still able to use the internet and post regularly on social media about the war. There was an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jan/28/iran-appears-to-ease-internet-blackout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier internet shutdown in January}}}\uc2  during nationwide protests, which helped obscure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/jan/27/iran-protests-death-toll-disappeared-bodies-mass-burials-30000-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme violence against Iran\u8217\'20\'19s population}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 9.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The Fars news agency, which is close to the Iranian security services, is reporting that 21 people have been killed and 13 others injured in Israeli attacks on Lebanon since this morning.\par \par \uc2 Attacks have been reported across southern Lebanon including in the towns of Qana and Maaroub. We have not been able to independently verify this information yet.\par \par \uc2 8.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Over in the UK, the health secretary, Wes Streeting, has said the failure to reach a deal in the US-Iran peace talks in Pakistan was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointing\u8221\'20\'1D. He told Sky News this morning:\par \par \uc2 The UK, which has been hit hard by rising bills resulting from the economic impact of the war, has been working on a \u8220\'20\'1Cpractical plan\u8221\'20\'1D to try to reopen the strait of Hormuz (to all vessels).\par \par \uc2 8.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Six people have been killed in an Israeli attack on the town of Maaroub in southern Lebanon, according to the country\u8217\'20\'19s national news agency.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military has demolished entire villages as part of its invasion of south {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2 , with airstrikes killing many civilians and damaging civilian infrastructure despite the IDF saying they are only targeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hezbollah}}}\uc2  infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 The renewed Israeli assault on Lebanon was launched on 2 March when Hezbollah, the Iranian backed Lebanese militant group, launched rocket fire at Israel after US-Israeli airstrikes killed former Iranian supreme leader, Ali Khamenei.\par \par \uc2 The US is due to host talks between Israel and Lebanon next week. Israeli prime minister, Benjamin Netanyahu, said he has given \u8220\'20\'1Capproval\u8221\'20\'1D for negotiations on two conditions: Hezbollah dismantling their weapons and \u8220\'20\'1Ca real peace agreement that will last for generations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.43am BST\par \par \uc2 8.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Saudi says east-west pipeline, energy facilities restored to 'operational capacity' after attacks\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s energy ministry said on Sunday that its key east-west oil pipeline and other facilities had been restored following attacks by Iran on infrastructure across the Gulf, news agency AFP reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnergy facilities and the east-west pipeline damaged by attacks have recovered and regained their operational capacity, enhancing the reliability of supplies,\u8221\'20\'1D the official Saudi Press Agency reported, citing an energy ministry statement.\par \par \uc2 It added that the attacks had led to a \u8220\'20\'1Closs of approximately 700,000 barrels per day of pumping capacity through the east-west pipeline\u8221\'20\'1D and work was underway to restore full production capacity at the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s Khurais oil field.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.37am BST\par \par \uc2 7.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Tehran says no one had expectation of reaching agreement with US in one session: Iran state TV\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry has downplayed the stalling of negotiations on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNaturally, from the beginning we should not have expected to reach an agreement in a single session. No one had such an expectation,\u8221\'20\'1D ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei\par \par \uc2 said, according to state broadcaster IRIB.\par \par \uc2 He said Tehran was \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident that contacts between us and Pakistan, as well as our other friends in the region, will continue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You can read more about the abrupt end to the talks here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/jd-vance-says-no-deal-us-iran-pakistan-talks-islamabad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance and US delegation leave Pakistan after failing to reach deal with Iran}}}\par \par \uc2 7.06am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Everything is gone\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 William Christou,\par \par \uc2 Abbas Abdel Karim and Lucy Swan have reported today on Israel destroying entire villages as part of its invasion of southern Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian reviewed three videos posted by the Israeli military and on social media, which showed Israel carrying out mass detonations in the villages of Taybeh, Naqoura and Deir Seryan along the Israel-Lebanon border.\par \par \uc2 Rights groups fear the tactic of \u8220\'20\'1Cdomicide\u8221\'20\'1D trialled in Gaza, where entire areas are made uninhabitable, is being used again.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military has said they are targeting Hezbollah infrastructure such as tunnels and military facilities, which it claims the armed group has embedded in civilian homes, through these demolitions.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/how-israeli-offensive-destroyed-entire-villages-in-lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8216\'20\'18Everything is gone\u8217\'20\'19: Israel destroys entire villages in Lebanon}}}\par \par \uc2 7.00am BST\par \par \uc2 IDF claims strike on rocket launcher in Lebanon that was 'ready to launch' toward Israel\par \par \uc2 A post about an hour ago on the Israel Defense Forces Telegram channel claimed that overnight, the IDF \u8220\'20\'1Cidentified a rocket launcher positioned and ready to launch toward the State of Israel in the area of Jouaiyya in southern Lebanon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The post included what the IDF said was footage of the strike, which the Guardian was not able to immediately verify.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/11/middle-east-crisis-live-iranian-officials-arrive-in-islamabad-for-conditional-peace-talks-with-us?page=with%3Ablock-69dab76b8f08dd4830774769#block-69dab76b8f08dd4830774769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an earlier update from Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry}}}\uc2 , recent Israeli attacks have pushed the death toll in Lebanon to more than 2,000, with at least 6,300 wounded.\par \par \uc2 6.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attends UFC fight as Middle East peace talks stall\par \par \uc2 As US negotiations with Iran were hitting an impasse, the US president attended a UFC fight, Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump entered the Miami venue alongside UFC president Dana White and several members of the Trump family soon after 9pm local time. As a Kid Rock song blasted from the speakers, Trump walked to his seat, where secretary of state Marco Rubio was waiting. Also nearby was Sergio Gor, the US ambassador to India.\par \par \uc2 Vance announced less than half an hour later, at around 6.30am in Islamabad, that US and Iranian negotiating teams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/jd-vance-says-no-deal-us-iran-pakistan-talks-islamabad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had failed to reach a peace deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NYT White House correspondent Katie Rogers, who noted via her colleague Tyler Pager on Air Force Two that officials were deferring to Trump for \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther comment about what is next for the US war with Iran\u8221\'20\'1D, said Trump remained at the Miami arena until at least 11.28pm local time.\par \par \uc2 5.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump shares article highlighting possibility of naval blockade\par \par \uc2 The US president, Donald Trump, has not yet formally commented on the breakdown of peace talks with Iran in Islamabad. But he just shared a link {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/116389798405349626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a post on his Truth Social platform}}}\uc2 , to an article titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump card the president holds if Iran won\u8217\'20\'19t bend: a naval blockade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The article \u8211\'20\'13 by John Solomon, a controversial veteran US journalist, and published on Solomon\u8217\'20\'19s conservative Just the News website \u8211\'20\'13 cites experts who suggest Trump \u8220\'20\'1Csimply could out-blockade Iran\u8217\'20\'19s hold over the Strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.42am BST\par \par \uc2 5.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign affairs minister,\par \par \uc2 Penny Wong, says it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointing\u8221\'20\'1D that peace talks have failed between the US and Iran, but has urged parties to return to negotiations as a matter of priority.\par \par \uc2 5.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Iranian foreign ministry has commented on the negotiations in Islamabad, saying the talks were conducted in an atmosphere of mistrust, and it was unrealistic to believe an agreement could be reached in one session, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Contact and consultation between Iran, Pakistan and other allies in the region would continue going forward, the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Pakistan foreign minister says 'imperative' for ceasefire to be upheld\par \par \uc2 Pakistan\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister Ishaq Darinsisted on Sunday that Washington and Tehran must uphold a ceasefire agreement, after marathon talks between the two sides to end the war in the Middle East ended without an agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is imperative that the parties continue to uphold their commitment to ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 4.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo XIV himself stepped into the international political arena yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/pope-leo-us-israel-iran-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Edward Helmore reported}}}\uc2 , saying \u8220\'20\'1Cenough of war\u8221\'20\'1D and decrying the \u8220\'20\'1Cdelusion of omnipotence\u8221\'20\'1D that drives leaders into global conflict, at evening prayers in St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica in Vatican City.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/pope-leo-us-israel-iran-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope says \u8216\'20\'18enough of war\u8217\'20\'19 and decries \u8216\'20\'18delusion of omnipotence\u8217\'20\'19 at peace vigil}}}\par \par \uc2 4.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Cardinal Robert McElroy, the archbishop of Washington and a close ally of Pope Leo XIV, has called for Catholics to take civic action against the \u8220\'20\'1Cimmoral\u8221\'20\'1D war on Iran.\par \par \uc2 Reporter Christopher Hale, whose Substack chronicles the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with the papacy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/christopherhale/status/2043144621912428789"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared a video of the archbishops\u8217\'20\'19s address}}}\uc2 , in which McElroy called for his congregation to \u8220\'20\'1Cmove beyond prayer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What makes this especially interesting, a colleague of mine points out, is that JD Vance, who less than two hours ago led the US exit from peace talks with Iran, converted to Catholicism in 2019.\par \par \uc2 He recently announced a new memoir on the subject, which you can read more about here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/apr/01/jd-vance-new-memoir-book-catholicism-communion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance announces a new memoir about his conversion to Catholicism}}}\par \par \uc2 4.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s semi-official Tasnim news agency is citing an \u8220\'20\'1Cinformed source\u8221\'20\'1D saying Iran is in no hurry to negotiate, Reuters reports \u8211\'20\'13 and that as long as the US does not agree to a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable deal\u8221\'20\'1D, there will be no change in situation in the strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 As William Christou {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/iran-us-strait-of-hormuz-mines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2 , the opening of the strait of Hormuz \u8211\'20\'13 a chokepoint for a fifth of the world\u8217\'20\'19s oil supply \u8211\'20\'13 is a primary demand of the US to end the war in Iran.\par \par \uc2 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, and welcome to our live coverage of events in the Middle East, as US-Iran peace talks in Islamabad seemingly broke down on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 After a marathon 21-hour first day of talks, US vice-president JD Vance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/12/jd-vance-says-no-deal-us-iran-pakistan-talks-islamabad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on Sunday}}}\uc2  that his negotiating team was leaving Pakistan without reaching a deal.\par \par \uc2 Vance said Iran had chosen not to accept American terms, including a commitment to not build nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Iranian state media said the talks had failed due to the US\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cunreasonable demands\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If you are just joining us, here is a quick recap of the latest updates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/11/middle-east-crisis-live-iranian-officials-arrive-in-islamabad-for-conditional-peace-talks-with-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the past few hours}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 * High-stakes negotiations between the US and Iran appeared to break down on Sunday, despite the historic and face-to-face meetings marking the highest-level direct engagement between Washington and Tehran in decades. The talks in Pakistan were aimed at securing a peace agreement to end the weeks-long war. The core US delegation was led by Vance, who has now left Pakistan.\par \par \uc2 * The Iranian foreign ministry had warned earlier that the\par \par \uc2 success of this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s talks depended on Washington avoiding \u8220\'20\'1Cexcessive demands\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful requests\u8221\'20\'1D. Among issues discussed were the strategic strait of Hormuz, nuclear development, war reparations, and sanctions.\par \par \uc2 * The strait of Hormuz remains among the main points of \u8220\'20\'1Cserious disagreement\u8221\'20\'1D, Iran\u8217\'20\'19s semi-official Tasnim news agency reported on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 * Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Saturday that Israel remains committed to keep fighting Iran. \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael under my leadership will continue to fight Iran\u8217\'20\'19s terror regime and its proxies,\u8221\'20\'1D Netanyahu wrote on social media. Israel was not present at the US-Iran talks.\par \par \uc2 * Donald Trump told reporters outside the White House that it made \u8220\'20\'1Cno difference\u8221\'20\'1D to him if a deal was reached with Iran. \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of what happens, we win,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether we make a deal or not, makes no difference to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The latest Israeli attacks on Lebanon have pushed the death toll to more than 2,000 with more than 6,300 wounded, according to the health ministry. Earlier, the Iranian negotiators demanded a ceasefire in Lebanon, reparations and commitment to unblock frozen assets as part of a peace deal in a preliminary meeting with Pakistani mediators.\par \par \uc2 * The US military says it \u8220\'20\'1Cbegan setting conditions for clearing mines in the strait of Hormuz\u8221\'20\'1D in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/11/iran-us-strait-of-hormuz-mines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an update released on Saturday afternoon}}}\uc2 , saying two navy destroyers had transited the strait. A spokesperson for Iran\u8217\'20\'19s joint military command later denied the claim by the US military that the navy destroyers transited the waterway.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260412em4c000gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
