\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 xAI\uc2  sues Colorado over new rules for artificial intelligence\b0\par\par\uc2 Dara Kerr \par \uc2 413 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2026\par 14:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company claims law regulating AI systems, set to go into effect in June, infringes on its first amendment rights\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s artificial intelligence company, \uc2 xAI\uc2 , has filed a lawsuit against the state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\uc2  over a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI}}}\uc2  law set to take effect in June.\par \par \uc2 The suit seeks to block the state from enforcing the law, which would impose new requirements on AI systems to protect state residents from \u8220\'20\'1Calgorithmic discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D in sectors such as education, employment, healthcare, housing and financial services.\par \par \uc2 Colorado was the first state to pass a comprehensive bill to regulate AI.\par \par \uc2 The company claims the law infringes on its first amendment free-speech protections and would force \uc2 xAI\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote the state\u8217\'20\'19s ideological views on various matters, racial justice in particular\u8221\'20\'1D, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/55e8cba9-d09c-4f94-b710-4ab447b987f9?syn-25a6b1a6=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Financial Times}}}\uc2 , which first reported the lawsuit. \u8220\'20\'1CIts provisions prohibit developers of AI systems from producing speech that the state of Colorado dislikes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in US district court in Colorado, comes as battles have raged at the state and federal level over how to regulate the fast-growing technology. States such as California and New York have been working to rein in AI with regulations, while the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has been trying to loosen the rules and place a moratorium on state laws.\par \par \uc2 xAI\uc2 , which makes the chatbot Grok, has been plagued with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jul/09/grok-ai-praised-hitler-antisemitism-x-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusations}}}\uc2  of discrimination. The chatbot has consistently spewed racist, sexist and antisemitic content, put forth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/12/elon-musk-grok-ai-trump-2020-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspiracies}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/14/elon-musk-grok-white-genocide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white genocide}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and referred to itself as \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jul/15/x-esafety-ai-chatbot-grok-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MechaHitler}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Katie Miller, a former spokesperson for \uc2 xAI\uc2  and the wife of Trump adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , heralded the lawsuit in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KatieMiller/status/2042351880815423592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2  on Thursday: \u8220\'20\'1CColorado wants to force Grok to follow its views on equity and race, instead of being maximally truth-seeking. Grok answers to evidence, not woke leftist government regulations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2 , Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, signed the bill into law in 2024 but said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cwith reservations\u8221\'20\'1D. He has called on state legislators to amend it. The legislation was intended to go into effect in February, but was pushed until 30 June.\par \par \uc2 xAI\uc2 , which merged with Musk\u8217\'20\'19s rocket business \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  earlier this year, is seeking an injunction to block the enforcement of the Colorado law and a court declaration saying the legislation is unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 The Colorado attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office declined to comment on the lawsuit and \uc2 xAI\uc2  did not return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260410em4a000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
