\par\par \uc2 Food\par \b \uc2 Five Guys\uc2  CEO says he gave a $1.5m bonus to his workers so he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get shot in the back\b0\par\par\uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas \par \uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2026\par 17:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jerry Murrell seemingly alluded to healthcare CEO killing when he explained giving bonus to workers after bungled promotionSign up for the Breaking News US email to get newsletter alerts in your inbox\par \par \uc2 Five Guys\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 chief executive officer, Jerry Murrell, said he gave a $1.5m bonus to employees of his US-based burger restaurant chain because \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t want anybody shooting me\u8221\'20\'1D after the company recently \u8220\'20\'1Cscrewed \u8230\'20\'26 up\u8221\'20\'1D a buy-one-get-one-free promotion.\par \par \uc2 Murrell did not elaborate on the comment, which he gave to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2026/03/25/five-guys-ceo-jerry-murrell-bonus-employees-bogo-burger/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fortune}}}\uc2  in an interview published on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 but it came a little more than a year after the UnitedHealthcare CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  was shot dead on a midtown Manhattan street in what was widely considered a murderous rebuke of the US health insurance industry\u8217\'20\'19s profit-driven practices.\par \par \uc2 Fortune\u8217\'20\'19s conversation with Murrell revisited a two-for-one promotion that \uc2 Five Guys\uc2  organized in February to celebrate its 40th anniversary that proved to be much more popular than the chain expected. \uc2 Five Guys\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 app crashed as customers sought to take advantage of the promotion, and many overwhelmed chain locations discontinued the offer early, inviting backlash on social media.\par \par \uc2 That criticism was intense enough that \uc2 Five Guys\uc2  apologized in a statement on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiveguys.com/news/blog/were-sorry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 18 February}}}\uc2  and then a follow-up note on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiveguys.com/news/press-release/five-guys-welcomes-guests-to-40th-birthday-after-party/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 9 March}}}\uc2 , when it restarted the promotion for four days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe let you down, and we\u8217\'20\'19re sorry,\u8221\'20\'1D read the first of those apologies, which also expressed regret for having placed the chain\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chardworking crews \u8230\'20\'26 in a difficult situation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The second statement told customers: \u8220\'20\'1CYou visited our restaurants in overwhelming numbers, and we weren\u8217\'20\'19t ready for you. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t meet our own standards, and that\u8217\'20\'19s not something we take lightly. So we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for a do-over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the conversation with Fortune, Murrell added that he gave a $1.5m bonus to employees of \uc2 Five Guys\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 1,500 US stores to try to make up for the chaos unleashed by the promotion at various locations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t want anybody shooting me in the back or anything \u8230\'20\'26 because we really screwed it up,\u8221\'20\'1D Murrell said to the publication. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had no idea that we were going to get that kind of response.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Murrell joked that he preferred the employees receiving the bonus over his wife getting \u8220\'20\'1Ca new fur coat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe still looks at me like I\u8217\'20\'19m stupid, but I thought it was worth it,\u8221\'20\'1D Murrell was quoted as saying by Fortune. \u8220\'20\'1CThey worked so hard. They were so overwhelmed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luigi Mangione is charged with murdering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/brian-thompson-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thompson}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 UnitedHealthcare\uc2  CEO, who was shot in the back and killed on 4 December 2024. Mangione has been awaiting trial in both state and federal courthouses after a manhunt in connection with Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s killing led to his arrest at a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s restaurant in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Five Guys\uc2  did not immediately respond to a request for comment on Murrell\u8217\'20\'19s remarks to Fortune.\par \par \uc2 Globally, \uc2 Five Guys\uc2  has 1,900 locations and 30,000 employees in 28 countries, according to the chain\u8217\'20\'19s website. Murrell founded the company in 1986 in Arlington, Virginia, and has led it since.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260327em3r004xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
