\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 $30 an hour by 2030: new pushes to increase minimum wage in New York and California\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,256 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2026\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oakland and New York campaigns for $30 minimum wage gain steam as workers battle high costs and pushback\par \par \uc2 Mark Dorsey, a lifelong East Oakland resident, works two jobs to make ends meet. The 35-year-old Californian relies on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/manufacturing-sector+useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 manufacturing}}}\uc2  and service work through temp agencies and tries to work overtime or 10- to 12-hour shifts because \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s the only way you can see a paycheck that\u8217\'20\'19s worth something\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dorsey often makes minimum wage or close to it. The city of Oakland\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oaklandca.gov/Government/Departments/Workplace-Employment-Standards/Download-Minimum-Wage-and-Hotel-Wage-Posters#:~:text=The%20minimum%20wage%20in%20Oakland%2C%20California%20will,English%20*%20Spanish%20*%20Chinese%20*%20Vietnamese"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $17.34 an hour}}}\uc2 , higher than the minimum wage for the state of California, currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dir.ca.gov/dlse/minimum_wage.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $16.90 an hour}}}\uc2 , but still not enough to support Dorsey.\par \par \uc2 Now, he is part of a campaign to almost double California\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage to $30. The drive comes as New York City has a bill tabled to increase its hourly minimum to $30 an hour, backed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/zohran-mamdani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Zohran Mamdani}}}\uc2 , the mayor.\par \par \uc2 The initiatives face powerful opposition from business interests and come against a background of political inaction. Despite widespread public support for minimum wage increases, the federal minimum wage still sits at $7.25 an hour, a rate last increased in 2009.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been more than 10 years since the \u8220\'20\'1CFight for $15\u8221\'20\'1D movement galvanized workers across the US to strike for a higher minimum wage. The movement helped push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/minimum-wage-tracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wages higher}}}\uc2  in 30 states. But in the meantime, inflation has hit low-wage workers hard.\par \par \uc2 The Oakland and Alameda Living Wage for All campaign, launched this month, filed two ballot initiatives for the November 2026 ballot to increase the minimum wage for the city of Oakland and Alameda county, California, to $30 an hour by 2030 for large employers.\par \par \uc2 Dorsey is a member if the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blackorganizingproject.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black Organizing Project}}}\uc2 , a grassroots organization that advances racial, social and economic justice for Black communities in Oakland and beyond.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have time to do anything on your own when you\u8217\'20\'19re working so hard, but this $30 an hour minimum wage would take a lot of burden and stress off of people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dorsey. \u8220\'20\'1CI do a lot of jobs. I go to temp agencies to keep my options open so I can continue to stay above water with paying bills. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been working off of 98th avenue in Oakland all this week and next week, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be in San Francisco all week. I just have to go where the money is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zach Norris, co-executive director of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blackorganizingproject.org/about-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black Organizing Project}}}\uc2 , said the ballot initiatives to increase the minimum wage in Oakland and Alameda county are also racial justice issues. Oakland has seen a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.ucla.edu/stories/state-of-black-california-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 46% decline}}}\uc2  of Black residents since 2000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about making sure that people who work here are able to afford to live here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Norris. \u8220\'20\'1CBlack folks have been pushed out of the Bay Area given the extremely high cost of living. For us, this is an existential issue, not just a wage issue. It\u8217\'20\'19s whether or not we can afford to stay in the Bay Area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He dismissed criticism of raising minimum wage by business groups, noting that small businesses backed the ballot initiatives when they were announced at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://understoryoakland.com/about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Understory}}}\uc2 , a worker-owned restaurant in Oakland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ballot initiative is structured such that those who can most afford to make this change are being asked to do so most immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D said Norris. \u8220\'20\'1CThe largest employers are being called upon to raise wages the soonest, which puts more money into the local economy the fastest, so that increased spending power really flows directly into small businesses and neighborhoods.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Community and labor groups are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/newsletter/2025-11-19/essential-california-30-minimum-wage-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2  for the Los Angeles county board of supervisors to take up a proposal to increase the minimum wage to $30 an hour, from the current minimum wage of{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dcba.lacounty.gov/workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $17.81 }}}\uc2 an hour, set to increase to $18.47 an hour on 1 July 2026.\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hoteldive.com/news/la-passed-a-30-minimum-wage-for-hospitality-workers-hotels-continue-to-fi/754168/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has already passed}}}\uc2  a $30 an hour wage increase for hotel and airport service workers by 2028, in time for the 2028 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles, as business industry groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitalandmain.com/business-groups-failed-to-stop-l-a-s-olympic-wage-increase-but-the-battles-not-over#:~:text=The%20minimum%20wage%20for%20hotel,Games%20are%20scheduled%20to%20commence."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to stop}}}\uc2  the increase.\par \par \uc2 In New York City, Sandy Nurse, a councilmember, recently introduced a bill to increase New York City\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage to $30 an hour by 2030 for large employers, giving small businesses more time, by 2032, to catch up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe cost of living is crushing New York City workers,\u8221\'20\'1D Nurse said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe current minimum wage is $17 an hour, and after taxes, that means those workers are trying to make do with about $500 a week, which is nearly impossible for most workers, even with shared expenses, even with cramming your life into a tiny apartment with a bunch of other people, it\u8217\'20\'19s astronomically challenging.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She cited a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2026/02/26/us-news/one-third-of-new-yorkers-want-to-flee-ny-survey-shows/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  that found one in three New Yorkers plan to leave the state in the next five years due to the high cost of living, and noted that other US cities have higher minimum wages than New York City.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe looked at other cities, Seattle, San Francisco, Denver, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flagstaff.az.gov/3520/Minimum-Wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Flagstaff, Arizona}}}\uc2 , they all have taken action to raise the minimum wage, and their cities are less expensive to live in than ours. So we feel that New York is behind,\u8221\'20\'1D added Nurse. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve done this before. We doubled the minimum wage in between 2013 and 2019 and we think it\u8217\'20\'19s time to do that again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mamdani {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cityandstateny.com/policy/2025/02/mamdani-unveils-30-30-minimum-wage-push-part-mayoral-campaign/403015/#:~:text=Assembly%20Member%20Zohran%20Mamdani%2C%20a%20Democratic%20socialist,cost%20of%20living%20increases%20or%20productivity%20increases."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran}}}\uc2  on a platform that included raising the city\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage to $30 an hour by 2030. New York City\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ny.gov/new-york-states-minimum-wage/new-york-states-minimum-wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $17 an hour}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Economic Policy Institute {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/a-30-by-2030-minimum-wage-in-new-york-city-is-a-bold-proposal-the-first-step-is-giving-the-city-the-freedom-to-set-its-own-wage-floor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 projects}}}\uc2  1.68 million New York City residents, 36.7% of the city\u8217\'20\'19s wage-earning workforce, will earn less than $30 an hour by 2030.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://livingwage.mit.edu/metros/35620"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MIT\u8217\'20\'19s living wage calculator,}}}\uc2  a living wage for a single adult with no dependents in New York City is currently $31.50 an hour.\par \par \uc2 Business groups in New York City have already voiced staunch opposition against the bill, and the state government may have to approve a minimum wage increase for the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a raise for workers. It is a closing notice for businesses,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jessica Walker, president and CEO of the Manhattan chamber of commerce, in a statement on the proposed bill. \u8220\'20\'1CWe share the goal of a city where working people can live with dignity. But the path to that goal requires a thriving private sector.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 2023 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.berkeley.edu/2023/03/14/even-in-small-businesses-minimum-wage-hikes-dont-cause-job-losses-study-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study }}}\uc2 co-authored by Michael Reich, a University of California, Berkeley economist, found minimum wage increases do not result in job losses or small business closures, rather the increases kill job vacancies and reduce turnover, similar to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/most-minimum-wage-studies-have-found-little-or-no-job-loss/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most minimum wage study findings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nurse dismissed the criticisms of the proposal, citing similar claims were made over previous wage increases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom 2013 to 2019, over a six year period, we raised the minimum wage from $7.25 to $15 an hour, more than double. New York businesses are still here,\u8221\'20\'1D Nurse concluded. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is that every time we try to do good by workers, there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be people who say we\u8217\'20\'19re going to end the world. This is not true, because we\u8217\'20\'19ve done it before and we are going to do it again. If we don\u8217\'20\'19t have workers, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have consumers, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have businesses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260327em3r002h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
