\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Baltimore sues \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s AI company over Grok\u8217\'20\'19s fake nude images\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early \par \uc2 529 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 March 2026\par 13:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit argues \uc2 XAI\uc2  failed to disclose risks, limitations and exposure to harm that come with using chatbot\par \par \uc2 The mayor and city council of Baltimore, Maryland, filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 xAI\uc2  company on Tuesday, alleging that its Grok chatbot violated consumer protections by generating nonconsensual sexualized images.\par \par \uc2 Baltimore\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit argues that \uc2 xAI\uc2  deceptively marketed Grok as a general-purpose AI assistant and X as a mainstream social media site, failing to disclose the risks, limitations and exposure to harm that come with using the platform and chatbot. The suit, filed in the circuit court for Baltimore city, argues that the court has jurisdiction over \uc2 xAI\uc2  given that the company advertises and operates in Baltimore.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGrok has flooded the feeds of Baltimore\u8217\'20\'19s X users with NCII (non-consensual intimate imagery) and CSAM (child sexual abuse material),\u8221\'20\'1D the city\u8217\'20\'19s complaint states. \u8220\'20\'1CGrok further exposed Baltimore residents to the risk that any photograph they uploaded \u8211\'20\'13 of themselves or of their children \u8211\'20\'13 could be ingested by Grok and transformed into sexually degrading deepfakes without their knowledge or consent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 xAI\uc2  did not immediately return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 xAI\uc2  has faced multiple lawsuits and international investigations over its Grok AI product in recent months, following a period when the chatbot generated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/ng-interactive/2026/jan/11/how-grok-nudification-tool-went-viral-x-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millions of AI-altered sexualized images}}}\uc2  earlier this year. Many of these sexualized images were created using photos of women without their consent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://counterhate.com/research/grok-floods-x-with-sexualized-images/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to researchers}}}\uc2  at the Center for Countering Digital Hate, which also estimated that Grok produced about 23,000 sexualized images of children over an 11-day period in December and January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re talking about tech companies enabling the sexual exploitation of children. Our city will not stand by and allow this to continue; it\u8217\'20\'19s a threat to privacy, dignity, and public safety, and those responsible must be held accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D the Baltimore mayor, \uc2 Brandon Scott\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Musk has denied any knowledge of Grok producing child sexual abuse material, stating in January that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot aware of any naked underage images generated by Grok. Literally zero.\u8221\'20\'1D The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jan/09/grok-image-generator-outcry-sexualised-ai-imagery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added restrictions to Grok\u8217\'20\'19s image generation}}}\uc2  capabilities in earlier January following backlash and threats of regulatory action from multiple countries.\par \par \uc2 Baltimore\u8217\'20\'19s case is unique in that it is alleging violations of city ordinance and consumer protection, as opposed to other suits brought by individual users claiming personal and reputational harms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe city is setting a powerful example for municipalities nationwide in confronting a novel and rapidly advancing technology \u8211\'20\'13 and an emerging area of law \u8211\'20\'13 where accountability has not yet caught up with innovation,\u8221\'20\'1D Adam Levitt, an attorney representing Baltimore in the case, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In another case against \uc2 xAI\uc2  filed earlier this month, three Tennessee teenage girls alleged that Grok used photos of them to create and distribute child sexual abuse material. The class-action lawsuit was the first filed by minors following Grok\u8217\'20\'19s nonconsensual image generation scandal, and alleged that a third-party app used \uc2 xAI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s technology to generate fully nude images of the girls which were then shared online.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260324em3o0050l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
