\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 TSA workers try to survive second shutdown and ICE influx: \u8216\'20\'18We need to be paid\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 843 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2026\par 16:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers are \u8216\'20\'18in the middle of chaos from political games\u8217\'20\'19 as Senate Republicans try to negotiate with Democrats to reopen DHSSign up for the Breaking News US email to get newsletter alerts in your inbox\par \par \uc2 Workers with the \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  (TSA) are reeling from the White House\u8217\'20\'19s deployment of immigration law enforcement into airports as TSA workers enter their sixth week without pay as the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) shutdown continues.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/400-tsa-officers-quit-shutdown-rcna264581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 400}}}\uc2  TSA workers have quit since the shutdown began in February, with major US airports reporting high call-out rates among workers, leading to longer security wait times. On Sunday, more than, 3,450 TSA officers called out of work, with as many as 40% of officers at some airports calling out that day, according to DHS data.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans are still trying to work with the White House to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5797166-trump-homeland-security-funding-deal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiate}}}\uc2  a deal with Democrats to reopen the DHS. To help with the TSA staffing issues, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/23/us-airports-latest-tsa-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent}}}\uc2  Immigration and Customers Enforcement (ICE) officers to 14 different airports on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2 , which represents TSA workers, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/afge-president-everett-kelley-slams-president-trumps-threat-to-deploy-ice-to-airports-to-perform-passenger-security-functions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Sunday that these ICE agents are unqualified to do the same jobs as TSA officers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CICE agents are not trained or certified in aviation security. TSA officers spend months learning to detect explosives, weapons and threats specifically designed to evade detection at checkpoints \u8211\'20\'13 skills that require specialized instruction, hands-on practice and ongoing recertification,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , the \uc2 AFGE\uc2  president. \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot improvise that. Putting untrained personnel at security checkpoints does not fill a gap. It creates one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Antoinette Wade, president of \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  Local 1047 that represents TSA workers in Louisiana and Mississippi and a TSA officer in Jackson, Mississippi, said the influx of ICE agents has deflated TSA workers, especially as ICE agents continue to be paid during the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt definitely impacts morale when were are expected to show up to work every day and fulfill the duties and the missions that we love and support, keeping the public safe, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not being paid,\u8221\'20\'1D Wade said. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people are skeptical about it and definitely offended by it. Basically, we need to be paid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Congress said they will not fund DHS until Republicans agree to ICE reforms after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s immigration enforcement operations resulted in the killing of two unarmed US citizens in Minnesota in January, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newjerseymonitor.com/2026/03/03/judge-issues-criminal-contempt-threat-over-ignored-immigration-orders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addition}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/20/trump-administration-immigration-ice-judge-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusations }}}\uc2 from federal judges that the agency has been recklessly violating the law and court orders.\par \par \uc2 Though \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, spoke with Trump on Sunday about a bipartisan deal that would fund DHS except for ICE, leaving the agency to be funded by a reconciliation bill later this year, Trump rejected the deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/32326-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  Punchbowl News.\par \par \uc2 Wade said TSA workers were still recovering from the earlier government shutdown in the fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people took out loans, maxed out credit cards, did what they had to do to survive during that time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had to catch up on all of our bills right in the peak of the holiday season. So people are still paying back some of those loans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That shutdown lasted for 43 days, but Wade noted backpay wasn\u8217\'20\'19t processed for several days after the shutdown ended. Now workers again don\u8217\'20\'19t know how long this shutdown is going to last and when they will eventually be paid.\par \par \uc2 She emphasized that the high cost of gas recently and family members also feeling the economic impacts of rising prices of goods have made it more difficult for TSA workers to work unpaid again during another shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis shutdown definitely feels a lot different, more intense, and it feels like it\u8217\'20\'19s coming quicker, and the anxiety and the stress is coming quicker than last time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re just in the middle of all the chaos from these political games; meanwhile, our livelihoods are at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lauren Bis, the acting DHS assistant secretary, blamed Democrats for the shutdown in a statement, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis pointless, reckless shutdown of our homeland security workforce has caused more than 400 TSA officers to quit and thousands to call out from work because they are not able to afford gas, childcare, food, or rent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is taking action to deploy hundreds of ICE officers, that are currently funded by Congress, to airports being adversely impacted,\u8221\'20\'1D Bis said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will help bolster TSA efforts to keep our skies safe and minimize air travel disruptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House made a similar claim in blaming Democrats, despite Trump turning down a deal offered by Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats decided to recklessly shut down the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 . Their decision has forced countless TSA employees to work without pay. Democrats could end this shutdown by simply funding the Department,\u8221\'20\'1D said White House spokesperson Abigail Jackson in an email.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260324em3o003pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
