\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Child labor violations rise in US \u8211\'20\'13 as Republicans still roll back protections\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,395 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 March 2026\par 13:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nebraska, Indiana and West Virginia Republicans have all rolled back child labor regulations while the number of violations has risen fivefold in the last decade\par \par \uc2 The number of child labor violations has risen fivefold in the last 10 years, but Republicans across the US are continuing to propose and pass legislation that rolls back protections or regulations for workers under the age of 18.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Nebraska, Indiana and West Virginia have successfully passed legislation in 2026 rolling back child labor regulations, with legislation led by Republicans pending in other states, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandoweekly.com/news/florida-republicans-advance-bill-to-allow-opportunity-to-earn-less-than-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://missouriindependent.com/briefs/bill-seeks-to-lower-the-minimum-wage-for-minors-in-missouri/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lis.virginia.gov/bill-details/20261/SB10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The efforts to roll back child labor protections at the state level, with the ultimate goal of eroding federal standards, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/child-labor-regulations-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/meetings/ED/ED10/20250325/118020/HHRG-119-ED10-20250325-SD003.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the rightwing Heritage Foundation thinktank\u8217\'20\'19s controversial blueprint for more conservative government.\par \par \uc2 Since 2021, 30 states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/research/child-labor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  legislation that would roll back child labor protections and regulations, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/research/child-labor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 states enacting}}}\uc2  rollbacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t just want to weaken state standards. They also have this broader goal of eroding the federal standards and the weakening of the state standards is a stepping stone toward that goal,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nina Mast, policy and economic analyst at the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf federal standards are eroded, then they have nothing in place to protect minors from hazardous work, exploitative conditions, being overscheduled, all these types of violations that we\u8217\'20\'19re already seeing across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mast.\par \par \uc2 The number of minors employed in violation of child labor laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/florida-legislature-proposes-dangerous-roll-back-of-child-labor-protections-at-least-16-states-have-introduced-bills-putting-children-at-risk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  from 1,012 children in fiscal year 2015 to 5,272 in fiscal year 2025, with 773 children illegally employed in hazardous occupations in 2025 compared to 355 in 2015.\par \par \uc2 Among the child labor investigations conducted by the Department of Labor amid an increase in violations, in 2022 several \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s franchises in Pennsylvania were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/06/mcdonalds-pennsylvania-franchisees-fined-excessive-hours"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fined }}}\uc2 by the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  after an investigation found 101 children were working excessive hours outside of allowable time periods. In 2023, another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/03/kentucky-mcdonalds-child-labor-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  discovered two 10-year-olds working at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s locations in Kentucky. In January 2025, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20250115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Perdue}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20250113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JBS USA}}}\uc2  reached settlements after an investigation found contractors were employing minors in hazardous occupations at meat processing plants.\par \par \uc2 Though the Biden administration ramped up enforcement in response to the increase in violations and egregious child labor violations, the Trump administration has presided over a drastic decrease in workplace safety inspections and enforcement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://goodjobsfirst.org/worker-protections-in-freefall-the-collapse-of-federal-labor-enforcement-under-the-second-trump-administration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  a 97% decline in wage and hour enforcement cases and a 35% decline in health and safety enforcement cases.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , signed legislation into law in February 2026 that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2026/02/05/legislature-passes-law-capping-annual-minimum-wage-bumps-creating-youth-wage-below-15-until-2065/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduces }}}\uc2 the minimum wage for 14 and 15-year-olds from $15 an hour to $13.50 an hour and limited increases to 1.5% annual starting in 2030.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nebraskapublicmedia.org/en/news/news-articles/legislature-passes-minimum-wage-decrease-for-teen-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  also creates a sub-minimum training wage for 16- to 19-year-olds, set at $13.50 an hour for their first 90 days of employment.\par \par \uc2 Noel Tonniges, campaigns organizer at the non-profit Nebraska Appleseed, explained efforts to create exemptions to the Nebraska minimum wage law passed by ballot initiative in 2022 began shortly after voters overwhelmingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Nebraska_Initiative_433,_Minimum_Wage_Increase_Initiative_(2022)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  the minimum wage increase, but only gained traction when the most recent bill was introduced in 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we continue to see these carve-outs that single out young people, it makes their working conditions worse, but it also means that they\u8217\'20\'19re not able to support family in the same way. It just discourages young people from entering the workplace until they\u8217\'20\'19re eligible for these protections and for these higher wages, because there\u8217\'20\'19s no incentive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tonniges. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are really alarmed by the precedent that this sets, but we are going to continue to do everything possible to fight back and make sure that young people are protected to the best of our ability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tonniges criticized the claims made in support of cutting minimum wage for young workers, noting Nebraska has an unemployment rate far below the national average, at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dol.nebraska.gov/infolink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3.0% }}}\uc2  compared with 4.4% nationally, and labor force participation for young workers, ages 16 to 24, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.naswa.org/system/files/2025-09/2025stateoftheworkforce-2025-09ne.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 68%}}}\uc2  in 2024 compared with 56% nationally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur lawmakers have clearly gone out of their way to say that they devalue this labor. They don\u8217\'20\'19t see it as something important,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of the rhetoric that we heard from lawmakers between 2025 and 2026 was that entering the workplace is sort of a gift enough to young people, that it is in some way burdensome for workplaces to hire young people, that young people are too unskilled to fully manage the typical expectations of a job, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no data to support that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1011now.com/2026/02/05/nebraska-lawmakers-approve-bill-wind-back-voter-approved-minimum-wage-growth/#:~:text=Senators%20clashed%20on%20the%20floor,a%20final%20vote%20on%20Thursday."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marked}}}\uc2  as a priority by the Republican majority in the state legislature and led by a Democrat whose family {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://brstores.com/2025/03/26/jane-raybould-announces-retirement-from-br-stores-inc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 runs}}}\uc2  a grocery store chain in Nebraska, Jane Raybould, who did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill not only rolls back the minimum wage approved by Nebraska voters, it creates a completely new exploitation wage for young workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Megan Hunt, state senator in Nebraska, who voted against the legislation. \u8220\'20\'1CIf a teen is doing the same job as an older co-worker, their labor has the same value. Writing a lower wage into law based solely on age sends the message that some Nebraskans\u8217\'20\'19 work is worth less, and that\u8217\'20\'19s not what voters approved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Indiana, the Republican governor, Mike Braun, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/investigations/2026/03/05/braun-signs-bill-eliminating-child-labor-tracking-in-indiana/88951525007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  legislation into law in March 2026 that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/investigations/2026/03/05/braun-signs-bill-eliminating-child-labor-tracking-in-indiana/88951525007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminates}}}\uc2  all tracking of workers under the age of 18 years old in the state, removing the database system implemented after Indiana Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/indiana-lawmakers-are-once-again-trying-to-weaken-child-labor-laws-bill-sponsored-by-business-owner-would-enable-employers-to-hide-child-labor-violations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  legislation in 2020 to eliminate work permits for young workers. Indiana has also extended working hours for teens and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/indiana-lawmakers-are-once-again-trying-to-weaken-child-labor-laws-bill-sponsored-by-business-owner-would-enable-employers-to-hide-child-labor-violations/#:~:text=Lawmakers%20made%20other%20substantial%20changes%20to%20Indiana,are%20key%20to%20preventing%20child%20labor%20violations."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated}}}\uc2  mandatory rest breaks for minors.\par \par \uc2 The Indiana department of labor assessed over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iga.in.gov/pdf-documents/124/2026/house/bills/HB1302/fiscal-notes/HB1302.04.ENGS.FN001.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $250,000}}}\uc2  in penalties on employers that failed to register youth employment in 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that eliminating this system compounds the mistake of ending the work permit system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Reid Maki, the director of Child Labor Advocacy and the coordinator of the Child Labor Coalition, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIn deciding not to track teen workers, Indiana is making child labor enforcement efforts significantly more difficult.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 2024 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4857432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis }}}\uc2 of federal child labor violations between 2008 to 2020 found states that require youth work permits had 13.3% fewer violation cases and 31.8% fewer minors involved in these violations, by acting as a deterrent for employers and serving to enhance awareness and monitoring of child labor laws.\par \par \uc2 The bill\u8217\'20\'19s author, Indiana representative Jake Teshka, did not return calls for comment.\par \par \uc2 In West Virginia, Republicans passed legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvlegislature.gov/Bill_Status/bills_history.cfm?INPUT=4005&year=2026&sessiontype=RS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 4005}}}\uc2 , that will eliminate the list of hazardous occupations for workers under the age of 18, a year after they passed legislation ending the requirement of work permits for young workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt constitutes probably the most significant child labor law rollback that I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen, at least in this state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Seth DiStefano, senior policy outreach director at the West Virginia Center on Budget and Policy. \u8220\'20\'1CEssentially what it does is it more or less is going to put 16- and 17-year-old kids in direct competition with adults for a lot of jobs that 16- and 17-year-old kids used to be prohibited from doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wvpolicy.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/HB-4005-myth-vs-fact-pdf.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  claims that the bill is predicated on creating apprenticeship opportunities for teen workers, as it removes direct supervision requirements for teen workers. Rather, he argues, it creates a cheaper labor pool for employers in West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19re after is cheap labor,\u8221\'20\'1D DiStefano concluded. \u8220\'20\'1CThis, in essence, is a cheap labor bill. The reason this is happening is because the West Virginia Manufacturers Association and their members want to pay less.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The author of the bill, West Virginia delegate Ryan Browning, disputed that the bill rolls back child labor laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHB4005 lines up state code with federal codes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Browning, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I appreciate concern for allowing this type of apprenticeship, I do not agree with the statement that we are rolling back youth labor laws in a sense that we are going to allow companies to exploit them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US Department of Labor did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260322em3m00361\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
