\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US company to pay $22.5m over newborn\u8217\'20\'19s death after denying woman remote work\b0\par\par\uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas \par \uc2 662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2026\par 17:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chelsea Walsh prematurely gave birth after firm rejected work from home request in 2021 amid high-risk pregnancySign up for the Breaking News US email to get newsletter alerts in your inbox\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  freight-brokerage firm must pay $22.5m in damages to a woman whom the company denied permission to work from home as she tried managing pregnancy complications \u8211\'20\'13 and then endured her newborn\u8217\'20\'19s death after prematurely giving birth, a state court jury has decided.\par \par \uc2 The case centering on Chelsea Walsh, her late daughter Magnolia, and \uc2 Total Quality Logistics\uc2  (TQL) unfolded as many employers increasingly allowed remote work during the Covid-19 pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 but then pushed to get workers physically back into the office.\par \par \uc2 Matthew C Metzger, an attorney for Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s family, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.woltermanlaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/2026-03-18-Larkin-v.-Total-Quality-Logistics-press-release-1-2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement that the sizable verdict handed up on Wednesday in favor of his client came only after TQL passed up \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple opportunities to resolve this \u8230\'20\'26 for far, far less\u8221\'20\'1D. Metzger\u8217\'20\'19s statement added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe wish those opportunities had been taken seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Cincinnati Enquirer, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/news/local/2026/03/18/cincinnati-area-jury-awards-22-5m-in-wrongful-death-case-against-tql/89213401007/?gnt-cfr=1&gca-cat=p&gca-uir=true&gca-epti=z116240p117850l11xx50c117850e1106xxv116240d--52--b--52--&gca-ft=124&gca-ds=sophi&fbclid=IwY2xjawQqR09leHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETF3VU5wbEt5SUdYVm91RkFlc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtEPQIZJgV_yyYEaij5GhFP1NuJ4Kf1eis68IwHEOGR8xLRsun48JVEdFC-q_aem_ZsYRfau5-CMMxivpxfrmsg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  a statement from TQL spokesperson Julia Daugherty that expressed \u8220\'20\'1Ccondolences to the Walsh family\u8221\'20\'1D while expressing disagreement \u8220\'20\'1Cwith the verdict and the way the facts were characterized\u8221\'20\'1D when the case was tried over seven days. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are evaluating legal options and remain committed to supporting the health and wellbeing of our employees,\u8221\'20\'1D Daugherty\u8217\'20\'19s statement also said.\par \par \uc2 As it was put to a jury of five women and three men in the Hamilton county court of common pleas, Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy had been classified as high-risk in early February 2021 after she underwent a cervical surgery aimed at preventing her from going into labor early. Her medical providers instructed her to work from home, observe partial bed rest and otherwise limit her activities.\par \par \uc2 But Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s bosses at TQL subsequently denied her permission to work remotely, according to what jurors heard. They instead required her to return to the office and later \u8211\'20\'13 over her objections \u8211\'20\'13 placed her on leave without pay.\par \par \uc2 Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Jacob, eventually spoke to a human resources official at his workplace about his wife\u8217\'20\'19s treatment by TQL. That HR official then contacted a friend who happened to be a TQL vice-president, warning that the company had erred in denying Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s request to work from home, the Enquirer and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/ohio-firm-must-pay-225-million-mom-whose-baby-died-was-denied-work-hom-rcna264321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit that Walsh\u8217\'20\'19s family later filed alleged that the TQL executive extended his gratitude to the HR official at Jacob\u8217\'20\'19s employer. \u8220\'20\'1CYou just saved us a lawsuit,\u8221\'20\'1D he was alleged to have said.\par \par \uc2 TQL ultimately told Walsh that she could work from home after all on 24 February 2021. But by then it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo late\u8221\'20\'1D, wrote the Wolterman law office where Metzger works in a statement. Walsh that same day experienced complications pertaining to her pregnancy, was admitted to a local hospital and gave birth to Magnolia at 20 weeks and six days.\par \par \uc2 Magnolia, who was more than 18 weeks away from being full term, died within hours.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was ... heartbreaking \u8230\'20\'26 for a young family,\u8221\'20\'1D Metzger said in his statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence showed that Chelsea Walsh was following her doctors\u8217\'20\'19 instructions for a high-risk pregnancy and simply asked to work from home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that the jurors who heard the wrongful death case brought by Magnolia\u8217\'20\'19s estate determined that \u8220\'20\'1CTQL\u8217\'20\'19s denial of that reasonable request led to the death of her daughter,\u8221\'20\'1D setting the stage for Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s verdict.\par \par \uc2 Based just outside Cincinnati, TQL is reputed to be one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest freight-brokerage firms, the Enquirer reported. It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/money/business/2025/11/13/cincinnati-enquirer-deloitte-100-list-for-2025/86678699007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  the Cincinnati area\u8217\'20\'19s largest private company, with 9,000 employees and more than $6bn in revenue.\par \par \uc2 The firm furthermore is the namesake of TQL Stadium, where the professional soccer team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/fc-cincinnati"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FC Cincinnati}}}\uc2  plays its home matches.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260320em3k0053e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
