\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 CBS News workers hold 24-hour walkout for new contract\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 338 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2026\par 15:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Writers Guild of America East\uc2  says management failed to offer fair wages and basic job protectionsSign up for the Breaking News US email to get newsletter alerts in your inbox\par \par \uc2 Workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS}}}\uc2  News walked out for 24 hours on Tuesday after a new contract agreement was not reached following the expiration of the contract last week.\par \par \uc2 About 60 workers at the streaming service CBS News 24/7 are represented by the \uc2 Writers Guild of America East\uc2 . The union is holding rallies and walkouts at the CBS News broadcast center in Manhattan, New York, and at KPIX-TV CBS News Bay Area in San Francisco, California.\par \par \uc2 The union contract expired on 9 March, and the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wgaeast.org/wgae-members-at-cbs-news-24-7-deliver-strike-pledge-to-cbs-paramount-management/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered }}}\uc2 a strike pledge to management on 10 March after 95% of the unit signed the pledge and 2,900 union members and supporters signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/letters/stand-with-wgae-members-at-cbs-news-247/?source=aflcio&link_id=2&can_id=8cf4a5788956afd88f4419a1e9884481&email_referrer=email_3126447&email_subject=solidarity-alert-stand-with-wgae-members-at-cbs-news-247&"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letters }}}\uc2 to management to reach a contract with the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/tag/cbs-news-24-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News 24/7}}}\uc2  journalists are walking off the job on both coasts today because management refuses to agree to a new contract with essential work protections and fair wages,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The union alleged management continues proposing worse terms than their previous contracts.\par \par \uc2 US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/24/paramount-skydance-merger-fcc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulators approved}}}\uc2  billionaire \uc2 David Ellison\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Skydance Media\uc2  $8.4bn takeover of \uc2 CBS\uc2  owner, Paramount, last year. \uc2 Skydance\uc2  is now finalizing a $110bn takeover of CNN\u8217\'20\'19s owner, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/warner-bros"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Warner Bros}}}\uc2  Discovery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CParamount has billions to spend acquiring \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2 , but still hasn\u8217\'20\'19t guaranteed fair wages and basic job protections for the workers who make their streaming news operation run,\u8221\'20\'1D said Beth Godvik, \uc2 WGAE\uc2  vice-president of broadcast/cable/streaming news. \u8220\'20\'1COur members are walking out today to show management they stand united in their demand for a fair contract \u8211\'20\'13 and the \uc2 WGAE\uc2  is with them every step of the way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A CBS News spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to negotiate in good faith and hope to reach a fair resolution quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260317em3h004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
