\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US airports ask for donations for unpaid TSA staff amid partial government shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Olivares \par \uc2 782 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 March 2026\par 20:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 TSA employees have been working in US airports without pay since the partial shutdown began in February\par \par \uc2 A rising number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US}}}\uc2  airports are asking for donations to support employees affected by the partial government shutdown with airport security officials missing their first full paychecks Friday.\par \par \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  (TSA) employees have been working in airports around the US without pay since a shutdown began in February after Republicans and Democrats failed to reach a funding agreement. Democrats have since refused to support a bill to fund the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , the TSA\u8217\'20\'19s parent agency, without first receiving guaranteed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration enforcement}}}\uc2  reforms.\par \par \uc2 Amid the shutdown, TSA workers have been faced with continuing to work at airports without pay or find other ways to make income.\par \par \uc2 Some airports in response have started food pantries while others have requested community members donate small grocery and gasoline gift cards.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, with some TSA workers not reporting for unpaid duty, lines at security checkpoints have intermittently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/09/airline-wait-times-dhs-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grown long}}}\uc2 . For instance, at Miami international airport on Thursday, lines sporadically doubled the normal clearance time for security checkpoints.\par \par \uc2 Video of a security line stretching out to the parking lot at New Orleans\u8217\'20\'19s international airport went viral several days earlier.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian reached out to four other separate international airports: Denver, Orlando, Las Vegas and Cleveland. According to the officials who spoke with the Guardian, they have seen relatively normal lines and security wait times, even during a busy travel day like Friday and amid the busy spring break travel season.\par \par \uc2 Asked at Miami\u8217\'20\'19s airport how many of his co-workers had called out, one agent replied:\u8220\'20\'1CNot enough. Nothing happens until the public feels some pain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Praharsha Pinninti, a recent college graduate who was at Miami\u8217\'20\'19s airport heading home to Raleigh, North Carolina, said she found the pay issue \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19s extremely unfair,\u8221\'20\'1D Pinninti added, describing the legislative standoff as \u8220\'20\'1Ca test of time, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a test of patience and it\u8217\'20\'19s a test of our integrity as an issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Airports in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DENAirport/status/2031788433933250627"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Denver}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/flySEA/status/2031831000771412348"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seattle}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.ctfassets.net/2pnrhs9eukyp/7Jc33lv1TPv8JkUoWM8hhE/1e6e98c9ad88003e4f8e3362eb52fcb2/Food_and_Essentials_Pantry_Reopens_Press_Release_.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Las Vegas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.renoairport.com/federal-gov-shutdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reno}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clevelandairport.com/about-cle/news-press/cle-accepting-food-pantry-donations-amid-partial-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cleveland}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://flymco.com/media/press-releases/item/orlando-international-airport-in-the-midst-of-the-busiest-period-for-spring/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Orlando}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/reel/911835828258870"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York and New Jersey}}}\uc2 , have all been accepting donations.\par \par \uc2 The public information officer for the Denver airport, Keylen Villagrana, told the Guardian the facility had received \u8220\'20\'1Cdozens\u8221\'20\'1D of gift cards from the public.\par \par \uc2 Any donations for TSA workers are subject to the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fedweek.com/issue-briefs/oge-raises-ethics-concerns-on-accepting-assistance-outside-work-during-shutdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulations}}}\uc2 . For example, employees are not allowed to accept cash nor any cash-equivalent cards, such as a Visa gift card. The regulations also say that all gift cards have to be valued at $20 or less.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, staff at the Las Vegas international airport recently launched a food and essentials pantry to support TSA employees during the shutdown. The airport\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson, Amanda Mazzagatti, told the Guardian the facility had received baby formula, toiletries, household essentials and non-perishable food items.\par \par \uc2 The Las Vegas food pantry was first opened in 2019 during a lengthy federal government shutdown during Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidency. Then in the fall, months into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second presidency and during the longest shutdown in US history, the Las Vegas airport food pantry was reopened.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs this shutdown stretches on, these workers \u8211\'20\'13 some of whom are still recovering from the last shutdown \u8211\'20\'13 are going to really be in need of these supplies,\u8221\'20\'1D Mazzagatti said.\par \par \uc2 At Cleveland\u8217\'20\'19s Hopkins international airport, employees initially began gathering resources themselves for TSA employees ensnared by the fall shutdown. But then the public sent inquiries on how to help, leading to a food pantry, Michele Dynia, the airport\u8217\'20\'19s public information officer said.\par \par \uc2 The Cleveland airport opened the pantry again earlier in March and began asking for donations of food and gift cards with small amounts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe airport is like a family, and this is our way to help out our family members here at the airport,\u8221\'20\'1D Dynia told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Since earlier this year, Democrats have been fighting further funding for DHS agencies, including \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)\uc2  and Customs and Border Protection (CBP), the two agencies tasked with carrying out the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation campaign.\par \par \uc2 Agents with ICE and CBP under the command of the Trump administration have been met with significant criticism over their aggressive arrest and detention tactics.\par \par \uc2 Amid the shutdown, Senate Democrats have pushed for a series of smaller bills that would fund specific agencies within the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , like the TSA, the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) and others not related to immigration enforcement. But Senate Republicans have opposed those requests.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260313em3d005v6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
