\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nearly 4,000 US meatpacking workers to strike at plant run by top Trump donor\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 932 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2026\par 19:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 JBS USA\uc2  to strike Monday in what will be the first labor strike in the meatpacking industry in decades\par \par \uc2 About 3,800 workers at \uc2 JBS USA\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest meat producer, are set to strike on Monday in what will be the first labor strike in the industry in decades.\par \par \uc2 The walkout threatens to put further strain on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/feb/25/beef-packers-under-fire-prices-soar#:~:text=Beef%20prices%20continued%20to%20climb,rate%20of%20other%20consumer%20goods."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US meat prices}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/economy/beef-prices-soar-american-families-pay-steep-prices-steaks-burgers-nationwide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ground beef prices }}}\uc2 soared 15% last year \u8211\'20\'13 and could prove a headache for the Trump administration as it struggles with poor polling on cost of living issues.\par \par \uc2 Pilgrim\u8217\'20\'19s Pride\uc2 , a subsidiary of the JBS Brazilian meat processing conglomerate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/warren-pushes-giant-meat-processor-pilgrims-pride-largest-donor-to-the-trump-vance-inaugural-committee-on-potential-corruption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donated $5m}}}\uc2  to the Trump-Vance inaugural committee, making it the largest single donor.\par \par \uc2 Workers at a \uc2 JBS USA\uc2  beef processing plant in Greeley, Colorado, are set to begin an unfair labor practice strike on 16 March. The decision came after 99% of workers represented by United Food and Commercial Workers Local 7 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw7.org/l7press/jbs-workers-vote-to-authorize-ulp-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted }}}\uc2 to authorize an unfair labor practice strike after nine months of negotiations over a new contract.\par \par \uc2 Kim Cordova\uc2 , president of UFCW Local 7, who was a union organizer when the plant workers first unionized in the early 1990s, said it will be the first strike action ever carried out at the plant.\par \par \uc2 Workers say JBS has forced them to pay out of pocket for expensive personal protective equipment, discriminated against immigrant workers and tried to force through low-ball contract options.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have never had a labor dispute at this plant,\u8221\'20\'1D Cordova told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThe industry hasn\u8217\'20\'19t had a labor dispute for a very long time and it\u8217\'20\'19s because they hire a very vulnerable workforce and the expectations are they keep their head down. They\u8217\'20\'19re doing the work frankly no one in this country wants to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cordova accused JBS of dragging out negotiations, noting the company has offered less than 2% in average annual wage increases, while not addressing rising healthcare costs or allegations of systemic wage theft at the plant. Many of the workers at the plant are immigrants, many with refugee or protected immigration statuses. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cpr.org/2026/02/05/jbs-meatpacking-workers-authorize-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 57 different languages}}}\uc2  are spoken at the plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were charging workers for the replacement of personal protective equipment, which they are required to buy for them. Some of this equipment is $1,100 and they are garnishing that at full cost for the equipment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cordova. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve committed unfair labor practices. They\u8217\'20\'19ve terminated bargaining committee members. They\u8217\'20\'19ve tried to take away options on the table, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/photo?fbid=1499079862227727&set=a.380801004055624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a payout bonus}}}\uc2 , if workers won\u8217\'20\'19t accept their lowball offers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union cited an{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://towardsjustice.org/2024/10/15/press-release-haitian-workers-file-charges-against-greeley-meatpacking-plant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ongoing lawsuit }}}\uc2 against JBS alleging discrimination against Haitian workers at the plant by increasing line speeds on Haitian employees. The lawsuit alleges they were recruited under false pretenses. Cleaning contractors have also faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coloradosun.com/2023/02/17/underage-workers-jbs-meatpacking-greeley/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fines}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  for illegally employing minors at the JBS Greeley plant. JBS agreed in January 2025 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20250625193351/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/16/us/perdue-jbs-slaughterhouses-child-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settle }}}\uc2 the child labor violations without admitting wrongdoing for $4m.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think they are emboldened by their relationship with the administration. They were Trump\u8217\'20\'19s largest donor to the inauguration,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cordova.\par \par \uc2 The company was later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/06/13/jbs-brazilian-meat-company-goes-public-in-the-us.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved }}}\uc2 for a public market debut on the New York Stock Exchange after years of attempts. \uc2 Pilgrim\u8217\'20\'19s Pride{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.meatpoultry.com/articles/31799-pilgrims-pride-donated-5-million-to-trump-inauguration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  it was part of a \u8220\'20\'1Clong bipartisan history of participating in the civic process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 JBS co-owner \uc2 Joesley Batista\uc2  met with Donald Trump in September 2025, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/trumps-change-heart-lula-may-be-thanks-brazilian-beef-tycoon-2025-09-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 Reuters, resulting in the US president taking a more favorable tone toward \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , the Brazilian president.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has also recently proposed a rule to allow increasing line speeds in poultry and pork plants under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2026/02/17/usda-takes-action-lower-food-costs-consumers-and-strengthen-supply-chain-through-proposed-changes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the claim that }}}\uc2 it will decrease costs for families. \uc2 UFCW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw.org/press-releases/ufcw-blasts-usdas-proposed-line-speed-rule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  the proposal, arguing it risks the safety of meat processing workers across the US.\par \par \uc2 JBS Beef North America{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalhogfarmer.com/market-news/jbs-beef-north-america-breaks-record-with-7-2b-q3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2 record revenue of $7.2bn in the third quarter of 2025, the most recent quarter with financial results released.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve never raised economic issues with us that they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford it. They\u8217\'20\'19ve had increased profits here and they\u8217\'20\'19ve gone public. They are doing quite well,\u8221\'20\'1D added Cordova. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thecounter.org/2020-six-employees-died-colorados-jbs-plant-workers-still-fear-for-lives/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most workers die during Covid}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://revealnews.org/podcast/immigrants-on-the-line/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 human trafficking }}}\uc2 allegations by workers, understaffing while increasing line speeds and the workers can\u8217\'20\'19t even afford, in most cases, to buy the meat they are processing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The labor dispute between JBS and UFCW Local 7 comes as the company{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw.org/actions/victories/jbs-meatpacking-workers-ratify-historic-contract/#:~:text=Key%20provisions%20of%20the%20national%20contract%20include%3A&text=Significant%20wage%20increases%20for%20UFCW,security%20for%20these%20essential%20workers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  finalized }}}\uc2 contracts last year with other \uc2 UFCW\uc2  locals, covering 26,000 workers in the US.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for JBS did not comment directly on the ongoing lawsuit they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law360.com/employment-authority/labor/articles/2449479/jbs-seeks-dismissal-of-haitian-workers-bias-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to dismiss}}}\uc2  or claims of wage theft, but said: \u8220\'20\'1CJBS Greeley operates in full compliance with all applicable federal and state labor and employment laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They said in the event of a strike, the company plans on temporarily shifting operations to other facilities to minimize disruptions for customers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite our continued efforts to reach a fair and responsible agreement, Local 7 chose to end negotiations and cancel the contract we had in place,\u8221\'20\'1D the JBS spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe stand by the offer we presented. It is strong, fair, and consistent with the historic national contract reached in 2025 in partnership with UFCW International \u8211\'20\'13 an agreement that has already delivered higher wages, a secure pension, and long\u8209\'20\'11term financial stability for team members at our other major facilities. UFCW Local 7 has refused to let team members vote on this offer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260311em3b003bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
