\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge rules Kari Lake unlawfully ran US media agency, voiding mass layoffs\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 489 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2026\par 15:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lake, whom Trump appointed without Senate confirmation to run Voice of America parent agency, cut over 1,000 jobs\par \par \uc2 A federal judge ruled Saturday that Kari Lake unlawfully led the US Agency for Global Media (USAGM) for several months last year and voided mass layoffs and other actions taken during that period to dismantle the agency.\par \par \uc2 The US Agency for Global Media (USAGM) is an independent federal agency that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usagm.gov/who-we-are/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oversees}}}\uc2  the Voice of America (VOA), the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest and oldest international broadcaster, and provides grants to \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2 , \uc2 Radio Free Europe\uc2  and other news agencies.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration moved to defund the agency in early 2025 and appointed Lake to oversee the agency, but did not receive Senate confirmation for her role. Despite efforts to defund the agency, Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/07/media/kari-lake-voice-america-usagm-judge-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appropriated}}}\uc2  half a billion dollars more than Lake requested in funding for the agency in 2026.\par \par \uc2 In her role, Lake cut contracts and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2026/03/08/nx-s1-5741594/u-s-judge-kari-lake-broke-law-voice-of-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 1,000 staff positions}}}\uc2  at the agency when she was appointed to the role on 31 July before she relinquished the position on 19 November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly the Appointments Clause or the Vacancies Act\u8217\'20\'19s exclusive structure may authorize service as a principal officer, and Lake satisfies the requirements of neither the statute nor the Constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D US district court judge Royce C Lamberth wrote in the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Lamberth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/07/kari-lake-usagm-judge-00818165?utm_campaign=RSS_Syndication&utm_medium=RSS&utm_source=RSS_Feed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaned}}}\uc2  on the ruling by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www2.ca3.uscourts.gov/opinarch/252635p.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third circuit}}}\uc2  court of appeals that ruled the appointment of Alina Habba, Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former personal lawyer, to lead the US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office in New Jersey was invalid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdopting Lake\u8217\'20\'19s position would require the Court to find that the President can fill a first assistantship at any time during a vacancy in a Senate-confirmed office and then \u8230\'20\'26 elevate the first assistant to serve as the acting officer,\u8221\'20\'1D Lamberth{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/07/kari-lake-usagm-judge-00818165?utm_campaign=RSS_Syndication&utm_medium=RSS&utm_source=RSS_Feed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  in the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Lake said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KariLake/status/2030489694673260925"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on social media: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will appeal this outrageous ruling from an activist DC District Court Judge.\u8221\'20\'1D Lake also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KariLake/status/2030464907842298232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reposted}}}\uc2  a claim that the judge slept through arguments in the trial, responding \u8220\'20\'1Cnot surprised. Morbid obesity can cause massive issues with blood sugar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lamberth was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fedbar.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/LamberthMay2008-pdf-3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed}}}\uc2  by Ronald Reagan in 1987.\par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs in the case, Voice of America\u8217\'20\'19s White House bureau chief Patsy Widakuswara, Jessica Jerreat and Kate Neeper, said they felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvindicated and deeply grateful\u8221\'20\'1D for the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://savevoa.com/documents/20260307__voa-summary-judgment-opinion__219.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  that Kari Lake\u8217\'20\'19s actions shall have no force or effect is a powerful step toward undoing the damage she has inflicted on this American institution that we love,\u8221\'20\'1D they said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://savevoa.com/statements/plaintiffs-call-ruling-a-powerful-step-to-undo-damage-inflicted-by-kari-lake.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CEven as we work through what this ruling means for colleagues harmed by her actions, it brings renewed hope and momentum to the next phase of our fight: restoring VOA\u8217\'20\'19s global operations and ensuring we continue to produce journalism, not propaganda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260308em38002js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
