\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Epstein-linked \uc2 Leon Black\uc2  waged bid to \u8216\'20\'18silence\u8217\'20\'19 law firm and accusers, suit says\b0\par\par\uc2 Victoria Bekiempis and Anna Betts \par \uc2 1,187 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 March 2026\par 21:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Wigdor LLP accuses billionaire of trying to \u8216\'20\'18destroy those who seek to hold him to account for alleged sexual assault\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A law firm that represented multiple women who accused former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  associate \uc2 Leon Black\uc2  of sexual misconduct alleged in a Manhattan civil suit on Monday that the powerful financier deployed \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple frivolous and malicious lawsuits\u8221\'20\'1D as retaliation for representing these accusers.\par \par \uc2 Wigdor LLP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aboutblaw.com/bk31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  Black, who co-founded and formerly chaired \uc2 Apollo Global Management\uc2 , tried \u8220\'20\'1Cto use his billions to buy his own form of justice\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cto weaponize the civil justice system to silence and destroy those who seek to hold him to account for alleged sexual assault\u8221\'20\'1D. Black has emphatically denied all wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for Black also strongly disputed the claims made in Wigdor\u8217\'20\'19s suit. \u8220\'20\'1CThis lawsuit is another bogus attempt by Wigdor to attack Mr Black under false pretenses,\u8221\'20\'1D said Black\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Susan Estrich of Estrich Goldin.\par \par \uc2 One of the three lawsuits cited by Wigdor involved Black accuser Guzel Ganieva, who sued him in June 2021 alleging that he \u8220\'20\'1Cviolently sexually assaulted\u8221\'20\'1D her for years. Black sued Ganieva and Wigdor, who represented her at the time, that October, claiming they \u8220\'20\'1Cconspired to harm\u8221\'20\'1D him; this civil action was dismissed. Ganieva\u8217\'20\'19s civil suit against Black was also dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Wigdor\u8217\'20\'19s suit against Black, filed in New York county supreme court, cites recently disclosed Epstein investigative files that appear to show Epstein plotting with the powerful Wall Street lawyer Brad Karp to try to arrange Ganieva\u8217\'20\'19s deportation. While Epstein and Karp\u8217\'20\'19s discussions did not result in deportation, these 2015 emails also reveal discussions about coordinated surveillance on Ganieva and whether she could be jailed.\par \par \uc2 Epstein on 29 July 2015 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2011/EFTA02353940.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  to Karp: \u8220\'20\'1CIs it possible for your contacts to 1 get her current visa status ? 2. Is there a way for us to file something that would revoke a tourist visa?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several hours later, Karp responded: \u8220\'20\'1CBoth good ideas; will work on this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These messages indicated that the woman was bothering an Epstein associate with the name \u8220\'20\'1CLeon\u8221\'20\'1D. Epstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2011/EFTA02493136.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on 16 August 2015: \u8220\'20\'1Ccan you tell me for certain that if leon decides enough is enough, ( she has not responded to an email from him that says i am checking on you). that you and lorin can have her arrested.!! fed extortion, high bail. . maybe deportation?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Lorin\u8217\'20\'19s surname is not mentioned in these documents, a lawyer with the name Lorin Reisner, who went to the white-shoe firm Paul Weiss approximately a year before these Epstein-Karp exchanges, had previously led the Manhattan federal prosecutor office\u8217\'20\'19s criminal section. Karp suggested in an email that \u8220\'20\'1CLorin\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D connections might move the needle in regards to Ganieva.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll check again with lorin, but my strong belief is that the answer is yes. Especially with the referral coming from the most recent head of the sdny usao,\u8221\'20\'1D Karp said on 16 August 2015.\par \par \uc2 Karp {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/05/paul-weiss-chairman-brad-karp-resigns-epstein-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepped down}}}\uc2  from his top role at Paul Weiss earlier this year after his correspondence with Epstein surfaced.\par \par \uc2 Neither Karp, Reisner nor Paul Weiss immediately responded to a request for comment. They also did not respond to prior requests for comment on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/10/jeffrey-epstein-brad-karp-woman-deported"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 10 February story}}}\uc2  detailing Epstein and Karp\u8217\'20\'19s communications about deportation.\par \par \uc2 Wigdor claims Black\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits violate New York state\u8217\'20\'19s anti-Slapp (Strategic Lawsuit Against Public Participation) law, which is designed to protect individuals and organizations from frivolous lawsuits. The complaint states that of the three lawsuits Black filed against the firm, two were dismissed and one is still pending.\par \par \uc2 Wigdor alleges that Black\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits tried thwarting accusers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to free speech and that the firm suffered reputational harm due to Black\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits. \u8220\'20\'1CPunishing lawyers for the clients they represent subverts not only the administration of justice but also the principle of equality under the law, and, thus, the American legal system,\u8221\'20\'1D the complaint states.\par \par \uc2 Black\u8217\'20\'19s ties to Epstein have drawn renewed attention in recent months as he was repeatedly mentioned in the recently released Epstein files. For example, Black appears on a page titled \u8220\'20\'1CPROMINENT NAMES\u8221\'20\'1D in an \uc2 FBI\uc2  presentation about Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear for whom this presentation was made, and the slideshow does not indicate whether authorities verified any allegations against these men. Black has not been charged with any crimes related to Epstein.\par \par \uc2 Estrich also noted last month that Black \u8220\'20\'1Casked for an independent investigation of his relationship with Epstein\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Dechert law firm investigated and reviewed more than 60,000 documents, interviewed more than 20 people and concluded that Mr Black paid Epstein for estate planning and tax advice and that he had no awareness of Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s criminal activities,\u8221\'20\'1D Estrich said.\par \par \uc2 Estrich also previously said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is absolutely no truth to any of the allegations against Mr Black.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under Black\u8217\'20\'19s name, the document referenced allegations that Epstein had reportedly \u8220\'20\'1Ctold [name redacted] to give Black a massage while Black was naked\u8221\'20\'1D. An accuser \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2010/EFTA01656173.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated}}}\uc2  another female gave Black a massage and he made her perform oral sex\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Black\u8217\'20\'19s team said Wigdor\u8217\'20\'19s suit was an effort to redeem itself for unsuccessful lawsuits against Black.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe facts are quite simple. Wigdor has abused the legal system, manipulated the media, and they are desperate to avoid being held accountable for their own failings,\u8221\'20\'1D said Estrich.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere have only been three lawsuits filed against Mr Black all by Wigdor and all have failed \u8211\'20\'13 one case has been dismissed, the other withdrawn, and the Jane Doe case is facing a motion for case terminating sanctions. Wigdor was fired by Guzel Ganieva and ceased representation of Jane Doe in an attempt to avoid being sanctioned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked for comment on Black\u8217\'20\'19s statement, Raymond Audain, the attorney representing Wigdor, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is about whether wealthy individuals can weaponize the justice system to silence not just their accusers, but also the attorneys who represent them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile too many foundational American institutions have been coopted and corrupted by billionaires, our courts have, thankfully, remained guarantors of equal justice,\u8221\'20\'1D said Audain, a partner at Giskan Solotaroff & Anderson. \u8220\'20\'1CRetaliating against lawyers for representing survivors subverts not just the principle of equality under the law, but also the American legal system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In January 2023, Black {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.finance.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/usvi_black_settlement_agreement_-_executedpdf.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed}}}\uc2  to pay $62.5m to the US Virgin Islands, as to be released from any possible legal claims related to local authorities\u8217\'20\'19 investigation of Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s sex trafficking in the territory. The Senate finance committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.finance.senate.gov/ranking-members-news/wyden-releases-new-information-on-financing-of-jeffrey-epsteins-operations-by-billionaire-leon-black-seeks-documents-from-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2 in March 2025 that they had encountered documents indicating that Black, who claimed he had hired Epstein for tax and estate planning advice, paid him $170m.\par \par \uc2 Epstein in 2008 landed a sweetheart plea deal with Florida prosecutors. He pleaded guilty to state-level prostitution charges and was able to avoid federal prosecution amid numerous allegations that he abused teen girls at his Palm Beach manse.\par \par \uc2 Epstein was arrested in 2019 on sex-trafficking charges. He died in jail awaiting his Manhattan federal court trial.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260303em33006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
