\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Jack Dorsey\uc2  to cut 4,000 jobs due to AI advances at Square parent Block\b0\par\par\uc2 Sanya Mansoor \par \uc2 683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2026\par 18:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shares in company increased over 20% as investors were encouraged by CEO\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that cuts will drive profitsSign up for the Breaking News US email to get newsletter alerts in your inbox\par \par \uc2 Fintech company Block announced that it would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/job-losses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laying off}}}\uc2  4,000 of its 10,000 employees because of gains in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI}}}\uc2  productivity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIntelligence tools have changed what it means to build and run a company,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/jack-dorsey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jack Dorsey}}}\uc2 , Block\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s29.q4cdn.com/628966176/files/doc_financials/2025/q4/Q4-2025-Shareholder-Letter_Block.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter to shareholders}}}\uc2  on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re already seeing it internally. A significantly smaller team, using the tools we\u8217\'20\'19re building, can do more and do it better. And intelligence tool capabilities are compounding faster every week.\u8221\'20\'1DBlock is the parent company for online payment platforms such as Square and Cash App.\par \par \uc2 Investors so far appear encouraged by Dorsey\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that the cuts, and increased reliance on AI, will drive profitability, analysts said. Shares increased more than 20% in pre-market trading on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Block\u8217\'20\'19s layoffs speak to larger fears about job cuts driven by a growing use of AI. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  noted in February that the increasing pace of AI adoption could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/companies-cutting-jobs-investments-shift-toward-ai-2026-02-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drive up unemployment}}}\uc2  this year, and estimated that the technology had already resulted in 5,000 to 10,000 monthly net job losses last year. A November study from the \uc2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\uc2  found that AI could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/11/26/mit-study-finds-ai-can-already-replace-11point7percent-of-us-workforce.html#:~:text=Massachusetts%20Institute%20of%20Technology%20released,and%20Oak%20Ridge%20National%20Laboratory."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already replace}}}\uc2  nearly 12% of the workforce in the US.\par \par \uc2 The tech sector is among the most hit, and workers at other tech companies are feeling the heat, too. \uc2 Marc Benioff\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Salesforce{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/02/salesforce-ceo-confirms-4000-layoffs-because-i-need-less-heads-with-ai.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut about 4,000 jobs}}}\uc2  last year, with the CEO saying that he \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds less heads\u8221\'20\'1D given AI\u8217\'20\'19s efficiency.\par \par \uc2 Dorsey claimed on Thursday that the decision to almost halve Block\u8217\'20\'19s workforce wasn\u8217\'20\'19t because the business was in trouble, and that economic performance had actually been strong. (Block beat Wall Street expectations for its fourth quarter, reporting $6.25 bn in total revenue).\par \par \uc2 Dorsey said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jack/status/2027129697092731343?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on X}}}\uc2  that he had two choices: gradually cut his workforce over months and years \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cor be honest about where we are and act on it now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CRepeated rounds of cuts are destructive to morale, to focus and to the trust that customers and shareholders place in our ability to lead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Block executives said on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s29.q4cdn.com/628966176/files/doc_financials/2025/q4/Q4-2025-Prepared-Remarks-Block.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s earnings call}}}\uc2  that the company had been increasing its reliance on AI for years, noting that some AI work streams were \u8220\'20\'1Cnearly fully rolled out, others are earlier in their maturity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Block had already laid off hundreds of workers in early February. Earlier this month, employees still at the company reported that there was rapidly deteriorating employee morale and that there were requirements to use generative AI, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/inside-rolling-layoffs-jack-dorsey-block/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wired}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wired said it reviewed an employee complaint submitted to Dorsey in a recent all-hands meeting that said \u8220\'20\'1Cmorale is probably the worst I\u8217\'20\'19ve felt in four years\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe overarching culture at Block is crumbling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dorsey acknowledged the risk of the cuts on X, and in his message to shareholders. The company\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d18rn0p25nwr6d.cloudfront.net/CIK-0001512673/7ee8874c-2cf3-4835-a112-27ac828d937a.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recent 10-K filing}}}\uc2  outlined ways its AI gamble could go wrong. \u8220\'20\'1COur ability to successfully operate with a reduced workforce is expected to depend in part on the effectiveness, reliability and adoption of our proactive intelligence and AI tools,\u8221\'20\'1D the company noted. \u8220\'20\'1CThese technologies may not perform as expected, may require more time or expense to implement effectively, may introduce operational or cybersecurity risks or may fail to enhance productivity and maintain operational efficiency as expected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, we have debated whether AI would dent jobs at the margin. Now we have a public case study in which the CEO explicitly says that intelligence tools have changed what it means to build and run a company,\u8221\'20\'1D Stephen Innes of SPI Asset Management told the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1COther large employers have announced tens of thousands of cuts in recent months. Some have downplayed the AI link. Block did not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260227em2r004sb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
