\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Workers decry \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  offshoring jobs despite praise for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,258 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2026\par 17:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The US has lost factory jobs amid promises of a tariff-led renaissance\par \par \uc2 Workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/whirlpool-corporation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Whirlpool}}}\uc2 , the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest appliance manufacturer and a champion of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tariff policies, are criticizing the company for cutting jobs at an Iowa plant while bolstering production in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The job cuts at \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  come as the company has continued to support the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trade policies and claimed they will help bolster US manufacturing. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade policies appear to have done little for US manufacturing so far. The US has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/us-trade-deficit-widens-sharply-december-goods-trade-gap-highest-record-2025-2026-02-19/#:~:text=The%20trade%20gap%20ballooned%2032.6,to%20%24901.5%20billion%20in%202025."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost 83,000 factory jobs}}}\uc2  since Trump took office in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 Effective 9 March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/amana-layoffs-union-accuses-whirlpool-214855746.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAACjChSZLARhSiHDKdJjzSEYc7Tb1pibRKvZ4jANxaEfG6GqBrjqhWtafpp-qySX__4Vxyo_pfmy8DojWXGuOnwzskam9vmi2t4U47G5vnss0Gr3xAghPX8EQrTxYTB8Diir_28YBR00sE88fM24A4t0VUmvNmfCkh06DdWQixG7h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 341 jobs}}}\uc2  are being cut at the \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  plant in Amana, Iowa. The cuts come less than a year after{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/business/2025/06/30/union-criticizes-whirlpool-layoffs-at-amana-factory/84422473007/?gnt-cfr=1&gca-cat=p&gca-uir=true&gca-epti=z115635p119650c119650v115635d--30--b--30--&gca-ft=156&gca-ds=sophi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  250 jobs}}}\uc2  were cut in July 2025. According to \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  union (IAM) officials, the company has informed them that more cuts are on the way later this year. The plant produces refrigerators under the \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2 , KitchenAid, \uc2 Maytag\uc2  and \uc2 Amana\uc2  brands.\par \par \uc2 Whirlpool{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.promexicoindustry.com/en/article/gp-desarrollos-completes-major-whirlpool-facility-expansion-in-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened}}}\uc2  a new manufacturing facility in Mexico in August 2025, and union officials and workers say their manufacturing work and jobs have been moved there.\par \par \uc2 Sandra Freytag, the first shift plant chair who has worked at the plant for 31 years, told the Guardian that \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  began cutting production lines from the plant and moving those to Mexico several years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing that they\u8217\'20\'19re making our product in Mexico,\u8221\'20\'1D said Freytag.\par \par \uc2 She said the number of workers at the plant had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://betterbuildingssolutioncenter.energy.gov/iso-50001/showcase-projects/whirlpool-amana-operations-%E2%80%94-50001-ready-facility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined from nearly 3,000}}}\uc2  just a few years ago to close to 1,300, and that she believed more cuts were likely. \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whirlpoolcorp.com/manufacturing.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 20,000 employees }}}\uc2 in the US, with 14,000 in manufacturing at 10 factories.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not seeing a ton of parts or new opportunities or changes in their platforms that might support all of us staying in the factory or even staying open long term,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  is the only big facility around this area. So they\u8217\'20\'19re about seven small towns that it\u8217\'20\'19s going to devastate when those people lose their jobs, and if we lose any more, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that we\u8217\'20\'19ll have small towns left in that area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  sought and received tariffs on imported washing machines, their competitors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investors.whirlpoolcorp.com/news-and-events/news/news-details/2018/Presidents-enforcement-decision-on-washers-is-a-win-for-US-manufacturing-jobs/default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  it a win \u8220\'20\'1Cfor American workers and consumers alike.\u8221\'20\'1D In 2020 Trump gave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefings-statements/remarks-president-trump-whirlpool-corporation-manufacturing-plant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a speech}}}\uc2  at a \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  plant in Ohio, calling the compan\par \par \uc2 y a \u8220\'20\'1Cshining example\u8221\'20\'1D of the \u8220\'20\'1Cbuy American and hire American\u8221\'20\'1D policies his administration was pursuing.\par \par \uc2 According to the conservative Heritage thinktank, the tariffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/trade/commentary/we-shouldnt-rinse-and-repeat-when-it-comes-costly-washing-machine-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drove up prices}}}\uc2  of the appliances, costing consumers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats.org/news/trump-visits-ohio-to-sell-his-tariffs-that-didnt-help-workers-falsely-tout-his-manufacturing-record/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.5bn annually}}}\uc2  and decreasing demand.\par \par \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  touted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs in 2025 as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/lifestyle/whirlpool-ceo-says-trump-tariffs-create-level-playing-field-us-manufacturing-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $300m investment}}}\uc2  in Ohio and the creation of 400 to 600 jobs. \uc2 Whirlpool{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whirlpoolcorp.com/latest-news/whirlpool-corporation-announces--300-million-investment-in--u-s-.html#:~:text=Approximately%2080%25%20of%20Whirlpool%20Corp,U.S.%20plants%20is%20sourced%20domestically."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  80% of its US sales are produced in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe would either have scaled down, made it later, or hesitated,\u8221\'20\'1D CEO \uc2 Marc Bitzer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/lifestyle/whirlpool-ceo-says-trump-tariffs-create-level-playing-field-us-manufacturing-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Fox News}}}\uc2  in October 2025 of the investment, one of several the CEO made on the outlet touting tariffs in 2025. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re strongly supportive of tariff policy and very thankful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  noted in its most recent earnings call in January 2026 that tariffs cost them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s202.q4cdn.com/229739679/files/doc_financials/2025/q4/CORRECTED-TRANSCRIPT_-Whirlpool-Corp-WHR-US-Q4-2025-Earnings-Call-29-January-2026-8_00-AM-ET.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $300m}}}\uc2  in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Sam Cicinelli, the midwest territory general vice-president for IAM, criticized \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  for the layoffs after the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://subsidytracker.goodjobsfirst.org/parent/whirlpool-corp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  millions of dollars in subsidies and tax credits in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 He explained when the union was informed by \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  of the recent job cuts: \u8220\'20\'1Cthe company also warned us that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be making even more cuts that are on the way at the end of the second quarter. This is not a one-time, one-off business decision on their part. It shows it\u8217\'20\'19s a deliberate pattern of corporate abandonment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He claimed \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  had a history of laying off workers in Iowa in search for cheaper labor.\par \par \uc2 Cicinelli called the layoffs \u8220\'20\'1Can absolute slap in the face to every American worker in this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump appeared at a \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  factory in Ohio in August 2020 where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/DCPD-202000577/pdf/DCPD-202000577.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoted }}}\uc2 the United States Mexico Canada agreement (USMCA), which he signed in 2018.\par \par \uc2 Cicinelli added on \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s job cuts: \u8220\'20\'1CIt goes against the USMCA agreement. We should be pumping more resources into the United States. The USMCA was sold to us as the new and improved Nafta, supposed to protect these good-paying jobs, and yet this definitely tells a different story.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kerry Waddell, who worked at the \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  plant in Iowa for 36 years before currently serving as a business agent for the union, said \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  workers affected by the cuts currently have no severance agreement, lose their health insurance the day they are laid off and face reduced unemployment benefits as Iowa cut unemployment benefit eligibility in 2022 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.niskanencenter.org/iowas-recent-unemployment-insurance-reforms-may-undermine-program-solvency/#:~:text=In%202022%2C%20the%20state%20reduced,revenue%20that%20will%20be%20raised."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16 weeks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Waddell claimed that employees had been provided with very little information on the cuts and the reasoning behind them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have tremendous capacity to produce and manufacture in that facility. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got a large employee base in the area for them to draw on to do that work that they\u8217\'20\'19ve chosen not to,\u8221\'20\'1D said Waddell. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19re actually doing is taking jobs out of Iowa, moving them to Mexico, and those very refrigerators are being brought back into the US for sale.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the US supreme court struck down most of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, Whirlpool {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-today-us-gdp-report-02-20-26/card/whirlpool-counting-on-remaining-tariffs-to-keep-its-edge-jHSNTy55OmUUEJZn0LhW?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=AWEtsqduRjo0ySPqXk4E0TjhtoL0hyw63nV5UTNMz3zdUZ27qpcgrXpNPhPQp4wFHXs%3D&gaa_ts=699b4b2b&gaa_sig=zYl_yK6UmG2M05wphU3k_7NJHv4BzD0uOsx-9tEDuerI9fqpzOCy24zymcDt4jId205x5ezK1XJHhEEQcQmhrg%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  the remaining tariffs on steel and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 10% global tariff announced after the decision, would grant them a competitive edge.\par \par \uc2 But workers at the Whirlpool plant in Amana, Iowa, noted that the tariffs are not preventing the company from continuing to cut jobs at the plant and move their work to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing there over 30 years, I\u8217\'20\'19ve grown myself with this company. I\u8217\'20\'19ve devoted my life to them. I\u8217\'20\'19ve raised my children there, and just thinking that I might not have a job in a year, it\u8217\'20\'19s just devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sandy Lorenz, third shift plant chair who has worked at the plant for 33 years. \u8220\'20\'1CThey could keep these products here, and they could keep these people working, but it just comes down to that they are greedy and want to make a little more money. And that\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Whirlpool did not comment on the union\u8217\'20\'19s complaints about offshoring to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The company said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1COur recent announcement is part of a multi-year modernization plan that will transform the plant into a dynamic operation that will continue to produce best-in-class refrigerators, while also incorporating warehousing, parts production and sub-assembly work. This transformation is necessary to position the Amana plant for continued stability and success. We are committed to supporting affected employees through this transition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company emphasized its continued support for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are confident that the US administration will continue to take strong actions to support domestic manufacturing and American workers,\u8221\'20\'1D the company added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe announcement of a new 15% global tariff under Section 122, the opening of new trade investigations and existence of previously-negotiated trade agreements gives us continued confidence that Whirlpool Corporation will ultimately benefit from trade policies aimed at leveling the playing field for US manufacturers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260226em2q002jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
