\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Officials investigate deadly California avalanche for possible criminal negligence\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 573 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2026\par 02:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nevada county sheriff said investigation includes learning why the ski trip was not cancelled by the guide company\par \par \uc2 Authorities are investigating whether any criminal negligence was involved in the deadly avalanche that swept California\u8217\'20\'19s Lake Tahoe this week, which killed at least eight skiers and their guides while returning from a three-day backcountry skiing trip.\par \par \uc2 The Nevada county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Friday said that they notified the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha)\uc2 , which regulates workplace safety, of the active investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are investigating the incident to determine if there were any factors that would be considered criminal negligence,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson for the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is too early to know if criminal charges will be applicable, as the investigation is preliminary and remains active and ongoing. The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office would ultimately be the determining authority for any criminal charges to be filed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The avalanche, the deadliest in California\u8217\'20\'19s modern history, killed at least eight people and a ninth skier is still missing but is presumed dead.\par \par \uc2 Blackbird Mountain Guides, which employed the ski guides that led the trek, said in a statement released on Wednesday that three of their workers died after the avalanche, and one of them survived.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was an enormous tragedy, and the saddest event our team has ever experienced,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zeb Blais, founder of Blackbird Mountain Guides, in the statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are doing what we can to support the families who lost so much, and the members of our team who lost treasured friends and colleagues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is still a lot that we\u8217\'20\'19re learning about what happened. It\u8217\'20\'19s too soon to draw conclusions, but investigations are underway,\u8221\'20\'1D Blais added in Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s statement.\par \par \uc2 As the 15 skiers were coming back from their trip, which started on Sunday, avalanche warnings were already in place. Blackbird Mountain Guides seemed to be aware of the hazardous weather conditions, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DUzjaE3j3Jt/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a social media video}}}\uc2  posted on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 During a press conference on Wednesday, Shannan Moon, Nevada county\u8217\'20\'19s sheriff, said that the investigation includes learning why the ski trip was not cancelled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose are the decisions that the guide company clearly had made,\u8221\'20\'1D Moon said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re still in conversation with them on the decision factors that they made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Six of the 15 skiers survived and were rescued, including the fourth guide. Amid hazardous weather conditions, the avalanche victims have not yet been extracted from the mountain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdverse weather, coupled with ongoing avalanche danger, has hindered the recovery process,\u8221\'20\'1D a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/nevadacountysheriffsoffice/posts/pfbid0QXY53nQi3gbw7eNQuBmWeuGp7xoJm1BLPNv7dYe3T5BwLcPbbSBfecjTyNnuZHYml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Friday by the Nevada county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office said. A statement released on Thursday said \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil the recovery mission is completed, the Nevada County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office is unable to confirm the identifications, ages, affiliations, or cities of origin for the victims.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Family members have confirmed the identities of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/19/california-avalanche-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six of the eight people}}}\uc2  who died in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s avalanche. The identified victims \u8211\'20\'13 Carrie Atkin, Liz Clabaugh, Danielle Keatley, Kate Morse, Caroline Sekar and Kate Vitt \u8211\'20\'13 were part of a group which frequently went on ski trips together.\par \par \uc2 The sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office also announced that avalanche mitigation was under way in California\u8217\'20\'19s Sierra Nevada on Friday, consisting of controlled \u8220\'20\'1Cexplosive deployment to intentionally release unstable snowpack\u8221\'20\'1D. These measures aim to reduce avalanche risk and improve first responder safety as they recover victims.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260220em2k006v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
