\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 West Virginia sues \uc2 Apple\uc2  over child sex abuse material stored and shared on iCloud\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 1,021 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 February 2026\par 22:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Attorney general JB McCuskey, a Republican, calls case the first of its kind by a government agency against company\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general filed a lawsuit on Thursday accusing \uc2 Apple\uc2  of allowing its iCloud service to become a vehicle for distributing child sexual abuse material.\par \par \uc2 The state alleges that the company facilitated the spread of child sexual abuse material by declining to deploy tools that scan photos and videos and detect such material in iCloud users\u8217\'20\'19 collections.\par \par \uc2 JB McCuskey, a Republican, accused \uc2 Apple\uc2  of prioritizing user privacy over child safety. His office called the case the first of its kind by a government agency over the distribution of child sexual abuse material on \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s data storage platform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese images are a permanent record of a child\u8217\'20\'19s trauma, and that child is revictimized every time the material is shared or viewed,\u8221\'20\'1D McCuskey said in the statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThis conduct is despicable, and \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inaction is inexcusable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  responded with a blanket denial to the allegations: \u8220\'20\'1CAt \uc2 Apple\uc2 , protecting the safety and privacy of our users, especially children, is central to what we do. We are innovating every day to combat ever-evolving threats and maintain the safest, most trusted platform for kids.\u8221\'20\'1D The company emphasized its controls that prevent children from uploading or receiving nude images, though West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit aims at abusers\u8217\'20\'19 use of \uc2 Apple\uc2  devices and services.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, an executive in charge of fraud detection at \uc2 Apple\uc2  texted a colleague: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the greatest platform for distributing child porn.\u8221\'20\'1D The exchange was made public during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/c/22611236/epic-v-apple-emails-project-liberty-app-store-schiller-sweeney-cook-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the trial between Apple and Fortnite maker Epic Games}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A group of victims of child sexual exploitation sued \uc2 Apple\uc2  in 2024, making similar allegations, for $1.2bn in damages. The suit is ongoing. The same year, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 National Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Children\uc2  (\uc2 NSPCC\uc2 ) accused \uc2 Apple\uc2  of vastly undercounting how often child sexual abuse material appeared in its products. In a year, child predators used \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s iCloud, iMessage and FaceTime to store and exchange CSAM in a higher number of cases in England and Wales alone than the company reported across all other countries combined, according to police data obtained by the \uc2 NSPCC\uc2 . \uc2 Apple\uc2  did not comment on the finding at the time.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  routinely makes far fewer reports of CSAM to the \uc2 National Center for Missing and Exploited Children\uc2  (NCMEC) than \uc2 Google\uc2  or \uc2 Meta\uc2 , according to data published by NCMEC.\par \par \uc2 The company has considered scanning images saved in private iCloud accounts but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/08/tech/apple-csam-tool"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abandoned the approach}}}\uc2  after concerns about user privacy and safety, including worries that it could be exploited by governments looking for other material for censorship or arrest.\par \par \uc2 McCuskey\u8217\'20\'19s office filed the lawsuit in Mason county circuit court. The lawsuit seeks statutory and punitive damages and asks to have a judge force \uc2 Apple\uc2  to implement more effective measures to detect abusive material and implement safer product designs.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and other platform providers check uploaded photos or emailed attachments against a database of identifiers of known child sex abuse material provided by the \uc2 National Center for Missing and Exploited Children\uc2  and other clearinghouses.\par \par \uc2 Until 2022, \uc2 Apple\uc2  took a different approach. It did not scan all files uploaded to its iCloud storage offerings, and the data was not end-to-end encrypted, meaning law enforcement officials could access it with a warrant.\par \par \uc2 Reuters in 2020 reported that \uc2 Apple\uc2  planned end-to-end encryption for iCloud, which would have put data into a form unusable by law enforcement officials. It abandoned the plan after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  complained it would harm investigations.\par \par \uc2 In August 2021, \uc2 Apple\uc2  announced NeuralHash, which it designed to balance the detection of child abuse material with privacy by scanning images on users\u8217\'20\'19 devices before upload.\par \par \uc2 The system was criticized by security researchers who worried it could yield false reports of abuse material, and it sparked a backlash from privacy advocates who claimed it could be expanded to permit government surveillance.\par \par \uc2 A month later, \uc2 Apple\uc2  delayed the introduction of NeuralHash before canceling it in December 2022, the state said in its statement. That same month, \uc2 Apple\uc2  launched an option for end-to-end encryption for iCloud data.\par \par \uc2 The state said NeuralHash was inferior to other tools and could be easily evaded. It said \uc2 Apple\uc2  stores and synchronizes data through iCloud without proactive abuse material detection, allowing such images to circulate.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Apple\uc2  did not go through with the effort to scan images being uploaded to iCloud, it did implement a feature called Communication Safety that blurs nudity and other sensitive content being sent to or from a child\u8217\'20\'19s device.\par \par \uc2 Federal law requires US-based technology companies to report abuse material to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children. Apple in 2023 made 267 reports, compared with 1.47m by Google and 30.6m by Meta Platforms, the state said.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s claims mirror allegations in a proposed class-action lawsuit filed against Apple in late 2024 in federal court in California by individuals depicted in such images.\par \par \uc2 Apple has moved to dismiss that lawsuit, saying the firm is shielded from liability under section 230 of the Communications Decency Act, a law that provides broad protections to internet companies from lawsuits over content generated by users. \u8226\'20\'22 In the US, call or text the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.childhelp.org/hotline/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Childhelp}}}\uc2  abuse hotline on 800-422-4453 or visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.childhelp.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their website}}}\uc2  for more resources and to report child abuse or DM for help. For adult survivors of child abuse, help is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ascasupport.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ascasupport.org}}}\uc2 . In the UK, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nspcc.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NSPCC}}}\uc2  offers support to children on 0800 1111, and adults concerned about a child on 0808 800 5000. The National Association for People Abused in Childhood ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://napac.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Napac}}}\uc2 ) offers support for adult survivors on 0808 801 0331. In Australia, children, young adults, parents and teachers can contact the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kidshelpline.com.au/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kids Helpline}}}\uc2  on 1800 55 1800; adult survivors can seek help at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.blueknot.org.au/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blue Knot Foundation}}}\uc2  on 1300 657 380. Other sources of help can be found at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.childhelplineinternational.org/child-helplines/child-helpline-network/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Child Helpline International}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260219em2j006v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
