\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Inside \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tumultuous two years as publisher of the \uc2 Washington Post\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeremy Barr in Washington \par \uc2 1,778 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 February 2026\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Before the Post\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping layoffs and Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt resignation, his tenure was marked by controversy and clashes with staff\par \par \uc2 Standing on the seventh floor in the center of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s open newsroom on the morning of 3 June 2024, publisher \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  decided to deliver some tough love to a news organization he had taken charge of five months earlier.\par \par \uc2 Lewis, a veteran of \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s media empire, had replaced Fred Ryan, a former Ronald Reagan aide who had presided over some of the Post\u8217\'20\'19s profitable years \u8211\'20\'13 during the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but lost the confidence of some staffers after clashing with employees during a late 2022 town hall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to turn this thing around, but let\u8217\'20\'19s not sugarcoat it: it needs turning around, right?\u8221\'20\'1D Lewis said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are losing large amounts of money. Your audience has halved in recent years. People are not reading your stuff. I can\u8217\'20\'19t sugarcoat it any more. So I\u8217\'20\'19ve had to take decisive, urgent action to set us on a different path.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It turned out to be one of the few times that Lewis would address the whole company. On Saturday evening, Lewis, 56, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/07/washington-post-will-lewis-resigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly announced his resignation}}}\uc2 , just three days after the Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/04/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slashed nearly a third of its entire staff}}}\uc2  in one of the largest layoffs in US media history. Instead of putting the Post on a more promising financial path, Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s two years were marked by controversy, clashes with staff and jargon-heavy initiatives that didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to amount to much.\par \par \uc2 Ire over the cuts was mostly directed at Lewis and the Post\u8217\'20\'19s billionaire owner, Jeff Bezos. While Lewis nominally ran the company, it was left to top editor Matt Murray to deliver the news of the cuts during an early morning \uc2 Zoom\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 But while he was a no-show for the meeting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NickiJhabvala/status/2019568890473508935"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lewis was spotted a day later}}}\uc2  at the pre-game festivities for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/super-bowl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Super Bowl}}}\uc2  by a former Post sports reporter, who noted his appearance came after he took apart the sports section, including football coverage.\par \par \uc2 While current and former staffers have suspicions about why, the bigger \u8211\'20\'13 and still unanswered \u8211\'20\'13 question about Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s departure is why now? Lewis had long been unpopular with many Post employees and seemed to have made little progress in his business-side efforts. A senior Post journalist told the Guardian in November that Lewis was \u8220\'20\'1Cuniversally reviled\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was surprised by the timing. I was not surprised by the outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Ruth Marcus, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/03/10/nx-s1-5323136/washington-post-editor-ruth-marcus-resigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned as a Post columnist}}}\uc2  in March 2025 after 40 years at the publication, said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe news of Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s departure triggered a thousand celebratory messages and emojis \u8211\'20\'13 we were popping the digital champagne, caseloads of it,\u8221\'20\'1D said a longtime Post staff writer who was not authorized to comment. \u8220\'20\'1CHere was a man who\u8217\'20\'19d been handed the reins of one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most storied journalistic institutions and who seemed, almost from the start, like a man who hated the job and hated us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, many Post employees believed that Bezos was not particularly interested in what they thought of Lewis. (Lewis did not respond to messages seeking comment.)\par \par \uc2 The Financial Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/5fa62c89-ebf2-4e2e-beb0-d09cfce22d81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that senior management at the Post were \u8220\'20\'1Clivid\u8221\'20\'1D about Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at the Super Bowl and disliked the optics of him appearing at a glamorous event a day after hundreds of employees lost their livelihoods.\par \par \uc2 Some Post staffers, though, have pointed out that Bezos had not previously seemed concerned about optics; in June 2025, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BenMullin/status/1927379424174866555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a month after the Post announced}}}\uc2  that it would once again incentivize staffers to leave the company via buyouts, Bezos and his now wife Lauren Sanchez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/jeff-bezos-lauren-sanchez-host-foam-party-ahead-of-wedding-11759414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hosted a foam party}}}\uc2  on a $500m yacht in advance of their star-studded wedding in Venice. (A Post spokesperson did not respond when asked whether Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s Super Bowl cameo factored into his departure.)\par \par \uc2 Some Post staffers, including Marcus, were initially encouraged when Lewis was named to the job in November 2023. Early on, she recalled getting personal emails from Lewis complimenting her columns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first time I met him was at a reception and I said: \u8216\'20\'18Hi, I\u8217\'20\'19m Ruth Marcus. I\u8217\'20\'19m your pen pal.\u8217\'20\'19 And he said: \u8216\'20\'18Oh, can I give you a hug? Your stuff is great.\u8217\'20\'19 I was initially well-disposed toward him \u8211\'20\'13 until I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sally Quinn, a former Post writer and the widow of the former Post executive editor Ben Bradlee, was asked to welcome Lewis to the Post and to introduce him around Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 She invited him to events and they had dinner every few months, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got along really well,\u8221\'20\'1D Quinn recalled. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was very charming and funny and smart and we had a good time. He seemed very excited and upbeat about the job, so I was looking forward to working with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Quinn said she stopped hearing from Lewis after he faced blowback for his handling of the ouster of \uc2 Sally Buzbee\uc2  as executive editor in early June 2024. \u8220\'20\'1CHe stopped calling and emailing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think he just didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to know what I had to say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There were signs early on that Lewis would be hampered by his past. Even before assuming the job, Lewis told a Post reporter that he would not comment on allegations that he had helped cover up a major hacking scandal at Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s UK publications in the early 2010s as part of his work for News Corporation. (Lewis has not been found to have committed any wrongdoing.)\par \par \uc2 But Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s ties to that sordid period in British journalism continued to dog him, even as they were unlikely to have factored much into Bezos\u8217\'20\'19s decision to oust him.\par \par \uc2 Early in his tenure, Lewis faced accusations, which he denied, of{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/05/business/media/washington-post-buzbee-lewis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  infringing on the Post\u8217\'20\'19s coverage}}}\uc2  of a lawsuit filed by Britain\u8217\'20\'19s Prince Harry against Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s British publishing operation that could have reflected on him and his work for the company.\par \par \uc2 To get around the obvious conflict of interest, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/06/17/washington-post-new-publisher-top-editor-william-lewis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Post tapped}}}\uc2  former managing editor Cameron Barr to oversee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2024/06/16/washington-post-editor-robert-winnett/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigative coverage}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2024/06/28/william-lewis-gordon-brown-phone-hacking/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of Lewis}}}\uc2  and Robert Winnett, a former colleague he had picked to replace Buzbee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it was a credit to the Post to undertake and to provide the resources, which were extensive,\u8221\'20\'1D Barr recalled in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Barr, who stepped down from the Post in 2023, described Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s tenure as publisher as \u8220\'20\'1Cineffective\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see that any of the initiatives that he launched have been a success,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt certainly hasn\u8217\'20\'19t turned around the financial fortunes of the Post.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, Lewis would get something of a reprieve in January 2025 when Prince Harry and Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s operation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/prince-harry-settles-lawsuit-murdoch-papers-apology-rcna188695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled the case}}}\uc2 . But questions about his past persisted. Last September, the Guardian reported that Lewis had played a prominent role in the effort to save {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/boris-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boris Johnson}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s prime ministership (Johnson, a former Telegraph colleague, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressgazette.co.uk/news/william-lewis-knighted/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 knighted Lewis}}}\uc2  in 2023.)\par \par \uc2 Part of Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s supposed appeal for the job was his background as a reporter. Lewis got his start at the Financial Times in 1994, gradually rising through the ranks before becoming business editor for the Sunday Times. He reached the upper echelons of British journalism in 2005, when he became editor-in-chief of the Telegraph, receiving acclaim for overseeing coverage of a scandal revealing lawmakers who were using public funds for personal benefit.\par \par \uc2 But, during that June 2024 meeting with staffers, Lewis immediately clashed with some of the Post\u8217\'20\'19s most respected reporters.\par \par \uc2 One of those reporters, the Pulitzer prize-winning journalist Carol D Leonnig, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CarolLeonnig/status/2020892204135293214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in a post on X}}}\uc2  on Monday that Lewis \u8220\'20\'1Cshowed his horrendous leadership when, at 1st staff mtg, he snapped at my question about his vision for \u8294\'20\'66\u8294\'20\'66@washingtonpost. He had none. In 18 months, \u8294\'20\'66@JeffBezos let him wreck a national treasure.\u8221\'20\'1D Leonnig left the Post for MSNBC \u8211\'20\'13 now called MS Now \u8211\'20\'13 last summer.\par \par \uc2 Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s pick of Winnett to take over the newsroom turned out to be a disaster. Just a few weeks after his appointment, after his career was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2024/06/16/washington-post-editor-robert-winnett/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutinized by the Post}}}\uc2  in a story headlined Incoming Post editor tied to self-described \u8216\'20\'18thief\u8217\'20\'19 who claimed role in his reporting, it was announced Winnett would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/article/2024/jun/21/uk-editor-backs-out-of-top-washington-post-job-after-us-scrutiny-of-his-past-rob-winnett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stick with his job}}}\uc2  as deputy editor of the Telegraph.\par \par \uc2 As the business continued to flounder into early 2025, Post staffers found new reasons to lash out at Lewis.\par \par \uc2 Late last April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.status.news/p/ryan-lizza-politico-substack-legal-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some staffers chafed after reading}}}\uc2  that the Post had thrown an ostentatious, over-the-top brunch to commemorate the annual White House correspondents\u8217\'20\'19 dinner weekend.\par \par \uc2 In May 2025, Lewis was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.status.news/p/donald-trump-jon-voight-hollywood-tariffs?utm_campaign=a-reel-trade-war&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_source=www.status.news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspicuously absent}}}\uc2  when Post staffers gathered to celebrate their Pulitzer prize wins, which some staffers took as a sign that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t value their journalism. (Staffers were told that Lewis was away on a long-planned trip.)\par \par \uc2 All the while, Lewis rebuffed efforts by the Post\u8217\'20\'19s unionized staffers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DCaETZehDtu/?hl=en&img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to get him to participate in a town hall}}}\uc2  meeting. Last month, amid widespread anxiety at the Post about layoffs, he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XKG03Bj4wAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Davos}}}\uc2  interviewing Bill Gates.\par \par \uc2 At the end of last month, Lewis was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BenMullin/status/2017632260262854716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still participating}}}\uc2  in the pomp and circumstance of the job, reportedly attending the prestigious Alfalfa Club dinner, along with Bezos and Murray \u8211\'20\'13 once again giving no indication that he was on the outs with his boss.\par \par \uc2 Just days before Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s departure, Murray defended Lewis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/washington-posts-top-editor-backs-bezos-critics-lash-out-over-struggling-papers-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with Fox News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CLook, Will has been engaged with me very closely on this for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray said, explaining his absence by saying \u8220\'20\'1Che had a lot of things to tend to today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Back in November 2023, when Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s appointment was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2023/11/04/william-lewis-publisher-ceo-washington-post/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first announced}}}\uc2 , Bezos said Lewis \u8220\'20\'1Cembodies the tenacity, energy and vision needed for this role\u8221\'20\'1D. Lewis also had experience running a digital media startup, having launched The News Movement, a social media-focused venture, after leaving Dow Jones in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In rare public remarks on Saturday, Bezos said the Post \u8220\'20\'1Chas an essential journalistic mission and an extraordinary opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D and praised Jeff D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio, the business executive who will serve as acting publisher, along with Murray and opinions editor Adam O\u8217\'20\'19Neal. He said nothing about Lewis.\par \par \uc2 In a terse, subject-less email announcing his departure, Lewis thanked Bezos \u8220\'20\'1Cfor his support and leadership\u8221\'20\'1D throughout his time at the Post and, amid calls by some for Bezos to sell the paper, told staffers that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe institution could not have a better owner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260212em2c002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
