\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editor acknowledges \u8216\'20\'18genuine trauma\u8217\'20\'19 over mass layoffs\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeremy Barr in Washington \par \uc2 694 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2026\par 20:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Matt Murray defends paper\u8217\'20\'19s strategy as \u8216\'20\'18demoralized\u8217\'20\'19 staffers ask tough questions in contentious town hall\par \par \uc2 Top \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editor Matt Murray acknowledged \u8220\'20\'1Ca widespread sense of loss, of genuine trauma\u8221\'20\'1D in a contentious town hall meeting with staff on Wednesday after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2026/feb/11/why-jeff-bezos-gutted-washington-post-full-story-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 company laid off}}}\uc2  nearly a third of its employees a week ago \u8211\'20\'13 though he expressed confidence that the Post was now on a path to success.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no doubt that just the sheer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/05/mass-layoffs-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 depth of the cuts}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and also, with that, the reality of what we face at the Post \u8211\'20\'13 has been a very hard thing to wrap our heads around and to grapple with,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray said, according to a recording of his remarks obtained by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Murray, who joined the Post in 2024, said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking discovery\u8221\'20\'1D for management to understand the scope of the financial problems the company is facing. But he said he did not want to \u8220\'20\'1Clook backwards and litigate the past\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe company has been a mess in lots of ways for a long time, but I\u8217\'20\'19m confident stars are aligning in a positive way,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Murray said Post leadership used data on readership trends to determine which areas to cut. The publication\u8217\'20\'19s sports, international, local and style sections were particularly hard-hit. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure we got some things wrong, but if I look around the room with everybody here, I know we got a lot of things right,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While the Post achieved historic success during the first Trump administration, as reporters broke scoops and readers signed up in droves to support the publication\u8217\'20\'19s mission, Murray said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno more Trump bump\u8221\'20\'1D these days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are reading [about] Donald Trump, but they also want to escape from Donald Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Amid questions about whether the publication\u8217\'20\'19s mandate and ambition had shrunk, Murray said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe mission of the Post is unchanged\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Murray played down the number of Post customers who have cancelled their subscriptions in protest against last week\u8217\'20\'19s cuts. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been not very heavy, and it\u8217\'20\'19s been completely within predicted models and expectations, and completely baked into the plan,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Jeff D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio\uc2 , who was named acting publisher by the owner, Jeff Bezos, after \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  abruptly resigned on Saturday night, introduced himself to employees and addressed the aftermath of the layoffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the past five years, the Post has not directly addressed deeply rooted problems, turning an eye at our revenue downturn and staying our course despite shifting traffic and user habits,\u8221\'20\'1D D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a decision to change the scope and direction of our business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seeking to reassure his assembled colleagues, D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio, who joined the Post last June as chief financial officer, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI need you to know that we will get to the other side of this \u8230\'20\'26 We are on the same team. It can\u8217\'20\'19t be any other way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Murray faced tough questions from some longtime employees who expressed skepticism about the Post\u8217\'20\'19s direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve not seen this place as demoralized as it is right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said one veteran reporter, who asked why employees should continue to believe in management. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t tell you to believe in me or believe in Jeff or believe in other Jeff,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray responded, acknowledging it was an \u8220\'20\'1Cessential question\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here, we\u8217\'20\'19re talking, and I have an incredible amount of faith in the masthead team,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow are we possibly supposed to move forward when we are demonstrating to the people we are begging to give us their money every day that we can\u8217\'20\'19t even do the basics any more?\u8221\'20\'1D another reporter asked, mentioning errors in the print product since the cuts happened.\par \par \uc2 During the town hall, Murray did not say much about Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s sudden exit after only two years on the job.\par \par \uc2 But when asked about accountability for executives who have contributed to the Post\u8217\'20\'19s financial challenges, Murray noted: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a new CEO. You can draw whatever conclusions you want from that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260211em2b005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
