\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US added 130,000 jobs in January, surpassing expectations as 2025 growth is slashed\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2026\par 16:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unemployment rate was 4.3% in January with gains 13,000 less than the 143,000 jobs added a year ago, report shows\par \par \uc2 The US jobs market added 130,000 jobs in January, according to a highly anticipated labor market report released on Wednesday, a surge of job growth after months of fatigue in the labor market.\par \par \uc2 The unemployment rate was 4.3% in January, a slight cooling since the fall. Economists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.spglobal.com/marketintelligence/en/mi/research-analysis/week-ahead-economic-preview-week-of-9-february-2026.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  70,000 in job gains and an unchanged unemployment rate for January.\par \par \uc2 The gains are still 13,000 jobsless than the the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/feb/07/job-growth-unemployment#:~:text=1%20year%20old-,US%20economy%20shows%20steady%20job%20growth%20in%20January%20amid%20Biden,according%20to%20the%20latest%20revisions."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 143,000 jobs}}}\uc2  added a year ago in January 2025, but morethan double the 50,000 jobs that were added in December.\par \par \uc2 Despite January\u8217\'20\'19s boost to the labor market, the report also included revisions to the total number of new jobs in 2025. After revisions, total new jobs for the year was 181,000, down from an initially reported 584,000 jobs, marking the weakest year of job growth since the Covid-19 pandemic. In comparison, 2m jobs were added to the economy in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The report comes after a tumultuous year for the US economy, with constantly changing trade and immigration policies marring the labor market with instability.\par \par \uc2 The jobs report, originally scheduled for release on 6 February, was also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/02/us-jobs-report-delayed-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delayed }}}\uc2 by the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  due to the brief government shutdown in early February.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  celebrated the new job figures, posting on social media: \u8220\'20\'1CJust in: GREAT JOBS NUMBERS, FAR GREATER THAN EXPECTED!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWOW! The Golden Age of America is upon us!!!\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 In advance of the report, private payroll grew by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/private-payroll-growth-in-january-misses-expectations-as-market-awaits-official-jobs-data-133441723.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly9maW5hbmNlLnlhaG9vLmNvbS9uZXdzL3RoZS1qb2ItbWFya2V0LXdhcy1icnVpc2luZy1pbi0yMDI1LXRoZS1zdGFydC1vZi0yMDI2LWRvZXNudC1sb29rLW11Y2gtYmV0dGVyLTE1MDA1NzAwOS5odG1sP2d1Y2NvdW50ZXI9MQ&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAKD1l_l8cd1li3igbIJs5nlWXRIjujBJ8B4ZQddw5sFMXPu0PhOE3SGeBYZjEB1Pt6frMjCpkivK4c4tUH16qGQsj9hISFUD6hW2rTIZHegmLGceYdyfiX2O4SJwgJcn6YCLEHxB86t0tHQhRZZPzEYoYluPZnA-4hkqgpt_VjMi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 22,000 jobs}}}\uc2  in January, below economists\u8217\'20\'19 expectations of 45,000 jobs. Last year, private payrolls gained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/the-job-market-was-bruising-in-2025-the-start-of-2026-doesnt-look-much-better-150057009.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAACjChSZLARhSiHDKdJjzSEYc7Tb1pibRKvZ4jANxaEfG6GqBrjqhWtafpp-qySX__4Vxyo_pfmy8DojWXGuOnwzskam9vmi2t4U47G5vnss0Gr3xAghPX8EQrTxYTB8Diir_28YBR00sE88fM24A4t0VUmvNmfCkh06DdWQixG7h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 140,000 jobs}}}\uc2  during the same period.\par \par \uc2 US employers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/02/05/layoff-and-hiring-announcements-hit-their-worst-january-levels-since-2009-challenger-says.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  108,435 layoffs in January 2026, according tooutplacement firm \uc2 Challenger, Gray & Christmas\uc2 , up 118% from January 2025 and the highest to start a year since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Job openings in the US dropped in December 2025 by 386,000 jobs to 6.542m, the lowest level since September 2020, according to the Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey (Jolts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/05/us-job-openings-five-year-low-december-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  released last week.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the White House adviser \uc2 Peter Navarro{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/business/5731440-peter-navarro-jobs-report-warning/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  against high expectations for the monthly jobs number, claiming that new jobs would be in the 50,000 range.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to revise our expectations down significantly for what a monthly job number should look like,\u8221\'20\'1D Navarro told Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Job figures during the Biden administration were actually inflated because \u8220\'20\'1Cwe were letting in 2 million illegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D, but \u8220\'20\'1Call of the jobs that we were creating in Biden years were going to illegals\u8221\'20\'1D, he said\par \par \uc2 The weakening labor market has not been slow enough to inspire the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  to slash interest rates as US inflation also remains unstable.\par \par \uc2 Last month, economists at the bank {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jan/28/federal-reserve-holds-rates-powell-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the unemployment rate leveling at 4.4% was a possible sign of stability in the labor market, though job gains have been low. Slowed job growth comes from new immigration policies and labor force participation, Powell added, as well as tempered demand for labor.\par \par \uc2 The central bank is also being cautious about increasing prices. US inflation was 2.7% in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jan/13/us-inflation-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December}}}\uc2 , and Powell said the effects of tariffs are still flowing through prices.\par \par \uc2 Higher prices have continued to affect consumer sentiment: according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s survey of consumers}}}\uc2 , sentiment was 57.3 in February, a lift up from over the past six months but more than 11% lower than the same period in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260211em2b002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
