\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US union elections declined in 2025 after Trump hobbled labor board\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 461 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2026\par 13:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Both the number of workers participating in union elections and the success of elections dropped off\par \par \uc2 The number of union elections overseen by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) dropped 30% in 2025 after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  left the federal labor watchdog powerless, according to an analysis released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The number of workers participating in union elections dropped by 59,000, a 42% decline compared with the year prior, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/nlrb-overseen-union-elections-fell-in-2025-amid-trump-administration-attacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 . The total number of union elections fell from a 10-year high of 2,124 in 2024 to 1,498 in 2025.\par \par \uc2 The success rate in union elections also dropped to 69.8% in 2025, after rising to 72% in 2023.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  presides over enforcing labor law in the private sector, including conducting union elections and enforcing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/guidance/key-reference-materials/national-labor-relations-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Labor Relations Act}}}\uc2 . Workers file to hold an election with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  once they have agreed to form a union but their employer doesn\u8217\'20\'19t voluntarily recognize it.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of his second term, Trump has made unprecedented moves to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/14/labor-movement-union-trump-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freeze}}}\uc2  the board.\par \par \uc2 Days after taking office, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/14/labor-movement-union-trump-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired }}}\uc2 NLRB\uc2  board member Gwynne Wilcox, leaving the board without a quorum needed to make decisions. When Trump eventually restored a quorum, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/nominating-scott-mayer-as-a-member-of-the-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed}}}\uc2  two Republicans to fill the vacant seats, creating a conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Though the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  was created to protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and rule on disputes, the political makeup of the board dictates how friendly it will be to either organizers or their employers.\par \par \uc2 The agency also lost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://data.opm.gov/explore-data/analytics/workforce-size-and-composition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 100 employees}}}\uc2  due to early retirements and resignation buyouts pushed by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unofficial \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, leaving roughly 1,100 workers to oversee collective bargaining and labor practices in the private sector. In comparison, 1,545 employees worked at the agency in 2016.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  workforce declined during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, though the private sector workforce grew from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/graph/?g=674i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 120 million}}}\uc2  in 2016 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://datatools.ahrq.gov/meps-ic/?tab=private-sector-national&dash=19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 135 million}}}\uc2  in 2024. The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  did not return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The decline in union activity comes despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/everybody-likes-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong public support}}}\uc2  for unions across age, educational and partisan lines. Public approval for labor unions climbed from 56% in 2016 to 68% in 2025, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/694472/labor-union-approval-relatively-steady.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Though the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has been \u8220\'20\'1Crelentlessly attacked\u8221\'20\'1D under the Trump administration, \u8220\'20\'1Cworkers still want unions\u8221\'20\'1D, said Aurelia Glass, author of the report and a policy analyst for the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s American Worker Project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s still a lot of interest and a lot of momentum behind these campaigns, so I think workers are going to continue to try to find ways to move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260211em2b002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
