\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  publisher \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  abruptly resigns amid criticism of staff cuts\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeremy Barr \par \uc2 868 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2026\par 18:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Departure comes days after newspaper laid off nearly one-third of staff, including more than 300 journalists\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/willlewis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Lewis}}}\uc2 , the Murdoch media veteran who took over as publisher and chief executive of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  in early 2024, announced abruptly on Saturday evening that he is leaving the company.\par \par \uc2 His departure comes just three days after the Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/04/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off nearly one-third}}}\uc2  of its entire staff, citing the need to cut costs and reposition the money-losing publication. Lewis, who did not appear on the all-staff meeting during which the cuts were announced, has faced criticism for his absence and leadership.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll \u8211\'20\'13 after two years of transformation at \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 , now is the right time for me to step aside,\u8221\'20\'1D Lewis wrote in an untitled email to Post staffers obtained by the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to thank Jeff Bezos for his support and leadership throughout my tenure as CEO and Publisher. The institution could not have a better owner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lewis then addressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/05/mass-layoffs-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of the criticism}}}\uc2  that the Post has received in recent days, including from many current employees. At least 300 journalists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/04/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were cut}}}\uc2  from the Post\u8217\'20\'19s newsroom in one of the largest round of layoffs in American media history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring my tenure, difficult decisions have been taken in order to ensure the sustainable future of The Post so it can for many years ahead publish high-quality nonpartisan news to millions of customers each day,\u8221\'20\'1D Lewis wrote, signing off: \u8220\'20\'1CWith gratitude, Will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeff D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio\uc2 , who joined the Post in June as chief financial officer, will serve as acting publisher and chief executive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a challenging time across all media organizations, and The Post is unfortunately no exception,\u8221\'20\'1D D\u8217\'20\'19Onofrio wrote in a memo to staffers. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had the privilege of helping chart the course of disrupters and cultural stalwarts alike. All faced economic headwinds in changing industry landscapes, and we rose to meet those moments. I have no doubt we will do just that, together.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m honored to take the helm as acting Publisher and CEO to lead us into a sustainable, successful future with the strength of our journalism as our north star,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to working shoulder to shoulder with all of you to make that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bezos, who has owned the Post since 2013, and who has received heavy criticism in recent days for his stewardship of the publication, released a statement touting the Post and its new leadership team \u8211\'20\'13 without addressing Lewis\u8217\'20\'19s tenure overseeing the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Post has an essential journalistic mission and an extraordinary opportunity. Each and every day our readers give us a roadmap to success. The data tells us what is valuable and where to focus,\u8221\'20\'1D Bezos said. \u8220\'20\'1CJeff, along with [executive editor Matt Murray] and [opinion editor Adam O\u8217\'20\'19Neal], are positioned to lead The Post into an exciting and thriving next chapter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During an interview last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/washington-posts-top-editor-backs-bezos-critics-lash-out-over-struggling-papers-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Murray defended Lewis}}}\uc2  when asked about his absence. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, Will has been engaged with me very closely on this for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray told Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd there were a lot of things that the company did and Will was engaged with all across the company, and I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t. He had a lot of things to tend to today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lewis also faced criticism when a former Post sports reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NickiJhabvala/status/2019568890473508935"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a photo of him}}}\uc2  at the festivities for Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s Super Bowl, even after the Post largely destroyed its sports section, laying off writers who cover football.\par \par \uc2 Lewis, 56, joined the Post after a lengthy career working for \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s media properties. Most recently, Lewis had spent six years as chief executive officer and publisher of the Wall Street Journal, departing in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Lewis began his career as a journalist at the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 . After working as business editor at the \uc2 Sunday Times\uc2  and editor in chief of the Telegraph from 2005 to 2010, Lewis was appointed group general manager at what was then called \uc2 News International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He played a key role in handling the aftermath of the hacking scandal that enveloped Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s UK media properties as part of the company-created management and standards committee that handled the company\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with police investigating the allegations. Lewis said upon joining the Post that he did not plan to discuss his role in the aftermath of the hacking scandal any further.\par \par \uc2 His departure was celebrated by some current and former Post journalists who spoke with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill can put on British charm and knows how to manage up but eventually results matter,\u8221\'20\'1D said Glenn Kessler, a former Post journalist who has been critical of the paper\u8217\'20\'19s leadership. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery initiative he launched failed and he never found a way to boost readers for the Post.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Will Lewis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exit is long overdue. His legacy will be the attempted destruction of a great American journalism institution,\u8221\'20\'1D said the union representing most Post employees. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s not too late to save The Post. Jeff Bezos must immediately rescind these layoffs or sell the paper to someone willing to invest in its future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260207em27004bl\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvert